\c 2
\s1 Elijah Taken Up to Heaven
\p \v 1 \rb Shortly before|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|בְּהַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb up to heaven|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb in a whirlwind,|בַּֽסְעָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb and Elisha|וֶאֱלִישָׁ֖ע\rb* \rb were on their way|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Gilgal,|הַגִּלְגָּֽל׃\rb* \v 2 \rb and Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֜ע\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb stay|שֵֽׁב־\rb* \rb here,|פֹ֗ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb on to|עַד־\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel.”|אֵ֔ל\rb*
\p \rb But Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb* \rb and as you yourself|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb live,|וְחֵֽי־\rb* \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb leave you.”|אֶעֶזְבֶ֑ךָּ\rb*
\p \rb So they went down|וַיֵּרְד֖וּ\rb* \rb to|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel.|אֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel|אֵל֮\rb* \rb came out|וַיֵּצְא֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁע֒\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “Do you know|הֲיָדַ֕עְתָּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will take|לֹקֵ֥חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your master|אֲדֹנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb away from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb you|רֹאשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb today?”|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*
\p \rb “Yes,|גַּם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb know,”|יָדַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “Do not speak of it.”|הֶחֱשֽׁוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb said to|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֣ע׀\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb stay|שֵֽׁב־\rb* \rb here,|פֹ֗ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb on to Jericho.”|יְרִיח֔וֹ\rb*
\p \rb But Elisha replied,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb* \rb and as you yourself|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb live,|וְחֵֽי־\rb* \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb leave you.”|אֶעֶזְבֶ֑ךָּ\rb*
\p \rb So they went|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Jericho.|יְרִיחֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at Jericho|בִּֽירִיחוֹ֮\rb* \rb came up|וַיִּגְּשׁ֨וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁע֒\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb “Do you know|הֲיָדַ֕עְתָּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb will take|לֹקֵ֥חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your master|אֲדֹנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb away from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb you|רֹאשֶׁ֑ךָ\rb* \rb today?”|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*
\p \rb “Yes,|גַּם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb know,”|יָדַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “Do not speak of it.”|הֶחֱשֽׁוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb And Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb to Elisha,|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb stay|שֵֽׁב־\rb* \rb here,|פֹ֗ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb on to the Jordan.”|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔נָה\rb*
\p \rb But Elisha replied,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb* \rb and as you|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb yourself live,|וְחֵֽי־\rb* \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb leave you.”|אֶעֶזְבֶ֑ךָּ\rb*
\p \rb So the two of them|שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb went on.|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Then a company|אִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb of fifty|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֨ים\rb* \rb of the sons|מִבְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִים֙\rb* \rb went|הָֽלְכ֔וּ\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּעַמְד֥וּ\rb* \rb at a distance,|מֵרָח֑וֹק\rb* \rb facing Elijah and Elisha|מִנֶּ֖גֶד\rb* \rb as the two|וּשְׁנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of them stood|עָמְד֥וּ\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Jordan.|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb* \v 8 \rb And Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֨הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb* \rb his cloak,|אַדַּרְתּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb rolled it up,|וַיִּגְלֹם֙\rb* \rb and struck|וַיַּכֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the waters,|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb which parted|וַיֵּחָצ֖וּ\rb* \rb to the right|הֵ֣נָּה\rb* \rb and to the left,|וָהֵ֑נָּה\rb* \rb so that the two|שְׁנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of them crossed over|וַיַּעַבְר֥וּ\rb* \rb on dry ground.|בֶּחָרָבָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb After|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb they had crossed over,|כְעָבְרָ֗ם\rb* \rb Elijah|וְאֵ֨לִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁע֙\rb* \rb “Tell me,|שְׁאַל֙\rb* \rb what|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb can I do|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb for you|לָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb before|בְּטֶ֖רֶם\rb* \rb I am taken away|אֶלָּקַ֣ח\rb* \rb from you?”|מֵעִמָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \rb “Please,|נָ֛א\rb* \rb let me|וִֽיהִי־\rb* \rb inherit|אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \rb a double|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb portion|פִּֽי־\rb* \rb of your spirit,”|בְּרוּחֲךָ֖\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb “You have requested|לִשְׁא֑וֹל\rb* \rb a difficult thing,”|הִקְשִׁ֣יתָ\rb* \rb said Elijah.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Nevertheless, if|אִם־\rb* \rb you see|תִּרְאֶ֨ה\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb as I am taken|לֻקָּ֤ח\rb* \rb from you,|מֵֽאִתָּךְ֙\rb* \rb it will be|יְהִֽי־\rb* \rb yours.|לְךָ֣\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb* \rb But if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb not,|אַ֖יִן\rb* \rb then it will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be so.”|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb As they|הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb were walking along|הֹלְכִ֤ים\rb*\rb |הָלוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb and talking together,|וְדַבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a chariot|רֶֽכֶב־\rb* \rb of fire|אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb with horses|וְס֣וּסֵי\rb* \rb of fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb appeared and separated|וַיַּפְרִ֖דוּ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the two of them,|שְׁנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and Elijah|אֵ֣לִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb into heaven|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb in a whirlwind.|בַּֽסְעָרָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb As Elisha|וֶאֱלִישָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb watched,|רֹאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb he|וְה֤וּא\rb* \rb cried out,|מְצַעֵק֙\rb* \rb “My father,|אָבִ֣י׀\rb* \rb my father,|אָבִ֗י\rb* \rb the chariots|רֶ֤כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּפָ֣רָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb of Israel!”|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb And he saw Elijah|רָאָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb more.|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb So taking hold|וַֽיַּחֲזֵק֙\rb* \rb of his own clothes,|בִּבְגָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb he tore them|וַיִּקְרָעֵ֖ם\rb* \rb in two.|לִשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |קְרָעִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Elisha also picked up|וַיָּ֙רֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cloak|אַדֶּ֣רֶת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had fallen|נָפְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מֵעָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb Elijah,|אֵלִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and he went back|וַיָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bank|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the Jordan.|הַיַּרְדֵּֽן׃\rb* \v 14 \rb Then he took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cloak|אַדֶּ֨רֶת\rb* \rb of Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had fallen|נָפְלָ֤ה\rb* \rb from him|מֵֽעָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and struck|וַיַּכֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the waters.|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb “Where now is|אַיֵּ֕ה\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Elijah?”|אֵלִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |אַף־\rb* \rb he asked.|וַיֹּאמַ֕ר\rb*
\p \rb And when he had struck|וַיַּכֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the waters,|הַמַּ֗יִם\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb they parted|וַיֵּֽחָצוּ֙\rb* \rb to the right|הֵ֣נָּה\rb* \rb and to the left,|וָהֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb and Elisha|אֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb* \rb crossed over.|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֖ר\rb*
\s1 Elisha Succeeds Elijah
\p \v 15 \rb When the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֤ים\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb watching him|מִנֶּ֔גֶד\rb* \rb from Jericho|בִּֽירִיחוֹ֙\rb* \rb saw what had happened,|וַיִּרְאֻ֨הוּ\rb* \rb they said,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “The spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb rests|נָ֛חָה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Elisha.”|אֱלִישָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb And they went|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and bowed down|וַיִּשְׁתַּחֲווּ־\rb* \rb to the ground|אָֽרְצָה׃\rb* \rb before him.|ל֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb “Look|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb now,”|נָ֣א\rb* \rb they said|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to Elisha,|אֵלָ֡יו\rb* \rb “we your servants|עֲבָדֶיךָ֩\rb* \rb have|יֵֽשׁ־\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֨ים\rb* \rb valiant|חַ֗יִל\rb* \rb men.|אֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Please|נָא֮\rb* \rb let them go|יֵ֣לְכוּ\rb* \rb and search for|וִיבַקְשׁ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your master.|אֲדֹנֶיךָ֒\rb* \rb Perhaps|פֶּן־\rb* \rb the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb has taken him up|נְשָׂאוֹ֙\rb* \rb and put him|וַיַּשְׁלִכֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb on one|בְּאַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the mountains|הֶהָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb* \rb in one|בְּאַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the valleys.”|הַגְּיָאוֹת\rb*
\p \rb “Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb send them,”|תִשְׁלָֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb Elisha replied.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb But when they pressed|וַיִּפְצְרוּ־\rb* \rb him|ב֥וֹ\rb* \rb to the point of|עַד־\rb* \rb embarrassment,|בֹּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Send them.”|שְׁלָ֑חוּ\rb*
\p \rb And they sent|וַֽיִּשְׁלְחוּ֙\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb men,|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who searched for|וַיְבַקְשׁ֥וּ\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹשָֽׁה־\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb but did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb find Elijah.|מְצָאֻֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb When they returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֣בוּ\rb* \rb to Elisha,|אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb who|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb was staying|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in Jericho,|בִּירִיח֑וֹ\rb* \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Didn’t|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb I tell|אָמַ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb you|אֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb to go?”|תֵּלֵֽכוּ׃\rb*
\s1 Elisha Heals the Waters of Jericho
\p \v 19 \rb Then the men|אַנְשֵׁ֤י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֞א\rb* \rb note,|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb our lord,|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb that the city’s|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb location|מוֹשַׁ֤ב\rb* \rb is good,|ט֔וֹב\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you can see.|רֹאֶ֑ה\rb* \rb But the water|וְהַמַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb is bad|רָעִ֖ים\rb* \rb and the land|וְהָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb is unfruitful.”|מְשַׁכָּֽלֶת׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb “Bring|קְחוּ־\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb* \rb a new|חֲדָשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb bowl,”|צְלֹחִ֣ית\rb* \rb he replied,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “and put|וְשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb some salt|מֶ֑לַח\rb* \rb in it.”|שָׁ֖ם\rb*
\p \rb So they brought it|וַיִּקְח֖וּ\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 21 \rb and Elisha went out|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the spring,|מוֹצָ֣א\rb*\rb |הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb cast|וַיַּשְׁלֶךְ־\rb* \rb the salt|מֶ֑לַח\rb* \rb into it,|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘I have healed|רִפִּ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb this|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb water.|לַמַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb will it cause|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֛ם\rb* \rb death|מָ֥וֶת\rb* \rb or unfruitfulness.|וּמְשַׁכָּֽלֶת׃\rb*\f + \fr 2:21 \ft Or \fqa barrenness\f*’”
\p \v 22 \rb And the waters there|הַמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb have been healthy|וַיֵּרָפ֣וּ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day,|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb spoken|דִּבֵּֽר׃פ\rb* \rb by Elisha.|אֱלִישָׁ֖ע\rb*
\s1 Elisha Mocked
\p \v 23 \rb From there,|מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb Elisha went up|וַיַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb to|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb Bethel,|אֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and as he|וְה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb was walking up|עֹלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the road,|בַדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb a group of boys|וּנְעָרִ֤ים\rb*\f + \fr 2:23 \ft Or \fqa some small youths \ft or \fqa some insignificant young men\ft ; similarly in verse 24\f* \rb |קְטַנִּים֙\rb*\rb came out|יָצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and jeered at|וַיִּתְקַלְּסוּ־\rb* \rb him,|בוֹ֙\rb* \rb chanting,|וַיֹּ֣אמְרוּ\rb* \rb “Go up,|עֲלֵ֥ה\rb* \rb you baldhead!|קֵרֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb Go up,|עֲלֵ֥ה\rb* \rb you baldhead!”|קֵרֵֽחַ׃\rb*
