\c 3
\s1 Moab’s Rebellion
\p \v 1 \rb In the eighteenth|שְׁמֹנֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat’s|לִיהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Jehoram|וִיהוֹרָ֣ם\rb*\f + \fr 3:1 \fqa Jehoram \ft is a variant spelling of \fqa Joram\ft ; also in verse 6.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֗ב\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and he reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb twelve|שְׁתֵּים־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּעֲשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֙\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb but|רַ֕ק\rb* \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb as his father|כְאָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb and mother had done.|וּכְאִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb He removed|וַיָּ֙סַר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacred pillar|מַצְּבַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb had made.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Nevertheless,|רַ֠ק\rb* \rb he clung|דָּבֵ֑ק\rb* \rb to the sins|בְּחַטֹּ֞אות\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֛ט\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to commit;|הֶחֱטִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֖ר\rb* \rb from them.|מִמֶּֽנָּה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Now Mesha|וּמֵישַׁ֥ע\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb a sheep breeder,|נֹקֵ֑ד\rb*\f + \fr 3:4 \ft Or \fqa sheepherder\f* \rb and he would render|וְהֵשִׁ֤יב\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵאָה־\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֣לֶף\rb* \rb lambs|כָּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and the wool|צָֽמֶר׃\rb* \rb of a hundred|וּמֵ֥אָה\rb* \rb thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb rams.|אֵילִ֥ים\rb* \v 5 \rb But after|וַיְהִ֖י\rb* \rb the death|כְּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Ahab,|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb* \rb rebelled|וַיִּפְשַׁ֥ע\rb* \rb against the king|בְּמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 6 \rb So at that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb time|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֛ם\rb* \rb set out|וַיֵּצֵ֞א\rb* \rb from Samaria|מִשֹּׁמְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb and mobilized|וַיִּפְקֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 7 \rb |וַיֵּ֡לֶךְ\rb* \rb And he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb a message to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֨ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb “The king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb has rebelled|פָּשַׁ֣ע\rb* \rb against me.|בִּ֔י\rb* \rb Will you go|הֲתֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֛י\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Moab?”|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb*
\p \rb “I will go,”|אֶעֱלֶ֔ה\rb* \rb replied Jehoshaphat.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I am|כָּמ֧וֹנִי\rb* \rb as you are,|כָמ֛וֹךָ\rb* \rb my people are|כְּעַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb your people,|כְעַמֶּ֖ךָ\rb* \rb and my horses are|כְּסוּסַ֥י\rb* \rb your horses.”|כְּסוּסֶֽיךָ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb Then he asked,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Which|אֵי־\rb* \rb way|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb shall we go up?”|נַעֲלֶ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb “By way|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Desert|מִדְבַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of Edom,”|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb replied Joram.|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So the king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb the king|וּמֶֽלֶך־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb set out,|וַיֵּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb and after they had traveled a roundabout|וַיָּסֹ֕בּוּ\rb* \rb route|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb for seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days,|יָמִ֑ים\rb* \rb they had no|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb water|מַ֧יִם\rb* \rb for their army|לַֽמַּחֲנֶ֛ה\rb* \rb or for their|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |בְּרַגְלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb animals.|וְלַבְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb “Alas,”|אֲהָ֕הּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb “for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb has summoned|קָרָ֣א\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb three|לִשְׁלֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb to deliver|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Moab!”|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb But Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֗ט\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Is there no|הַאֵ֨ין\rb* \rb prophet|נָבִיא֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb here?|פֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb Let us inquire|וְנִדְרְשָׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb through him.”|מֵאוֹת֑וֹ\rb*
\p \rb And one|אֶחָ֞ד\rb* \rb of the servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb answered,|וַ֠יַּעַן\rb* \rb “Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphat|שָׁפָ֔ט\rb* \rb is here.|פֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb He|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb used to pour|יָ֥צַק\rb* \rb water|מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|יְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Elijah.|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*\f + \fr 3:11 \ft Or \fqa He was Elijah’s personal assistant\f*”
\p \v 12 \rb Jehoshaphat|יְה֣וֹשָׁפָ֔ט\rb* \rb affirmed,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “The word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb with him.”|אוֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb So the king|מֶ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and Jehoshaphat|וִיהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb and the king|וּמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱדֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb went down|וַיֵּרְד֣וּ\rb* \rb to him.|אֵלָ֗יו\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Elisha, however,|אֱלִישָׁ֜ע\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb “What have we to do|מַה־\rb*\rb |לִּ֣י\rb* \rb with each other?|וָלָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Go|לֵ֚ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |נְבִיאֵ֖י\rb* \rb of your mother!”|אִמֶּ֑ךָ\rb*
\p \rb “No,”|אַ֗ל\rb* \rb replied|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb “for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it is the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb who has summoned|קָרָ֤א\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb three|לִשְׁלֹ֙שֶׁת֙\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֣ים\rb* \rb to deliver|לָתֵ֥ת\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Moab.”|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֗ע\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hosts|צְבָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb before|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I stand,|עָמַ֣דְתִּי\rb*\rb |כִּ֗י\rb* \rb were it not|לוּלֵ֛י\rb*\rb |אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb for my regard|נֹשֵׂ֑א\rb* \rb for the presence|פְּנֵ֛י\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb I would not|אִם־\rb* \rb look|אַבִּ֥יט\rb* \rb at you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb acknowledge you.|אֶרְאֶֽךָּ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb But now,|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb bring|קְחוּ־\rb* \rb me|לִ֣י\rb* \rb a harpist.|מְנַגֵּ֑ן\rb*\f + \fr 3:15 \ft Or \fqa a musician\ft ; twice in this verse\f*”
\p \rb And while|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb the harpist|הַֽמְנַגֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb played,|כְּנַגֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb came|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb upon Elisha|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \v 16 \rb and he said,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Dig|עָשֹׂ֛ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb valley|הַנַּ֥חַל\rb*\rb |גֵּבִ֥ים׀\rb* \rb full of ditches.’|גֵּבִֽים׃\rb* \v 17 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |כֹ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says,|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘You will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see|תִרְא֥וּ\rb* \rb wind|ר֙וּחַ֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |תִרְא֣וּ\rb* \rb or rain,|גֶ֔שֶׁם\rb* \rb but the|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb valley|וְהַנַּ֥חַל\rb* \rb will be filled|יִמָּ֣לֵא\rb* \rb with water,|מָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and you will drink—|וּשְׁתִיתֶ֛ם\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb and your cattle|וּמִקְנֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and your animals.’|וּֽבְהֶמְתְּכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb This|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb is a simple matter|וְנָקַ֥ל\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and He will also deliver|וְנָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb the Moabites|מוֹאָ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into your hand.|בְּיֶדְכֶֽם׃\rb* \v 19 \rb And you shall attack|וְהִכִּיתֶ֞ם\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb fortified|מִבְצָר֙\rb* \rb city|עִ֤יר\rb* \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of importance.|מִבְח֔וֹר\rb* \rb You shall cut down|תַּפִּ֔ילוּ\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb good|טוֹב֙\rb* \rb tree,|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb stop up|תִּסְתֹּ֑מוּ\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb spring,|מַעְיְנֵי־\rb*\rb |מַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and ruin|תַּכְאִ֖בוּ\rb* \rb every|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb good|הַטּוֹבָ֔ה\rb* \rb field|הַחֶלְקָ֣ה\rb* \rb with stones.”|בָּאֲבָנִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb The next morning,|בַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb at the time of the morning sacrifice,|כַּעֲל֣וֹת\rb*\rb |הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb water|מַ֥יִם\rb* \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb flowed|בָּאִ֖ים\rb* \rb from the direction|מִדֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֑וֹם\rb* \rb and filled|וַתִּמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb the land.|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Now all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Moabites|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb had heard|שָֽׁמְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the kings|הַמְּלָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb had come up|עָל֥וּ\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּ֣חֶם\rb* \rb against them.|בָּ֑ם\rb* \rb So all|מִכֹּ֨ל\rb* \rb who could bear arms,|חֹגֵ֤ר\rb*\rb |חֲגֹרָה֙\rb* \rb young and old,|וָמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb were summoned|וַיִּצָּעֲק֗וּ\rb* \rb and stationed|וַיַּעַמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb at|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the border.|הַגְּבֽוּל׃\rb* \v 22 \rb When they got up early|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb in the morning,|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb the sun|וְהַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb* \rb was shining|זָרְחָ֣ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the water,|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb and it|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb looked|וַיִּרְא֨וּ\rb* \rb as red|אֲדֻמִּ֥ים\rb* \rb as blood|כַּדָּֽם׃\rb* \rb to the Moabites|מוֹאָ֥ב\rb* \rb across the way.|מִנֶּ֛גֶד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb “This|זֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |הָחֳרֵ֤ב\rb* \rb is blood!”|דָּ֣ם\rb* \rb they exclaimed.|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb “The kings|הַמְּלָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb have clashed swords|נֶֽחֶרְבוּ֙\rb* \rb and slaughtered|וַיַּכּ֖וּ\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb another.|רֵעֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb to the plunder,|לַשָּׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb Moab!”|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb But when the Moabites came|וַיָּבֹאוּ֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb rose up|וַיָּקֻ֤מוּ\rb* \rb and attacked|וַיַּכּ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb them,|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and they fled|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb* \rb before them.|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb So the Israelites invaded their land|וַיָּבוֹ\rb* \rb and struck down|וְהַכּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Moabites.|מוֹאָֽב׃\rb* \v 25 \rb They destroyed|יַהֲרֹ֡סוּ\rb* \rb the cities,|וְהֶעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and each man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb threw|יַשְׁלִ֨יכוּ\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנ֜וֹ\rb* \rb on every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb good|ט֠וֹבָה\rb* \rb field|חֶלְקָ֣ה\rb* \rb until it was covered.|וּמִלְא֗וּהָ\rb* \rb They stopped up|יִסְתֹּ֙מוּ֙\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb spring|מַעְיַן־\rb*\rb |מַ֤יִם\rb* \rb and cut down|יַפִּ֔ילוּ\rb* \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb good|ט֣וֹב\rb* \rb tree.|עֵֽץ־\rb* \rb Only|עַד־\rb*\rb |בַּקִּ֖יר\rb* \rb Kir-haraseth|חֲרָ֑שֶׂת\rb* \rb was left|הִשְׁאִ֧יר\rb* \rb with stones in place,|אֲבָנֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb but men with slings|הַקַּלָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb surrounded it|וַיָּסֹ֥בּוּ\rb* \rb and attacked it as well.|וַיַּכּֽוּהָ׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb When the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָ֔ב\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּרְא֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the battle|הַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb was too fierce|חָזַ֥ק\rb* \rb for him,|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb he took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb with him|א֠וֹתוֹ\rb* \rb seven|שְׁבַע־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֨וֹת\rb* \rb swordsmen|אִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |שֹׁ֣לֵֽף\rb*\rb |חֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb to break through|לְהַבְקִ֛יעַ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Edom,|אֱד֖וֹם\rb* \rb but they could not prevail.|יָכֹֽלוּ׃\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb* \v 27 \rb So he took|וַיִּקַּח֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his firstborn|הַבְּכ֜וֹר\rb* \rb son,|בְּנ֨וֹ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb was to succeed him,|יִמְלֹ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |תַּחְתָּ֗יו\rb* \rb and offered him|וַיַּעֲלֵ֤הוּ\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָה֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the city wall.|הַ֣חֹמָ֔ה\rb*
\p \rb And there was|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb great|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb fury|קֶצֶף־\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*\f + \fr 3:27 \ft Or \fqa And Israel’s fury was great\f* \rb so they withdrew|וַיִּסְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |מֵֽעָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ\rb* \rb to their own land.|לָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*
\c 4
\s1 The Widow’s Oil
\p \v 1 \rb Now the wife|מִנְּשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |וְאִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb of one|אַחַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַ֠נְּבִיאִים\rb* \rb cried out|צָעֲקָ֨ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֜ע\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “Your servant,|עַבְדְּךָ֤\rb* \rb my husband,|אִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb is dead,|מֵ֔ת\rb* \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb know|יָדַ֔עְתָּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb feared|יָרֵ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb And now his creditor|וְהַ֨נֹּשֶׁ֔ה\rb* \rb is coming|בָּ֗א\rb* \rb to take|לָקַ֜חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my two|שְׁנֵ֧י\rb* \rb children|יְלָדַ֛י\rb* \rb as his|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb slaves!”|לַעֲבָדִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb “How|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb can I|אֶֽעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb help you?”|לָּ֔ךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb Elisha.|אֱלִישָׁע֙\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֤יהָ\rb* \rb “Tell|הַגִּ֣ידִי\rb* \rb me,|לִ֔י\rb* \rb what|מַה־\rb* \rb do you have|יֶּשׁ־\rb*\rb |לְכִי\rb* \rb in the house?”|בַּבָּ֑יִת\rb*
\p \rb She answered,|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Your servant|לְשִׁפְחָתְךָ֥\rb* \rb has nothing|אֵ֣ין\rb*\rb |כֹל֙\rb* \rb in the house|בַּבַּ֔יִת\rb*\rb |כִּ֖י\rb* \rb but|אִם־\rb* \rb a jar|אָס֥וּךְ\rb* \rb of oil.”|שָֽׁמֶן׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb “Go,”|לְכִ֨י\rb* \rb said Elisha,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “borrow|שַׁאֲלִי־\rb*\rb |לָ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |כֵּלִים֙\rb* \rb empty|רֵקִ֖ים\rb* \rb jars|כֵּלִ֥ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb*\rb |הַח֔וּץ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your neighbors.|שִׁכְנָכֵי\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb gather just a few.|תַּמְעִֽיטִי׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Then go inside,|וּבָ֗את\rb* \rb shut|וְסָגַ֤רְתְּ\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb behind you|בַּעֲדֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and|וּבְעַד־\rb* \rb your sons,|בָּנַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb and pour|וְיָצַ֕קְתְּ\rb* \rb oil into|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb jars,|הַכֵּלִ֖ים\rb* \rb setting the full ones|וְהַמָּלֵ֖א\rb* \rb aside.”|תַּסִּֽיעִי׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So she left|וַתֵּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb him,|מֵֽאִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and after she had shut|וַתִּסְגֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֔לֶת\rb* \rb behind her|בַּעֲדָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and|וּבְעַ֣ד\rb* \rb her sons,|בָּנֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb they|הֵ֛ם\rb* \rb kept bringing jars|מַגִּשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb to her,|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb and she|וְהִ֥יא\rb* \rb kept pouring.|מֵיצָקֶת׃\rb* \v 6 \rb When|וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb all the jars|הַכֵּלִ֗ים\rb* \rb were full,|כִּמְלֹ֣את\rb* \rb she said|וַתֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her son,|בְּנָהּ֙\rb* \rb “Bring me|הַגִּ֨ישָׁה\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֥י\rb* \rb another.”|עוֹד֙\rb*\rb |כֶּ֔לִי\rb*
\p \rb But he replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb “There are no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb more|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb jars.”|כֶּ֑לִי\rb* \rb Then the oil|הַשָּֽׁמֶן׃\rb* \rb stopped flowing.|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb She went|וַתָּבֹ֗א\rb* \rb and told|וַתַּגֵּד֙\rb* \rb the man|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb and he said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Go,|לְכִי֙\rb* \rb sell|מִכְרִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the oil,|הַשֶּׁ֔מֶן\rb* \rb and pay|וְשַׁלְּמִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your debt.|נִשְׁיֵכִי\rb* \rb Then you|וְאַ֣תְּ\rb* \rb and your sons|בְּנֵיכִי\rb* \rb can live|תִֽחְיִ֖י\rb* \rb on the remainder.”|בַּנּוֹתָֽר׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Shunammite Woman
\r \ref Matthew 10:40–42|MAT 10:40-42\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb |וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb One day|הַיּ֜וֹם\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb went|וַיַּעֲבֹ֧ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shunem,|שׁוּנֵ֗ם\rb* \rb and a prominent|גְדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb woman|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb who lived there|וְשָׁם֙\rb* \rb persuaded|וַתַּחֲזֶק־\rb* \rb him|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to have a meal.|לֶאֱכָל־\rb*\rb |לָ֑חֶם\rb* \rb So whenever|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb*\rb |מִדֵּ֣י\rb* \rb he would pass by,|עָבְר֔וֹ\rb* \rb he would stop|יָסֻ֥ר\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb to eat.|לֶאֱכָל־\rb*\rb |לָֽחֶם׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then the woman said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her husband,|אִישָׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb “Behold,|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb now|נָ֣א\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֔עְתִּי\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the one|ה֑וּא\rb* \rb who often|תָּמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb comes our way|עֹבֵ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb is a holy|קָד֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God.|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \v 10 \rb Please|נָּ֤א\rb* \rb let us make|נַֽעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb a small|קְטַנָּ֔ה\rb* \rb room upstairs|עֲלִיַּת־\rb*\rb |קִיר֙\rb* \rb and put|וְנָשִׂ֨ים\rb* \rb in it|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb a bed,|מִטָּ֥ה\rb* \rb a table,|וְשֻׁלְחָ֖ן\rb* \rb a chair,|וְכִסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb and a lamp|וּמְנוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb for him.|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb Then when|וְהָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb he comes|בְּבֹא֥וֹ\rb* \rb to us,|אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb he can stay|יָס֥וּר\rb* \rb there.”|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb |וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb One day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb Elisha came to visit|וַיָּ֣בֹא\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑מָּה\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּ֥סַר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his upper room|הָעֲלִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to lie down.|וַיִּשְׁכַּב־\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gehazi|גֵּחֲזִ֣י\rb* \rb his servant,|נַעֲר֔וֹ\rb* \rb “Call|קְרָ֖א\rb* \rb the|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb Shunammite woman.”|לַשּׁוּנַמִּ֣ית\rb*
\p \rb And when he had called|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb her,|לָ֔הּ\rb* \rb she stood|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb before him,|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb* \v 13 \rb and Elisha said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to Gehazi,|ל֗וֹ\rb* \rb “Now|נָ֣א\rb* \rb tell|אֱמָר־\rb* \rb her,|אֵלֶיהָ֮\rb* \rb ‘Look,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb you have gone to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֒\rb* \rb trouble|חָרַ֣דְתְּ׀\rb*\rb |הַחֲרָדָ֣ה\rb* \rb for us.|אֵלֵינוּ֮\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb What|מֶ֚ה\rb* \rb can we do|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb for you?|לָ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |הֲיֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb Can we speak|לְדַבֶּר־\rb* \rb on your behalf to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb or|א֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the army?’”|הַצָּבָ֑א\rb*
\p \rb “I|אָנֹכִ֥י\rb* \rb have a home|יֹשָֽׁבֶת׃\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb my own people,”|עַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb she replied.|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb So he asked,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Then what|וּמֶ֖ה\rb* \rb should be done|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb for her?”|לָ֑הּ\rb*
\p \rb “Well,|אֲבָ֛ל\rb* \rb she has|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb son,”|בֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb Gehazi|גֵּיחֲזִ֗י\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “and her husband|וְאִישָׁ֥הּ\rb* \rb is old.”|זָקֵֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “Call|קְרָא־\rb* \rb her,”|לָ֑הּ\rb* \rb said Elisha.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb So Gehazi called|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb her,|לָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and she stood|וַֽתַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb in the doorway.|בַּפָּֽתַח׃\rb* \v 16 \rb And Elisha declared,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “At this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb time|לַמּוֹעֵ֤ד\rb* \rb next year,|כָּעֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |חַיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb you|אַתִּי\rb* \rb will hold|חֹבֶ֣קֶת\rb* \rb a son in your arms.”|בֵּ֑ן\rb*
\p \rb “No,|אַל־\rb* \rb my lord,”|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb* \rb she said.|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb lie|תְּכַזֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb to your maidservant,|בְּשִׁפְחָתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb O man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God.”|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb But the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb did conceive,|וַתַּ֥הַר\rb* \rb and at that|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb time|לַמּוֹעֵ֤ד\rb* \rb the next year|כָּעֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |חַיָּ֔ה\rb* \rb she gave birth to|וַתֵּ֣לֶד\rb* \rb a son,|בֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb just as|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb* \rb had told|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb her.|אֵלֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\s1 Elisha Raises the Shunammite’s Son
\r \ref Acts 20:7–12|ACT 20:7-12\ref*)
\p \v 18 \rb And|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb the child|הַיָּ֑לֶד\rb* \rb grew,|וַיִּגְדַּ֖ל\rb* \rb and one day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb he went out|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father,|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb who was with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the harvesters.|הַקֹּצְרִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “My head!|רֹאשִׁ֣י׀\rb* \rb My head!”|רֹאשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb he complained|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his father.|אָבִ֖יו\rb*
\p \rb So his father told|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb a servant,|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb “Carry him|שָׂאֵ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his mother.”|אִמּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb After the servant had picked him up|וַיִּשָּׂאֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb and carried him|וַיְבִיאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his mother,|אִמּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb the boy sat|וַיֵּ֧שֶׁב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb her lap|בִּרְכֶּ֛יהָ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb noon,|הַֽצָּהֳרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and then he died.|וַיָּמֹֽת׃\rb* \v 21 \rb And she went up|וַתַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb and laid him|וַתַּשְׁכִּבֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bed|מִטַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb Then she shut the door|וַתִּסְגֹּ֥ר\rb*\rb |בַּעֲד֖וֹ\rb* \rb and went out.|וַתֵּצֵֽא׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And the woman called|וַתִּקְרָא֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb her husband|אִישָׁהּ֒\rb* \rb and said,|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb send|שִׁלְחָ֨ה\rb* \rb me|לִי֙\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the servants|הַנְּעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and one|וְאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the donkeys,|הָאֲתֹנ֑וֹת\rb* \rb that I may go quickly|וְאָר֛וּצָה\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb and return.”|וְאָשֽׁוּבָה׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb “Why|מַ֠דּוּעַ\rb* \rb would you|אַתִּי\rb* \rb go|הֹלַכְתִּי\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb today?”|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “It is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb a New Moon|חֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb a Sabbath.”|שַׁבָּ֑ת\rb*
\p \rb “Everything is all right,”|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb she said.|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Then she saddled|וַֽתַּחֲבֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb the donkey|הָֽאָת֔וֹן\rb* \rb and told|וַתֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb her servant,|נַעֲרָ֖הּ\rb* \rb “Drive|נְהַ֣ג\rb* \rb onward;|וָלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb slow|תַּעֲצָר־\rb* \rb the pace|לִרְכֹּ֔ב\rb* \rb for me|לִ֣י\rb*\rb |כִּ֖י\rb* \rb unless|אִם־\rb* \rb I tell|אָמַ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb you.”|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \v 25 \rb So she set out|וַתֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb and went|וַתָּב֛וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Carmel.|הַכַּרְמֶ֑ל\rb*\rb |וַ֠יְהִי\rb*
\p \rb When the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְא֨וֹת\rb* \rb her|אֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb at a distance,|מִנֶּ֔גֶד\rb* \rb he said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servant|נַעֲר֔וֹ\rb* \rb Gehazi,|גֵּיחֲזִ֣י\rb* \rb “Look,|הִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb there is|הַלָּֽז׃\rb* \rb the Shunammite woman.|הַשּׁוּנַמִּ֥ית\rb* \v 26 \rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb run out|רֽוּץ־\rb* \rb now|עַתָּה֮\rb* \rb to meet her|לִקְרָאתָהּ֒\rb* \rb and ask,|וֶאֱמָר־\rb* \rb ‘Are you all right?|הֲשָׁל֥וֹם\rb*\rb |לָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb Is your husband|לְאִישֵׁ֖ךְ\rb* \rb all right?|הֲשָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb Is your child|לַיָּ֑לֶד\rb* \rb all right?’”|הֲשָׁל֣וֹם\rb*
\p \rb And she answered,|וַתֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Everything is all right.”|שָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb When she reached|וַתָּבֹ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountain,|הָהָ֔ר\rb* \rb she clung|וַֽתַּחֲזֵ֖ק\rb* \rb to his feet.|בְּרַגְלָ֑יו\rb* \rb Gehazi|גֵּֽיחֲזִ֜י\rb* \rb came over|וַיִּגַּ֨שׁ\rb* \rb to push her away,|לְהָדְפָ֗הּ\rb* \rb but the man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb* \rb “Leave her alone,|הַרְפֵּֽה־\rb*\rb |לָהּ֙\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb her soul|נַפְשָׁ֣הּ\rb* \rb is in deep distress,|מָֽרָה־\rb* \rb and the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb has hidden|הֶעְלִ֣ים\rb* \rb it from me|מִמֶּ֔נִּי\rb* \rb and has not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb told|הִגִּ֖יד\rb* \rb me.”|לִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Then she said,|וַתֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Did I ask you|הֲשָׁאַ֥לְתִּי\rb* \rb for a son,|בֵ֖ן\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb my lord?|אֲדֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb Didn’t|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb I say,|אָמַ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb ‘Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb deceive me?’”|תַשְׁלֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹתִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb So Elisha said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to Gehazi,|לְגֵיחֲזִ֜י\rb* \rb “Tie up|חֲגֹ֣ר\rb* \rb your garment,|מָתְנֶ֗יךָ\rb*\f + \fr 4:29 \ft Literally \fqa Gird up your loins\f* \rb take|וְקַ֨ח\rb* \rb my staff|מִשְׁעַנְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb in your hand,|בְיָדְךָ֮\rb* \rb and go!|וָלֵךְ֒\rb* \rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you meet|תִמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb anyone,|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb greet him,|תְבָרְכֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb and if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb anyone|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb greets you,|יְבָרֶכְךָ֥\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb answer him.|תַעֲנֶנּ֑וּ\rb* \rb Then lay|וְשַׂמְתָּ֥\rb* \rb my staff|מִשְׁעַנְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the boy’s|הַנָּֽעַר׃\rb* \rb face.”|פְּנֵ֥י\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb And the mother|אֵ֣ם\rb* \rb of the boy|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb said,|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb lives|חַי־\rb* \rb and as you yourself|נַפְשְׁךָ֖\rb* \rb live,|וְחֵֽי־\rb* \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb leave you.”|אֶעֶזְבֶ֑ךָּ\rb* \rb So he got up|וַיָּ֖קָם\rb* \rb and followed|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb her.|אַחֲרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb Gehazi|וְגֵחֲזִ֞י\rb* \rb went on|עָבַ֣ר\rb* \rb ahead of them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and laid|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the staff|הַמִּשְׁעֶ֙נֶת֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the boy’s|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb face,|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb but there was no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb sound|ק֖וֹל\rb* \rb or|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb response.|קָ֑שֶׁב\rb* \rb So he went back|וַיָּ֤שָׁב\rb* \rb to meet Elisha|לִקְרָאתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb him,|ל֣וֹ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “The boy|הַנָּֽעַר׃\rb* \rb has not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb awakened.”|הֵקִ֖יץ\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb When Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֖ע\rb* \rb reached|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb the house,|הַבָּ֑יְתָה\rb* \rb there was|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the boy|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb lying|מֻשְׁכָּ֖ב\rb* \rb dead|מֵ֔ת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his bed.|מִטָּתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 33 \rb So he went in,|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb* \rb closed|וַיִּסְגֹּ֥ר\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֖לֶת\rb* \rb behind|בְּעַ֣ד\rb* \rb the two of them,|שְׁנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֖ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb Then Elisha got on the bed|וַיַּ֜עַל\rb* \rb and lay|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the boy,|הַיֶּ֗לֶד\rb*\rb |וַיָּשֶׂם֩\rb* \rb mouth|פִּ֨יו\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb mouth,|פִּ֜יו\rb* \rb eye|וְעֵינָ֤יו\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb eye,|עֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb and hand|וְכַפָּ֣יו\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb hand.|כַּפּוֹ\rb* \rb As he stretched himself out|וַיִּגְהַ֖ר\rb* \rb over him,|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb the boy’s|הַיָּֽלֶד׃\rb* \rb body|בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb became warm.|וַיָּ֖חָם\rb* \v 35 \rb Elisha turned away|וַיָּ֜שָׁב\rb* \rb and paced|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb back and forth|אַחַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הֵ֙נָּה֙\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb across the room.|בַּבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb Then he got on the bed|וַיַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb and stretched himself out|וַיִּגְהַ֣ר\rb* \rb over the boy again,|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb and the boy|הַנַּ֙עַר֙\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb sneezed|וַיְזוֹרֵ֤ר\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb and opened|וַיִּפְקַ֥ח\rb*\rb |הַנַּ֖עַר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his eyes.|עֵינָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb Elisha summoned|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Gehazi|גֵּיחֲזִ֗י\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Call|וַיִּקְרָאֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb the|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb Shunammite woman.”|הַשֻּׁנַמִּ֣ית\rb* \rb So he called her|קְרָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb and she came.|וַתָּב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb*
\p \rb Then Elisha said,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Pick up|שְׂאִ֥י\rb* \rb your son.”|בְנֵֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb She came in,|וַתָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb fell|וַתִּפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb his feet,|רַגְלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and bowed|וַתִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb to the ground.|אָ֑רְצָה\rb* \rb Then she picked up|וַתִּשָּׂ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and went out.|וַתֵּצֵֽא׃פ\rb*
\s1 Elisha Purifies the Poisonous Stew
\p \v 38 \rb When Elisha|וֶאֱלִישָׁ֞ע\rb* \rb returned|שָׁ֤ב\rb* \rb to Gilgal,|הַגִּלְגָּ֙לָה֙\rb* \rb there was a famine|וְהָרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb in the land.|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb As the sons|וּבְנֵי֙\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb were sitting|יֹשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb at his feet,|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to his attendant,|לְנַעֲר֗וֹ\rb* \rb “Put on|שְׁפֹת֙\rb* \rb the large|הַגְּדוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb pot|הַסִּ֣יר\rb* \rb and boil|וּבַשֵּׁ֥ל\rb* \rb some stew|נָזִ֖יד\rb* \rb for the sons|לִבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the prophets.”|הַנְּבִיאִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 39 \rb One of them|אֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the field|הַשָּׂדֶה֮\rb* \rb to gather|לְלַקֵּ֣ט\rb* \rb herbs,|אֹרֹת֒\rb* \rb and he found|וַיִּמְצָא֙\rb* \rb a wild|שָׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb vine|גֶּ֣פֶן\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּ֛נּוּ\rb* \rb which he gathered|וַיְלַקֵּ֥ט\rb* \rb as many wild|שָׂדֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |מְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb gourds|פַּקֻּעֹ֥ת\rb* \rb as his garment could hold.|בִגְד֑וֹ\rb* \rb Then he came back|וַיָּבֹ֗א\rb* \rb and cut them up|וַיְפַלַּ֛ח\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the pot|סִ֥יר\rb* \rb of stew,|הַנָּזִ֖יד\rb* \rb though|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb no one|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb knew what they were.|יָדָֽעוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 40 \rb And they poured it out|וַיִּֽצְק֥וּ\rb* \rb for the men|לַאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb to eat,|לֶאֱכ֑וֹל\rb*\rb |וַ֠יְהִי\rb* \rb but when they tasted|כְּאָכְלָ֨ם\rb* \rb the stew|מֵהַנָּזִ֜יד\rb* \rb they|וְהֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb cried out,|צָעָ֗קוּ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb “There is death|מָ֤וֶת\rb* \rb in the pot,|בַּסִּיר֙\rb* \rb O man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God!”|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb And they could not|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יָכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb eat it.|לֶאֱכֹֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 41 \rb Then Elisha said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Get|וּקְחוּ־\rb* \rb some flour.”|קֶ֔מַח\rb* \rb He threw|וַיַּשְׁלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb it into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the pot|הַסִּ֑יר\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Pour it out|צַ֤ק\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָם֙\rb* \rb to eat.”|וְיֹאכֵ֔לוּ\rb* \rb And there was|הָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb harmful|רָ֖ע\rb* \rb in the pot.|בַּסִּֽיר׃ס\rb*
\s1 Feeding a Hundred Men
\r \ref Matthew 15:29–39|MAT 15:29-39\ref*; \ref Mark 8:1–10|MRK 8:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 42 \rb Now a man|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִבַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb from Baal-shalishah|שָׁלִ֗שָׁה\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֵא֩\rb* \rb came|בָּ֜א\rb* \rb to the man|לְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb with a sack|בְּצִקְלֹנ֑וֹ\rb* \rb of twenty|עֶשְׂרִֽים־\rb* \rb loaves|לֶ֤חֶם\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb from the first|בִּכּוּרִים֙\rb* \rb ripe grain.|וְכַרְמֶ֖ל\rb*
\p \rb “Give|תֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb it to the people|לָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb to eat,”|וְיֹאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb said Elisha.|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 43 \rb But his servant|מְשָׁ֣רְת֔וֹ\rb* \rb asked,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “How|מָ֚ה\rb* \rb am I to set|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb twenty loaves|זֶ֔ה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb a hundred|מֵ֣אָה\rb* \rb men?”|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*
\p \rb “Give|תֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb it to the people|לָעָם֙\rb* \rb to eat,”|וְיֹאכֵ֔לוּ\rb* \rb said Elisha,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb ‘They will eat|אָכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb and have some left over.’”|וְהוֹתֵֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 44 \rb So he set it|וַיִּתֵּ֧ן\rb* \rb before them,|לִפְנֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and they ate|וַיֹּאכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb and had some left over,|וַיּוֹתִ֖רוּ\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*
\c 5
\s1 Naaman Cured of Leprosy
\r \ref Luke 17:11–19|LUK 17:11-19\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now Naaman,|וְ֠נַעֲמָן\rb* \rb the commander|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the army|צְבָ֨א\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram,|אֲרָ֜ם\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֨וֹל\rb* \rb man|אִישׁ֩\rb* \rb in his master’s|אֲדֹנָיו֙\rb* \rb sight|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb and highly regarded,|וּנְשֻׂ֣א\rb*\rb |פָנִ֔ים\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb through him|ב֛וֹ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb had given|נָֽתַן־\rb* \rb victory|תְּשׁוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Aram.|לַאֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb And he was|הָיָ֛ה\rb* \rb a mighty|גִּבּ֥וֹר\rb* \rb man|וְהָאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb of valor,|חַ֖יִל\rb* \rb but he was a leper.|מְצֹרָֽע׃\rb*\f + \fr 5:1 \ft A \fqa leper\ft , or one with \fqa leprosy\ft , was one afflicted with a skin disease; here and throughout this chapter; see \ref Leviticus 13|LEV 13\ref*.\f*
\p \v 2 \rb At this time the Arameans|וַאֲרָם֙\rb* \rb had gone out|יָצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb in bands|גְדוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and had taken|וַיִּשְׁבּ֛וּ\rb* \rb a young|קְטַנָּ֑ה\rb* \rb girl|נַעֲרָ֣ה\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and she was serving|וַתְּהִ֕י\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb Naaman’s|נַעֲמָֽן׃\rb* \rb wife.|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb* \v 3 \rb She said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb her mistress,|גְּבִרְתָּ֔הּ\rb* \rb “If only|אַחֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb would go to the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is in Samaria,|בְּשֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb*\rb |אָ֛ז\rb* \rb he would cure|יֶאֱסֹ֥ף\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb of his leprosy.”|מִצָּרַעְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb And Naaman went|וַיָּבֹ֕א\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגֵּ֥ד\rb* \rb his master|לַאדֹנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb what|כָּזֹ֤את\rb*\rb |וְכָזֹאת֙\rb* \rb the girl|הַֽנַּעֲרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb had said.|דִּבְּרָ֣ה\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb “Go now,”|לֶךְ־\rb*\rb |בֹּ֔א\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram,|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb “and I will send you with|וְאֶשְׁלְחָ֥ה\rb* \rb a letter|סֵ֖פֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel.”|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*
\p \rb So Naaman departed,|וַיֵּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb taking|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb with him|בְּיָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb talents|כִּכְּרֵי־\rb* \rb of silver,|כֶ֗סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 5:5 \fqa \ref 10|0\ref* talents\ft is \ref approximately 754|754\ref* pounds or 342 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb six|וְשֵׁ֤שֶׁת\rb* \rb thousand shekels|אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb of gold,|זָהָ֔ב\rb*\f + \fr 5:5 \fqa \ref 6,000|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 150|150\ref*.8 pounds or 68.4 kilograms of gold.\f* \rb and ten|וְעֶ֖שֶׂר\rb* \rb sets|חֲלִיפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of clothing.|בְּגָדִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb And the letter|הַסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb that he took|וַיָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb stated:|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “With|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb letter|הַסֵּ֤פֶר\rb* \rb I am sending|שָׁלַ֤חְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb my servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb Naaman,|נַעֲמָ֣ן\rb* \rb so that you may cure him|וַאֲסַפְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of his leprosy.”|מִצָּרַעְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb |וַיְהִ֡י\rb* \rb When the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֨ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb read|כִּקְרֹא֩\rb* \rb the letter,|הַסֵּ֜פֶר\rb* \rb he tore|וַיִּקְרַ֣ע\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָ֗יו\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Am I|אָ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb God,|הַאֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \rb killing|לְהָמִ֣ית\rb* \rb and giving life,|וּֽלְהַחֲי֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this man|זֶה֙\rb* \rb expects|שֹׁלֵ֣חַ\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb to cure|לֶאֱסֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb a leper?|מִצָּֽרַעְתּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אַךְ־\rb* \rb Surely you can|דְּעֽוּ־\rb*\rb |נָא֙\rb* \rb see|וּרְא֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb is seeking a quarrel|מִתְאַנֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb with me!”|לִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb when Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb heard|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ׀\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had torn|קָרַ֤ע\rb* \rb his clothes,|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb he sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb a message to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king:|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Why|לָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb have you torn|קָרַ֖עְתָּ\rb* \rb your clothes?|בְּגָדֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb let the man come|יָבֹֽא־\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb and he will know|וְיֵדַ֕ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb there is|יֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb in Israel.”|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So Naaman|נַעֲמָ֖ן\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb with his horses|בְּסוּסוֹ\rb* \rb and chariots|וּבְרִכְבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb at the door|פֶּֽתַח־\rb* \rb of Elisha’s|לֶאֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb* \rb house.|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֖ע\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb a messenger,|מַלְאָ֣ךְ\rb* \rb who said,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Go|הָל֗וֹךְ\rb* \rb and wash yourself|וְרָחַצְתָּ֤\rb* \rb seven|שֶֽׁבַע־\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִים֙\rb* \rb in the Jordan,|בַּיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb and your flesh|בְּשָׂרְךָ֛\rb* \rb will be restored,|וְיָשֹׁ֧ב\rb* \rb and you will be clean.”|וּטְהָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb But Naaman|נַעֲמָ֖ן\rb* \rb went away|וַיֵּלַ֑ךְ\rb* \rb angry,|וַיִּקְצֹ֥ף\rb* \rb saying,|וַיֹּאמֶר֩\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb “I thought that|אָמַ֜רְתִּי\rb* \rb he would surely come out,|יֵצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |יָצ֗וֹא\rb* \rb stand|וְעָמַד֙\rb* \rb and call|וְקָרָא֙\rb* \rb on the name|בְּשֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb his God,|אֱלֹהָ֔יו\rb* \rb and wave|וְהֵנִ֥יף\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֛וֹ\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb the spot|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb to cure|וְאָסַ֥ף\rb* \rb my leprosy.|הַמְּצֹרָֽע׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Are not|הֲלֹ֡א\rb* \rb the Abanah|אֲבָנָה\rb* \rb and Pharpar,|וּפַרְפַּ֜ר\rb* \rb the rivers|נַהֲר֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Damascus,|דַּמֶּ֗שֶׂק\rb* \rb better|טוֹב֩\rb* \rb than all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the waters|מֵימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb Could I not|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb have washed|אֶרְחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb in them|בָּהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and been cleansed?”|וְטָהָ֑רְתִּי\rb* \rb So he turned|וַיִּ֖פֶן\rb* \rb and went away|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb in a rage.|בְּחֵמָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Naaman’s servants, however,|עֲבָדָיו֮\rb* \rb approached him|וַיִּגְּשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb and said,|וַיְדַבְּר֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֒\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “My father,|אָבִי֙\rb* \rb if the prophet|הַנָּבִ֛יא\rb* \rb had told|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to do some great|גָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb thing,|דָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb would you not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb have done it?|תַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb How much more, then,|וְאַ֛ף\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he tells|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb you,|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb ‘Wash|רְחַ֥ץ\rb* \rb and be cleansed’?”|וּטְהָֽר׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb So Naaman went down|וַיֵּ֗רֶד\rb* \rb and dipped himself|וַיִּטְבֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb in the Jordan|בַּיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb times,|פְּעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֖ר\rb* \rb of the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and his flesh|בְּשָׂר֗וֹ\rb* \rb was restored|וַיָּ֣שָׁב\rb* \rb and became like that|כִּבְשַׂ֛ר\rb* \rb of a little|קָטֹ֖ן\rb* \rb child,|נַ֥עַר\rb* \rb and he was clean.|וַיִּטְהָֽר׃\rb*
\s1 Gehazi’s Greed and Leprosy
\p \v 15 \rb Then Naaman|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb and all|וְכָֽל־\rb* \rb his attendants|מַחֲנֵ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹא֮\rb* \rb went back|וַיָּשָׁב֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb before him,|לְפָנָיו֒\rb* \rb and declared,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Now|נָ֤א\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb* \rb for sure|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb there is no|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb except|כִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb in Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb So|וְעַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֥א\rb* \rb accept|קַח־\rb* \rb a gift|בְרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb your servant.”|עַבְדֶּֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb But Elisha replied,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “As surely as the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb before whom|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb I stand,|עָמַ֥דְתִּי\rb* \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb accept it.”|אֶקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb And although Naaman urged|וַיִּפְצַר־\rb* \rb him|בּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb to accept it,|לָקַ֖חַת\rb* \rb he refused.|וַיְמָאֵֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb “If you will not,”|וָלֹ֕א\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb* \rb Naaman,|נַעֲמָן֒\rb* \rb “please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb let me, your servant,|לְעַבְדְּךָ֔\rb* \rb be given|יֻתַּן־\rb* \rb as much soil|אֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb as a pair|צֶֽמֶד־\rb* \rb of mules|פְּרָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb can carry.|מַשָּׂ֥א\rb* \rb For|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֜\rb* \rb will never|לֽוֹא־\rb* \rb again|ע֨וֹד\rb* \rb make|יַעֲשֶׂה֩\rb* \rb a burnt offering|עֹלָ֤ה\rb* \rb or a sacrifice|וָזֶ֙בַח֙\rb* \rb to any other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb god|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb but|אִם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb Yet may the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb forgive|יִסְלַ֥ח\rb* \rb your servant|לְעַבְדֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb one thing:|לַדָּבָ֣ר\rb* \rb When my master|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb goes into|בְּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb the temple|בֵית־\rb* \rb of Rimmon|רִמּוֹן֩\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֨ת\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֜מָּה\rb* \rb and he|וְה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb leans|נִשְׁעָ֣ן\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my arm,|יָדִ֗י\rb* \rb and I bow down|וְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֵ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb in the temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Rimmon,|רִמֹּ֔ן\rb*\rb |בְּהִשְׁתַּחֲוָיָ֙תִי֙\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |רִמֹּ֔ן\rb* \rb may|נא\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb forgive|יִסְלַח־\rb* \rb your servant|לְעַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb matter.”|בַּדָּבָ֥ר\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb “Go|לֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in peace,”|לְשָׁל֑וֹם\rb* \rb said Elisha.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb But after Naaman had traveled|וַיֵּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |מֵאִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb a short distance,|כִּבְרַת־\rb* \v 20 \rb Gehazi,|גֵּיחֲזִ֗י\rb* \rb the servant|נַעַר֮\rb* \rb of Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֣ע\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִים֒\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Look,|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb has spared|חָשַׂ֣ךְ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Aramean,|הָֽאֲרַמִּי֙\rb* \rb Naaman,|נַעֲמָ֤ן\rb* \rb by not accepting|מִקַּ֥חַת\rb*\rb |מִיָּד֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he brought.|הֵבִ֑יא\rb* \rb As surely as the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb lives,|חַי־\rb* \rb I will run|רַ֣צְתִּי\rb* \rb after him|אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb and get|וְלָקַחְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb something|מְאֽוּמָה׃\rb* \rb from him.”|מֵאִתּ֖וֹ\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb So Gehazi|גֵּיחֲזִ֖י\rb* \rb pursued|וַיִּרְדֹּ֥ף\rb* \rb Naaman.|נַֽעֲמָ֑ן\rb* \rb And when Naaman|נַֽעֲמָן֙\rb* \rb saw him|וַיִּרְאֶ֤ה\rb* \rb running|רָ֣ץ\rb* \rb toward him,|אַחֲרָ֔יו\rb* \rb he got down|וַיִּפֹּ֞ל\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֧ל\rb* \rb the chariot|הַמֶּרְכָּבָ֛ה\rb* \rb to meet him|לִקְרָאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb “Is everything all right?”|הֲשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb “Everything is all right,”|שָׁל֗וֹם\rb* \rb Gehazi replied.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb “My master|אֲדֹנִי֮\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to say,|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb ‘Look,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵֽי־\rb* \rb young men|נְעָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb from the sons|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֑ים\rb* \rb have just now|עַתָּ֡ה\rb*\rb |זֶ֠ה\rb* \rb come|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֧י\rb* \rb from the hill country|מֵהַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Ephraim.|אֶפְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb Please|נָּ֤א\rb* \rb give|תְּנָה־\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb a talent|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 5:22 \fqa A talent\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref*.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of silver.\f* \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb sets|חֲלִפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of clothing.’”|בְּגָדִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb But Naaman|נַעֲמָ֔ן\rb* \rb insisted,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Please,|הוֹאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb take|קַ֣ח\rb* \rb two talents.”|כִּכָּרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb And he urged|וַיִּפְרָץ־\rb* \rb Gehazi to accept them.|בּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Then he tied up|וַיָּצַר֩\rb* \rb two talents|כִּכְּרַ֨יִם\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֜סֶף\rb* \rb in two|בִּשְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb bags|חֲרִטִ֗ים\rb* \rb along with two|וּשְׁתֵּי֙\rb* \rb sets|חֲלִפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of clothing|בְּגָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and gave them|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his servants,|נְעָרָ֔יו\rb* \rb who carried them|וַיִּשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb ahead of Gehazi.|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb When Gehazi came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the hill,|הָעֹ֔פֶל\rb* \rb he took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the gifts from the servants|מִיָּדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and stored them|וַיִּפְקֹ֣ד\rb* \rb in the house.|בַּבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb Then he dismissed|וַיְשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men,|הָאֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and they departed.|וַיֵּלֵֽכוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb When Gehazi|וְהוּא־\rb* \rb went in|בָא֙\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master,|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him,|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “Gehazi,|גֵּחֲזִ֑י\rb* \rb where have you been?”|מֵאָן\rb*
\p \rb “Your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֖\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go|הָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb anywhere,”|אָ֥נֶה\rb*\rb |וָאָֽנָה׃\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb But Elisha questioned him,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “Did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb my spirit|לִבִּ֣י\rb* \rb go with you|הָלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the man|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb got down|הָֽפַךְ־\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb his chariot|מֶרְכַּבְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to meet you?|לִקְרָאתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Is this the time|הַעֵ֞ת\rb* \rb to accept|לָקַ֤חַת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb money|הַכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb*\rb |וְלָקַ֣חַת\rb* \rb and clothing,|בְּגָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb olive groves|וְזֵיתִ֤ים\rb* \rb and vineyards,|וּכְרָמִים֙\rb* \rb sheep|וְצֹ֣אן\rb* \rb and oxen,|וּבָקָ֔ר\rb* \rb menservants|וַעֲבָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb and maidservants?|וּשְׁפָחֽוֹת׃\rb* \v 27 \rb Therefore, the leprosy|וְצָרַ֤עַת\rb* \rb of Naaman|נַֽעֲמָן֙\rb* \rb will cling|תִּֽדְבַּק־\rb* \rb to you|בְּךָ֔\rb* \rb and your descendants|וּֽבְזַרְעֲךָ\rb* \rb forever!”|לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb And as Gehazi left|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb his presence,|מִלְּפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb he was leprous—|מְצֹרָ֥ע\rb* \rb as white as snow.|כַּשָּֽׁלֶג׃ס\rb*
\c 6
\s1 The Axe Head Floats
\p \v 1 \rb Now the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֖ים\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֣א\rb* \rb take note|הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb that the place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֜חְנוּ\rb* \rb meet|יֹשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb with you|לְפָנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb is too small|צַ֥ר\rb* \rb for us.|מִמֶּֽנּוּ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Please|נָּ֣א\rb* \rb let us go|נֵֽלֲכָה־\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Jordan,|הַיַּרְדֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb where|מִשָּׁם֙\rb* \rb each of us|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb can get|וְנִקְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb log|קוֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb so we can build|וְנַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb ourselves|לָּ֥נוּ\rb* \rb a place|מָק֖וֹם\rb* \rb to live|לָשֶׁ֣בֶת\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb there.”|שָׁ֛ם\rb*
\p \rb “Go,”|לֵֽכוּ׃\rb* \rb said Elisha.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Then one of them|הָֽאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֖א\rb*\rb |ה֥וֹאֶל\rb* \rb come|וְלֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb your servants.”|עֲבָדֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb “I will|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb come,”|אֵלֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So Elisha went|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb with them,|אִתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb and when they came|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb to the Jordan,|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔נָה\rb* \rb they began to cut down|וַֽיִּגְזְר֖וּ\rb* \rb some trees.|הָעֵצִֽים׃\rb* \v 5 \rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb As one|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb of them was cutting down|מַפִּ֣יל\rb* \rb a tree,|הַקּוֹרָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the iron axe head|הַבַּרְזֶ֖ל\rb* \rb fell|נָפַ֣ל\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the water.|הַמָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb “Oh,|אֲהָ֥הּ\rb* \rb my master,”|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb he cried out,|וַיִּצְעַ֥ק\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “it|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was borrowed!”|שָׁאֽוּל׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb “Where|אָ֣נָה\rb* \rb did it fall?”|נָפָ֑ל\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God.|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*
\p \rb And when he showed|וַיַּרְאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb him|אֶת־\rb* \rb the place,|הַמָּק֔וֹם\rb* \rb the man of God cut|וַיִּקְצָב־\rb* \rb a stick,|עֵץ֙\rb* \rb threw|וַיַּשְׁלֶךְ־\rb* \rb it there,|שָׁ֔מָּה\rb* \rb and made the iron|הַבַּרְזֶֽל׃\rb* \rb float.|וַיָּ֖צֶף\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb “Lift it out,”|הָ֣רֶם\rb*\rb |לָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb and the man reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb and took it.|וַיִּקָּחֵֽהוּ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Elisha Captures the Blinded Arameans
\p \v 8 \rb Now the king|וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb at war|נִלְחָ֖ם\rb* \rb against Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb After consulting|וַיִּוָּעַץ֙\rb* \rb with|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants,|עֲבָדָ֣יו\rb* \rb he said,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “My camp will be|תַּחֲנֹתִֽי׃\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb such|פְּלֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb and such|אַלְמֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb a place.”|מְק֛וֹם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel:|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Be careful not|הִשָּׁ֕מֶר\rb* \rb to pass by|מֵעֲבֹ֖ר\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place,|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֥ם\rb* \rb are going down|נְחִתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb there.”|שָׁ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb* \rb had pointed out.|אָֽמַר־\rb*\rb |ל֧וֹ\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb Time and again|אַחַ֖ת\rb*\f + \fr 6:10 \ft Literally \fqa Not once and not twice\f* \rb |וְלֹ֥א\rb*\rb |שְׁתָּֽיִם׃\rb*\rb Elisha warned the king,|וְהִזְהִירָהּ\rb* \rb so that he was on his guard|וְנִשְׁמַ֣ר\rb* \rb in such places.|שָׁ֑ם\rb* \v 11 \rb For|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb reason|הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb became enraged|וַיִּסָּעֵר֙\rb*\rb |לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and called|וַיִּקְרָ֤א\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb to demand|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb of them,|אֶל־\rb* \rb “Tell me,|תַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb which one|מִ֥י\rb* \rb of us|מִשֶּׁלָּ֖נוּ\rb* \rb is on the side|אֶל־\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel?”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb But one|אַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of his servants|מֵֽעֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “No one,|ל֖וֹא\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king.|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֤ע\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb tells|יַגִּיד֙\rb* \rb the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the very words|הַ֨דְּבָרִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you speak|תְּדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb in your bedroom.”|בַּחֲדַ֥ר\rb*\rb |מִשְׁכָּבֶֽךָ׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb So the king said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Go|לְכ֤וּ\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb where|אֵיכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb he is,|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb that I may send|וְאֶשְׁלַ֖ח\rb* \rb men to capture him.”|וְאֶקָּחֵ֑הוּ\rb*
\p \rb On receiving the report,|וַיֻּגַּד־\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb “Elisha is in Dothan,”|בְדֹתָֽן׃\rb* \v 14 \rb the king of Aram sent|וַיִּשְׁלַח־\rb* \rb horses,|סוּסִ֥ים\rb* \rb chariots,|וְרֶ֖כֶב\rb* \rb and a great|כָּבֵ֑ד\rb* \rb army.|וְחַ֣יִל\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛מָּה\rb* \rb They went there|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb by night|לַ֔יְלָה\rb* \rb and surrounded|וַיַּקִּ֖פוּ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the city.|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb When the servant|מְשָׁרֵ֨ת\rb* \rb of the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֮\rb* \rb got up|לָקוּם֒\rb* \rb and went out|וַיֵּצֵ֕א\rb* \rb early in the morning,|וַ֠יַּשְׁכֵּם\rb* \rb behold,|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb an army|חַ֛יִל\rb* \rb with horses|וְס֣וּס\rb* \rb and chariots|וָרָ֑כֶב\rb* \rb had surrounded|סוֹבֵ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city.|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb So he|נַעֲר֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֛יו\rb* \rb asked Elisha,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “Oh,|אֲהָ֥הּ\rb* \rb my master,|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb what|אֵיכָ֥ה\rb* \rb are we to do?”|נַֽעֲשֶֽׂה׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid,”|תִּירָ֑א\rb* \rb Elisha answered,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “for|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb those who are|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with us|אִתָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb are more|רַבִּים֙\rb* \rb than those who are|מֵאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb with them.”|אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then Elisha|אֱלִישָׁע֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb prayed,|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֤ל\rb* \rb “O LORD,|יְהוָ֕ה\rb* \rb please|נָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb open|פְּקַח־\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָ֖יו\rb* \rb that he may see.”|וְיִרְאֶ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|וַיִּפְקַ֤ח\rb* \rb the eyes|עֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the young man,|הַנַּ֔עַר\rb* \rb and he saw that|וַיַּ֗רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the hills|הָהָ֜ר\rb* \rb were full of|מָלֵ֨א\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֥ים\rb* \rb and chariots|וְרֶ֛כֶב\rb* \rb of fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb all around|סְבִיבֹ֥ת\rb* \rb Elisha.|אֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb As the Arameans came down|וַיֵּרְדוּ֮\rb* \rb against him,|אֵלָיו֒\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֤ע\rb* \rb prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strike|הַךְ־\rb* \rb these|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb people|הַגּוֹי־\rb* \rb with blindness.”|בַּסַּנְוֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb So He struck them|וַיַּכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb with blindness,|בַּסַּנְוֵרִ֖ים\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of Elisha.|אֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֗ע\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb “This|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the way,|הַדֶּרֶךְ֮\rb* \rb and this|זֹ֣ה\rb* \rb is not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb the city.|הָעִיר֒\rb* \rb Follow|וְאוֹלִ֣יכָה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb me,|אַחֲרַ֔י\rb* \rb and I will take|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are seeking.”|תְּבַקֵּשׁ֑וּן\rb* \rb And he led|וַיֹּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to Samaria.|שֹׁמְרֽוֹנָה׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb |וַיְהִי֮\rb* \rb When they had entered|כְּבֹאָ֣ם\rb* \rb Samaria,|שֹׁמְרוֹן֒\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “O LORD,|יְהוָ֕ה\rb* \rb open|פְּקַ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the eyes|עֵינֵֽי־\rb* \rb of these men|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb that they may see.”|וְיִרְא֑וּ\rb*
\p \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb opened|וַיִּפְקַ֤ח\rb* \rb their eyes,|עֵ֣ינֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and they looked around|וַיִּרְא֕וּ\rb* \rb and discovered that|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb they were in|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb Samaria.|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb And when the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְאֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb them,|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb “My father,|אָבִֽי׃\rb* \rb shall I kill them?|אַכֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb Shall I kill them?”|הַאַכֶּ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb “Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb kill them,”|תַכֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Would you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb kill|מַכֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb those|הַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have captured|שָׁבִ֛יתָ\rb* \rb with your own sword|בְּחַרְבְּךָ֥\rb* \rb or bow?|וּֽבְקַשְׁתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb Set|שִׂים֩\rb* \rb food|לֶ֨חֶם\rb* \rb and water|וָמַ֜יִם\rb* \rb before them,|לִפְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that they may eat|וְיֹֽאכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb and drink|וְיִשְׁתּ֔וּ\rb* \rb and then return|וְיֵלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their master.”|אֲדֹנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb So the king prepared a great|גְדוֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb feast|וַיִּכְרֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb for them,|כֵּרָ֣ה\rb* \rb and after they had finished eating|וַיֹּֽאכְלוּ֙\rb* \rb and drinking,|וַיִּשְׁתּ֔וּ\rb* \rb he sent them away,|וַֽיְשַׁלְּחֵ֔ם\rb* \rb and they returned|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their master.|אֲדֹֽנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb And the Aramean|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb raiders|גְּדוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb come|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb into the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb* \rb again.|יָ֤סְפוּ\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb*
\s1 The Siege and Famine of Samaria
\p \v 24 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Some time later,|אַחֲרֵי־\rb*\rb |כֵ֔ן\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֥ד\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb assembled|וַיִּקְבֹּ֛ץ\rb* \rb his entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|מַחֲנֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and marched up|וַיַּ֕עַל\rb* \rb to besiege|וַיָּ֖צַר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Samaria.|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb So there was|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb a great|גָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb famine|רָעָ֤ב\rb* \rb in Samaria.|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb Indeed,|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb they besieged|צָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb the city|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb so long that|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb a donkey’s|חֲמוֹר֙\rb* \rb head|רֹאשׁ־\rb* \rb sold|הֱי֤וֹת\rb* \rb for eighty shekels|בִּשְׁמֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb of silver,|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 6:25 \fqa \ref 80|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref* pounds or 907.2 grams of silver.\f* \rb and a quarter|וְרֹ֛בַע\rb* \rb cab|הַקַּ֥ב\rb* \rb of dove’s dung|חֲרֵייוֹנִים\rb*\f + \fr 6:25 \ft Or \fqa a quarter cab of seed pods\ft ; that is, \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.28 dry quarts or 0.31 liters\f* \rb sold for five shekels|בַּחֲמִשָּׁה־\rb* \rb of silver.|כָֽסֶף׃\rb*\f + \fr 6:25 \fqa 5 shekels\ft is \ref approximately 2|2\ref* ounces or 57 grams of silver.\f*
\p \v 26 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb As the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb was passing by|עֹבֵ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall,|הַחֹמָ֑ה\rb* \rb a woman|וְאִשָּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb cried out|צָעֲקָ֤ה\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָיו֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Help me,|הוֹשִׁ֖יעָה\rb* \rb my lord|אֲדֹנִ֥י\rb* \rb the king!”|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb He answered,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “If the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb does not|אַל־\rb* \rb help you,|יוֹשִׁעֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb where|מֵאַ֖יִן\rb* \rb can I find help for you?|אֽוֹשִׁיעֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb From|הֲמִן־\rb* \rb the threshing floor|הַגֹּ֖רֶן\rb* \rb or|א֥וֹ\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb* \rb the winepress?”|הַיָּֽקֶב׃\rb* \v 28 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּֽאמֶר־\rb* \rb her,|לָ֥הּ\rb* \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb is the matter?”|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \rb And she answered,|וַתֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “This|הַזֹּ֜את\rb* \rb woman|הָאִשָּׁ֨ה\rb* \rb said|אָמְרָ֣ה\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb ‘Give up|תְּנִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your son,|בְּנֵךְ֙\rb* \rb that we may eat him,|וְנֹאכְלֶ֣נּוּ\rb*\rb |הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָֽר׃\rb* \rb we will eat|נֹאכַ֥ל\rb* \rb my son.’|בְּנִ֖י\rb* \v 29 \rb So we boiled|וַנְּבַשֵּׁ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my son|בְּנִ֖י\rb* \rb and ate him,|וַנֹּֽאכְלֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and the next|הָאַחֵ֗ר\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I said|וָאֹמַ֨ר\rb* \rb to her,|אֵלֶ֜יהָ\rb* \rb ‘Give up|תְּנִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your son,|בְּנֵךְ֙\rb* \rb that we may eat him.’|וְנֹ֣אכְלֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb But she had hidden|וַתַּחְבִּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her son.”|בְּנָֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb When the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִשְׁמֹ֨עַ\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the woman,|הָֽאִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb he tore|וַיִּקְרַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes.|בְּגָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb And as he|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb passed by|עֹבֵ֣ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall,|הַחֹמָ֑ה\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֣רְא\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the sackcloth|הַשַּׂ֛ק\rb* \rb under his clothes|מִבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \rb next to|עַל־\rb* \rb his skin.|בְּשָׂר֖וֹ\rb* \v 31 \rb He announced,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “May God|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb punish|כֹּֽה־\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂה־\rb* \rb me,|לִּ֥י\rb* \rb and ever so|וְכֹ֣ה\rb* \rb severely,|יוֹסִ֑ף\rb* \rb if|אִֽם־\rb* \rb the head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֧ע\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphat|שָׁפָ֛ט\rb* \rb remains|יַעֲמֹ֞ד\rb* \rb on his shoulders|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb through this day!”|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb Now Elisha|וֶאֱלִישָׁע֙\rb* \rb was sitting|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in his house,|בְּבֵית֔וֹ\rb* \rb and the elders|וְהַזְּקֵנִ֖ים\rb* \rb were sitting|יֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb with him.|אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb The king sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb a messenger|אִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb ahead,|מִלְּפָנָ֗יו\rb* \rb but before|בְּטֶ֣רֶם\rb* \rb he|הַמַּלְאָ֨ךְ\rb* \rb arrived,|יָבֹא֩\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb Elisha|וְה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the elders,|הַזְּקֵנִ֗ים\rb* \rb “Do you see|הַרְּאִיתֶם֙\rb* \rb how|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb murderer|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |הַֽמְרַצֵּ֤חַ\rb* \rb has sent|שָׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb someone to cut off|לְהָסִ֣יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my head?|רֹאשִׁ֔י\rb* \rb Look,|רְא֣וּ׀\rb* \rb when the messenger|הַמַּלְאָ֗ךְ\rb* \rb comes,|כְּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb shut|סִגְר֤וּ\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb to keep him out.|וּלְחַצְתֶּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |בַּדֶּ֔לֶת\rb* \rb Is not|הֲל֗וֹא\rb* \rb the sound|ק֛וֹל\rb* \rb of his master’s|אֲדֹנָ֖יו\rb* \rb footsteps|רַגְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb behind him?”|אַחֲרָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb While Elisha was still|עוֹדֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb with them,|עִמָּ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb the messenger|הַמַּלְאָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb came down|יֹרֵ֣ד\rb* \rb to him.|אֵלָ֑יו\rb* \rb And the king said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*\rb |הִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb “This|זֹ֤את\rb* \rb calamity is|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb Why|מָֽה־\rb* \rb should I wait|אוֹחִ֥יל\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb any longer?”|עֽוֹד׃ס\rb*
\c 7
\s1 Elisha’s Prophecy of Plenty
\p \v 1 \rb Then Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD!|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb This is what|כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘About this time|כָּעֵ֤ת׀\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָר֙\rb* \rb at the gate|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Samaria,|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb a seah|סְאָֽה־\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֣לֶת\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa A seah\ft is \ref approximately 6|6\ref*.6 dry quarts or 7.3 liters (probably about 8.2 pounds or 3.7 kilograms of flour); here and in verses 16 and 18.\f* \rb will sell for a shekel,|בְּשֶׁ֗קֶל\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa A shekel\ft is \ref approximately 0|0\ref*.4 ounces or 11.4 grams, probably of silver; here and in verses 16 and 18.\f* \rb and two seahs|וְסָאתַ֧יִם\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִ֛ים\rb*\f + \fr 7:1 \fqa 2 seahs\ft is \ref approximately 13|13\ref*.2 dry quarts or 14.6 liters (probably about 19.3 pounds or 8.8 kilograms of barley); here and in verses 16 and 18.\f* \rb will sell for a shekel.’”|בְּשֶׁ֖קֶל\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb But the officer|הַשָּׁלִ֡ישׁ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb whose arm|יָד֜וֹ\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb leaned|נִשְׁעָ֨ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb answered|וַיַּ֣עַן\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִים֮\rb* \rb “Look,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb even if the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb were to make|עֹשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb windows|אֲרֻבּוֹת֙\rb* \rb in heaven,|בַּשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb could this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb really happen?”|הֲיִהְיֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֣ר\rb*
\p \rb “You will see it|רֹאֶה֙\rb* \rb with your own eyes,”|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb replied Elisha,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*\rb |הִנְּכָ֤ה\rb* \rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb “but you will not eat|תֹאכֵֽל׃ס\rb* \rb any of it.”|וּמִשָּׁ֖ם\rb*
\s1 The Arameans Flee
\p \v 3 \rb Now there were|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb four|וְאַרְבָּעָ֧ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb with leprosy|מְצֹרָעִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 7:3 \fqa Leprosy \ft was a term used for various skin diseases; here and in verse 8; see Leviticus 13.\f* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the city gate,|הַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb* \rb and they said|וַיֹּֽאמְרוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another,|רֵעֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “Why|מָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲנַ֛חְנוּ\rb* \rb just sit|יֹשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb here|פֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb we die?|מָֽתְנוּ׃\rb* \v 4 \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb we say,|אָמַרְנוּ֩\rb* \rb ‘Let us go into|נָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb the city,’|הָעִ֜יר\rb* \rb we will die|וָמַ֣תְנוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb from the famine|וְהָרָעָ֤ב\rb* \rb in the city;|בָּעִיר֙\rb* \rb but if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb we sit|יָשַׁ֥בְנוּ\rb* \rb here,|פֹ֖ה\rb* \rb we will also die.|וָמָ֑תְנוּ\rb* \rb So come|לְכוּ֙\rb* \rb now,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb let us go over|וְנִפְּלָה֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the Arameans.|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb If|אִם־\rb* \rb they let us live,|נִֽחְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb we will live;|יְחַיֻּ֣נוּ\rb* \rb if|וְאִם־\rb* \rb they kill us,|יְמִיתֻ֖נוּ\rb* \rb we will die.”|וָמָֽתְנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So they arose|וַיָּק֣וּמוּ\rb* \rb at twilight|בַנֶּ֔שֶׁף\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the Arameans.|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb But when they came|לָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the outskirts|קְצֵה֙\rb* \rb of the camp,|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb there was not|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb a man|אִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb to be found.|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \v 6 \rb For the Lord|וַאדֹנָ֞י\rb* \rb had caused the Arameans|אֲרָ֗ם\rb*\rb |מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb to hear|הִשְׁמִ֣יעַ׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of chariots,|רֶ֙כֶב֙\rb*\rb |ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb horses,|ס֔וּס\rb*\rb |ק֖וֹל\rb* \rb and a great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb army,|חַ֣יִל\rb* \rb so that they said|וַיֹּאמְר֞וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another,|אָחִ֗יו\rb* \rb “Look,|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb must have hired|שָֽׂכַר־\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the Hittites|הַחִתִּ֛ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb to attack|לָב֥וֹא\rb* \rb us.”|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Thus the Arameans had arisen|וַיָּקוּמוּ֮\rb* \rb and fled|וַיָּנ֣וּסוּ\rb* \rb at twilight,|בַנֶּשֶׁף֒\rb* \rb abandoning|וַיַּעַזְב֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their tents|אָהֳלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb horses|סֽוּסֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb donkeys.|חֲמֹ֣רֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb The camp was intact,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הִ֑יא\rb* \rb and they had run|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb their lives.|נַפְשָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb When the|הָאֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb lepers|הַֽמְצֹרָעִ֨ים\rb* \rb reached|וַיָּבֹאוּ֩\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb the edge|קְצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the camp,|הַֽמַּחֲנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb they went|וַיָּבֹ֜אוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb tent|אֹ֤הֶל\rb* \rb to eat|וַיֹּאכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb and drink.|וַיִּשְׁתּ֔וּ\rb* \rb Then they carried off|וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb* \rb the silver,|כֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb gold,|וְזָהָב֙\rb* \rb and clothing,|וּבְגָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb and hid them.|וַיַּטְמִ֑נוּ\rb* \rb On returning,|וַיָּשֻׁ֗בוּ\rb* \rb they entered|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb another|אַחֵ֔ר\rb* \rb tent,|אֹ֣הֶל\rb* \rb carried off some items|וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb from there,|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb*\rb |וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb and hid them.|וַיַּטְמִֽנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Finally, they said|וַיֹּאמְרוּ֩\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb another,|רֵעֵ֜הוּ\rb* \rb “We are|אֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb doing|עֹשִׂ֗ים\rb* \rb what is right.|כֵ֣ן׀\rb* \rb Today|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb is a day|יוֹם־\rb* \rb of good news.|בְּשֹׂרָ֣ה\rb*\rb |ה֔וּא\rb* \rb If we|וַאֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb are silent|מַחְשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb and wait|וְחִכִּ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning|הַבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb light,|א֥וֹר\rb* \rb our sin|עָו֑וֹן\rb* \rb will overtake us.|וּמְצָאָ֣נוּ\rb* \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb*\rb |לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb let us go|וְנָבֹ֔אָה\rb* \rb and tell|וְנַגִּ֖ידָה\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb household.”|בֵּ֥ית\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb So they went|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb and called out|וַֽיִּקְרְאוּ֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gatekeepers|שֹׁעֵ֣ר\rb* \rb of the city,|הָעִיר֒\rb* \rb saying,|וַיַּגִּ֤ידוּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “We went|בָּ֚אנוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Aramean|אֲרָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb and no|אֵֽין־\rb* \rb one was|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb there—|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb not a trace—|וְק֣וֹל\rb*\rb |אָדָ֑ם\rb*  \rb only|אִם־\rb* \rb tethered|אָסוּר֙\rb* \rb horses|הַסּ֤וּס\rb* \rb and donkeys,|וְהַחֲמ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |אָס֔וּר\rb* \rb and the tents|וְאֹהָלִ֖ים\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were intact.”|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb The gatekeepers|הַשֹּֽׁעֲרִ֑ים\rb* \rb shouted the news,|וַיִּקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb and it was reported|וַיַּגִּ֕ידוּ\rb* \rb to the king’s|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |פְּנִֽימָה׃\rb* \rb household.|בֵּ֥ית\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb got up|וַיָּ֨קָם\rb* \rb in the night|לַ֗יְלָה\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his servants,|עֲבָדָ֔יו\rb* \rb “Let me tell|אַגִּֽידָה־\rb*\rb |נָּ֣א\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb have done|עָ֥שׂוּ\rb* \rb to us.|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb They know|יָדְע֞וּ\rb* \rb we|אֲנַ֗חְנוּ\rb* \rb are starving,|רְעֵבִ֣ים\rb* \rb so they have left|וַיֵּצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb the camp|הַֽמַּחֲנֶה֙\rb* \rb to hide|לְהֵחָבֵ֤ה\rb* \rb in the field,|בְהַשָּׂדֶה\rb* \rb thinking,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘When|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they come out|יֵצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the city,|הָעִיר֙\rb* \rb we will take them|וְנִתְפְּשֵׂ֣ם\rb* \rb alive|חַיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and enter|נָבֹֽא׃\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the city.’”|הָעִ֖יר\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb But one|אֶחָ֨ד\rb* \rb of his servants|מֵעֲבָדָ֜יו\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb replied,|וַיַּעַן֩\rb* \rb “Please,|נָ֞א\rb* \rb have scouts take|וְיִקְחוּ־\rb* \rb five|חֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the horses|הַסּוּסִים֮\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb remain|הַֽנִּשְׁאָרִים֮\rb*\rb |נִשְׁאֲרוּ־\rb* \rb in the city.|בָהּ֒\rb* \rb Their plight|הִנָּ֗ם\rb* \rb will be no worse than all|כְּכָל־\rb*\rb |הֶהָמוֹן\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb are left|נִשְׁאֲרוּ־\rb* \rb here.|בָ֔הּ\rb* \rb You can see|הִנָּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כְּכָל־\rb*\rb |הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb all the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb here|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb are doomed.|תָּ֑מּוּ\rb* \rb So let us send them|וְנִשְׁלְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb and find out.”|וְנִרְאֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then the scouts took|וַיִּקְח֕וּ\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֖י\rb* \rb chariots|רֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb with horses,|סוּסִ֑ים\rb* \rb and the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb sent them|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֧י\rb* \rb the Aramean|אֲרָ֛ם\rb* \rb army,|מַחֲנֵֽה־\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb “Go|לְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb and see.”|וּרְאֽוּ׃\rb* \v 15 \rb And they tracked them|וַיֵּלְכ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as the Jordan,|הַיַּרְדֵּן֒\rb* \rb and indeed,|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the whole|כָל־\rb* \rb way|הַדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb was littered with|מְלֵאָ֤ה\rb* \rb the clothing|בְגָדִים֙\rb* \rb and equipment|וְכֵלִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb had thrown off|הִשְׁלִ֥יכוּ\rb* \rb in haste.|בְּהֵחָפְזָם\rb* \rb So the scouts|הַמַּלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגִּ֖דוּ\rb* \rb the king.|לַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*
\s1 Elisha’s Prophecy Fulfilled
\p \v 16 \rb Then the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb and plundered|וַיָּבֹ֕זּוּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the camp|מַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the Arameans.|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb It was then that|וַיְהִ֨י\rb* \rb a seah|סְאָה־\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֜לֶת\rb* \rb sold for a shekel,|בְּשֶׁ֗קֶל\rb* \rb and two seahs|וְסָאתַ֧יִם\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִ֛ים\rb* \rb sold for a shekel,|בְּשֶׁ֖קֶל\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Now the king|וְהַמֶּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb had appointed|הִפְקִ֨יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the officer|הַשָּׁלִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb arm|יָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb he leaned|נִשְׁעָ֤ן\rb* \rb to be in charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the gate,|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb but the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb trampled him|וַיִּרְמְסֻ֧הוּ\rb* \rb in the gateway,|בַּשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb and he died,|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had foretold|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb when the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb had come|בְּרֶ֥דֶת\rb* \rb to him.|אֵלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 18 \rb It happened|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb just as the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb had told|כְּדַבֵּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the king:|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “About this time|כָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb tomorrow|מָחָ֔ר\rb* \rb at the gate|בְּשַׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb of Samaria,|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb two seahs|סָאתַ֨יִם\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִ֜ים\rb* \rb will sell for a shekel,|בְּשֶׁ֗קֶל\rb* \rb and a seah|וּֽסְאָה־\rb* \rb of fine flour|סֹ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb will sell|יִהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb for a shekel.”|בְּשֶׁ֔קֶל\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And the officer|הַשָּׁלִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had answered|וַיַּ֨עַן\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִים֮\rb* \rb “Look,|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb even if the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb were to make|עֹשֶׂ֤ה\rb* \rb windows|אֲרֻבּוֹת֙\rb* \rb in heaven,|בַּשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb could this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb really happen?”|הֲיִהְיֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |כַּדָּבָ֣ר\rb*
\p \rb So Elisha had replied,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb |הִנְּךָ֤\rb* \rb “You will see it|רֹאֶה֙\rb* \rb with your own eyes,|בְּעֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb but you will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|תֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb any of it!”|וּמִשָּׁ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And that|כֵּ֑ן\rb* \rb is just what happened|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb to him.|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb The people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb trampled|וַיִּרְמְס֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֥וֹ\rb* \rb in the gateway,|בַּשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb and he died.|וַיָּמֹֽת׃ס\rb*
\c 8
\s1 The Shunammite’s Land Restored
\p \v 1 \rb Now Elisha|וֶאֱלִישָׁ֡ע\rb* \rb had said|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁה֩\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb son|בְּנָ֜הּ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb he had restored to life,|הֶחֱיָ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb “Arise,|ק֤וּמִי\rb* \rb you|אַתִּי\rb* \rb and your household;|וּבֵיתֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb go|וּלְכִי֙\rb* \rb and live as a foreigner|וְג֖וּרִי\rb* \rb wherever|בַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you can.|תָּג֑וּרִי\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has decreed that|קָרָ֤א\rb* \rb a seven-year|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb*\rb |שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb famine|לָֽרָעָ֔ב\rb*\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb will come|בָּ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land.”|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb So the woman|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb had proceeded|וַתָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb to do|וַתַּ֕עַשׂ\rb* \rb as the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וַתֵּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb had instructed.|כִּדְבַ֖ר\rb* \rb And she|הִיא֙\rb* \rb and her household|וּבֵיתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb lived as foreigners|וַתָּ֥גָר\rb* \rb for seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of the Philistines.|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb At the end|מִקְצֵה֙\rb* \rb of seven|שֶׁ֣בַע\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb when the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb returned|וַתָּ֥שָׁב\rb* \rb from the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Philistines,|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb* \rb she went|וַתֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb to appeal|לִצְעֹ֣ק\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb her house|בֵּיתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb her land.|שָׂדָֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Now the king|וְהַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb had been speaking|מְדַבֵּר֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gehazi,|גֵּ֣חֲזִ֔י\rb* \rb the servant|נַ֥עַר\rb* \rb of the man|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb “Please|נָּ֣א\rb* \rb relate|סַפְּרָה־\rb* \rb to me|לִ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the great things|הַגְּדֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb* \rb has done.”|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And|וַ֠יְהִי\rb* \rb Gehazi|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb was telling|מְסַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb the king|לַמֶּלֶךְ֮\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Elisha had brought the dead|הַמֵּת֒\rb* \rb back to life.|הֶחֱיָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Just then|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb the woman|הָאִשָּׁ֜ה\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb son|בְּנָהּ֙\rb* \rb Elisha had revived|הֶחֱיָ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb came to appeal|צֹעֶ֣קֶת\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb her house|בֵּיתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and|וְעַל־\rb* \rb her land.|שָׂדָ֑הּ\rb* \rb So Gehazi|גֵּֽחֲזִי֙\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “My lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb the king,|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb this|זֹ֚את\rb* \rb is the woman,|הָֽאִשָּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and this|וְזֶה־\rb* \rb is the son|בְּנָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָֽׁע׃\rb* \rb restored to life.”|הֶחֱיָ֥ה\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb When the king|הַמֶּ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb asked|וַיִּשְׁאַ֥ל\rb* \rb the woman,|לָאִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb she confirmed it.|וַתְּסַפֶּר־\rb*\rb |ל֑וֹ\rb* \rb So the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb appointed|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb for her|לָ֣הּ\rb* \rb an|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb officer,|סָרִ֨יס\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “Restore|הָשֵׁ֤יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that was|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb hers,|לָהּ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb along with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the proceeds|תְּבוּאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb from the day|מִיּ֛וֹם\rb* \rb that she left|עָזְבָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the country|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb now.”|עָֽתָּה׃פ\rb*
\s1 Hazael Murders Ben-hadad
\p \v 7 \rb Then Elisha|אֱלִישָׁע֙\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb to Damascus|דַּמֶּ֔שֶׂק\rb*\rb |וּבֶן־\rb* \rb while Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֥ד\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb was sick,|חֹלֶ֑ה\rb* \rb and the king was told,|וַיֻּגַּד־\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “The man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֛א\rb* \rb here.”|הֵֽנָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb So the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hazael,|חֲזָהאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֤ח\rb* \rb a gift|מִנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb in your hand,|בְּיָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb go|וְלֵ֕ךְ\rb* \rb to meet|לִקְרַ֖את\rb* \rb the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God,|הָאֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb* \rb and inquire|וְדָרַשְׁתָּ֨\rb* \rb of|אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb through him,|מֵֽאוֹתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Will I recover|הַאֶחְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from this|זֶֽה׃\rb* \rb illness?’”|מֵחֳלִ֥י\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So Hazael|חֲזָאֵל֮\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to meet Elisha,|לִקְרָאתוֹ֒\rb* \rb taking|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb with him|בְיָדוֹ֙\rb* \rb a gift|מִנְחָ֤ה\rb* \rb of forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb camel loads|מַשָּׂ֖א\rb*\rb |גָּמָ֑ל\rb* \rb of every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb good thing|ט֣וּב\rb* \rb from Damascus.|דַּמֶּ֔שֶׂק\rb* \rb And he went in|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֔יו\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Your son|בִּנְךָ֨\rb*\rb |בֶן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֤ד\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָם֙\rb* \rb has sent me|שְׁלָחַ֤נִי\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb to ask,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Will I recover|הַאֶחְיֶ֖ה\rb* \rb from this|זֶֽה׃\rb* \rb illness?’”|מֵחֳלִ֥י\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb answered,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb “Go|לֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and tell him,|אֱמָר־\rb*\rb |לֹא\rb* \rb ‘You will surely recover.’|חָיֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |תִחְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 8:10 \ft Or \fqa “Go and say, ‘You will surely not recover.’ And the LORD\f* \rb has shown me|וְהִרְאַ֥נִי\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb in fact he will die.”|מ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |יָמֽוּת׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb Elisha fixed|וַיַּעֲמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb his gaze|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb steadily|וַיָּ֣שֶׂם\rb* \rb on him until|עַד־\rb* \rb Hazael became uncomfortable.|בֹּ֑שׁ\rb* \rb Then the man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb* \rb began to weep.|וַיֵּ֖בְךְּ\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb “Why|מַדּ֖וּעַ\rb* \rb is my lord|אֲדֹנִ֣י\rb* \rb weeping?”|בֹכֶ֑ה\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Hazael.|חֲזָאֵ֔ל\rb*
\p \rb “Because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I know|יָדַ֡עְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the evil|רָעָ֗ה\rb* \rb you will do|תַּעֲשֶׂה֩\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb to the Israelites,”|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb Elisha replied.|וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb* \rb “You will set|תְּשַׁלַּ֤ח\rb* \rb fire|בָּאֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb to their fortresses,|מִבְצְרֵיהֶ֞ם\rb* \rb kill|תַּהֲרֹ֔ג\rb* \rb their young men|וּבַחֻֽרֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb with the sword,|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb dash their little ones|וְעֹלְלֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb to pieces,|תְּרַטֵּ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and rip open|תְּבַקֵּֽעַ׃\rb* \rb their pregnant women.”|וְהָרֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb “But|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb how could|מָ֤ה\rb* \rb your servant,|עַבְדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb a mere dog,|הַכֶּ֔לֶב\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb do|יַעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb such|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb a monstrous|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb thing?”|הַדָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Hazael.|חֲזָהאֵ֔ל\rb*
\p \rb And Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb answered,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “The LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb has shown me|הִרְאַ֧נִי\rb* \rb that you will be|אֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Aram.”|אֲרָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb So Hazael left|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ׀\rb* \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֗ע\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his master,|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb who asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb him,|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb “What|מָֽה־\rb* \rb did Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֑ע\rb* \rb say|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb to you?”|לְךָ֖\rb*
\p \rb And he replied,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “He told me|אָ֥מַר\rb* \rb that|לִ֖י\rb* \rb you would surely recover.”|חָיֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |תִחְיֶֽה׃\rb* \v 15 \rb But|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb the next day|מִֽמָּחֳרָ֗ת\rb* \rb Hazael took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb a thick cloth,|הַמַּכְבֵּר֙\rb* \rb dipped|וַיִּטְבֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb it in water,|בַּמַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb and spread|וַיִּפְרֹ֥שׂ\rb* \rb it over|עַל־\rb* \rb the king’s face.|פָּנָ֖יו\rb*
\p \rb So Ben-hadad died,|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb* \rb and Hazael|חֲזָהאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 Jehoram Reigns in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 21:1–7|2CH 21:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 16 \rb In the fifth|חָמֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Joram|לְיוֹרָ֤ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb over Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֥ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb* \rb succeeded his father|מָלַ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |וִיהוֹשָׁפָ֖ט\rb*\rb |מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb as king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb Jehoram was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb thirty-two|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֛יִם\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \rb eight|וּשְׁמֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָה\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb And Jehoram walked|וַיֵּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדֶ֣רֶךְ׀\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb had done.|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb he married|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb a daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb*\rb |הָֽיְתָה־\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Yet for the sake|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb of His servant|עַבְדּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb David,|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was unwilling|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אָבָ֤ה\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַשְׁחִ֣ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Judah,|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb since|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He had promised|אָֽמַר־\rb* \rb to maintain|לָתֵ֨ת\rb* \rb a lamp|נִ֛יר\rb* \rb for David|ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb and his descendants|לְבָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb forever.|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb*
\s1 Edom and Libnah Rebel
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 21:8–11|2CH 21:8-11\ref*)
\p \v 20 \rb In the days of Jehoram,|בְּיָמָיו֙\rb*\f + \fr 8:20 \ft Literally \fqa In his days\f* \rb Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb rebelled|פָּשַׁ֣ע\rb* \rb against|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb and appointed|וַיַּמְלִ֥כוּ\rb* \rb their own|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb king.|מֶֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \v 21 \rb So Jehoram|יוֹרָם֙\rb*\f + \fr 8:21 \ft Hebrew \fqa Joram\ft , a variant of \fqa Jehoram \ft (the son of Jehoshaphat), as in verse 16; also in verses 23 and 24\f* \rb crossed over|וַיַּעֲבֹ֤ר\rb* \rb to Zair|צָעִ֔ירָה\rb* \rb with|עִמּ֑וֹ\rb*\rb |וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his chariots.|הָרֶ֖כֶב\rb* \rb When the Edomites|אֱד֜וֹם\rb* \rb surrounded|הַסֹּבֵ֤יב\rb* \rb him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb his chariot|הָרֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb commanders,|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb he|ה֞וּא\rb* \rb rose up|קָ֣ם\rb* \rb and attacked|וַיַּכֶּ֨ה\rb* \rb by night.|לַ֗יְלָה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His troops, however,|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּ֥נָס\rb* \rb to their homes.|לְאֹהָלָֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb So to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb Edom|אֱד֗וֹם\rb* \rb has been in rebellion|וַיִּפְשַׁ֣ע\rb* \rb against|מִתַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb the hand of|יַד־\rb* \rb Judah.|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb Likewise,|אָ֛ז\rb* \rb Libnah|לִבְנָ֖ה\rb* \rb rebelled|תִּפְשַׁ֥ע\rb* \rb at the same|הַהִֽיא׃\rb* \rb time.|בָּעֵ֥ת\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jehoram,|יוֹרָ֖ם\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments,|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb* \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And Jehoram|יוֹרָם֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb them|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David.|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb And his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 Ahaziah Reigns in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 22:1–7|2CH 22:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 25 \rb In the twelfth|שְׁתֵּים־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Joram|לְיוֹרָ֥ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb over Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֖ם\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 26 \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb year.|וְשָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּוֹ֙\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb was Athaliah,|עֲתַלְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb the granddaughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Omri|עָמְרִ֖י\rb* \rb king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb And Ahaziah walked|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדֶ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb and did|וַיַּ֧עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb like the house|כְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab,|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb he|הֽוּא׃\rb* \rb was a son-in-law|חֲתַ֥ן\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Ahab.|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Then Ahaziah went|וַיֵּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Joram|יוֹרָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֗ב\rb* \rb to fight|לַמִּלְחָמָ֛ה\rb* \rb against|עִם־\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָהאֵ֥ל\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb at Ramoth-gilead,|בְּרָמֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֑ד\rb* \rb and the Arameans|אֲרַמִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wounded|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb Joram.|יוֹרָֽם׃\rb* \v 29 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb Joram|יוֹרָ֨ם\rb* \rb returned|וַיָּשָׁב֩\rb* \rb to Jezreel|בְיִזְרְעֶ֗אל\rb* \rb to recover|לְהִתְרַפֵּ֣א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the wounds|הַמַּכִּים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרַמִּים֙\rb* \rb had inflicted on him|יַכֻּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb at Ramah|בָּֽרָמָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 8:29 \fqa Ramah \ft is a variant of \fqa Ramoth\ft ; see verse 28.\f* \rb when he fought|בְּהִלָּ֣חֲמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָהאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram.|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb Then Ahaziah|וַאֲחַזְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoram|יְהוֹרָ֜ם\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb went down|יָרַ֡ד\rb* \rb to Jezreel|בְּיִזְרְעֶ֖אל\rb* \rb to visit|לִרְא֞וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joram|יוֹרָ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab,|אַחְאָ֛ב\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Joram|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb had been wounded.|חֹלֶ֥ה\rb*
\c 9
\s1 Jehu Anointed King of Israel
\p \v 1 \rb Now Elisha|וֶאֱלִישָׁע֙\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb summoned|קָרָ֕א\rb* \rb one|לְאַחַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the sons|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֑ים\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to him,|ל֜וֹ\rb* \rb “Tuck your cloak|חֲגֹ֣ר\rb* \rb under your belt,|מָתְנֶ֗יךָ\rb*\f + \fr 9:1 \ft Literally \fqa Gird up your loins\f* \rb take|וְ֠קַח\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb flask|פַּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of oil,|הַשֶּׁ֤מֶן\rb*\rb |בְּיָדֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb and go|וְלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to Ramoth-gilead.|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָֽד׃\rb* \v 2 \rb When you arrive,|וּבָ֖אתָ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑מָּה\rb* \rb look|וּרְאֵֽה־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֠ם\rb* \rb for Jehu|יֵה֨וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat,|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֜ט\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nimshi.|נִמְשִׁ֗י\rb* \rb Go in,|וּבָ֙אתָ֙\rb* \rb get him away|וַהֲקֵֽמֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb from|מִתּ֣וֹך\rb* \rb his companions,|אֶחָ֔יו\rb* \rb and take|וְהֵבֵיאתָ֥\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb to an inner room.|חֶ֥דֶר\rb*\rb |בְּחָֽדֶר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Then take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֤\rb* \rb the flask|פַךְ־\rb* \rb of oil,|הַשֶּׁ֙מֶן֙\rb* \rb pour|וְיָצַקְתָּ֣\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb his head,|רֹאשׁ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and declare,|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb ‘This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb I anoint|מְשַׁחְתִּ֥יךָֽ\rb* \rb you king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb Israel.’|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Then open|וּפָתַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֛לֶת\rb* \rb and run.|וְנַ֖סְתָּה\rb* \rb Do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb delay!”|תְחַכֶּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb So the young|הַנַּ֛עַר\rb*\rb |הַנַּ֥עַר\rb* \rb prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Ramoth-gilead,|רָמֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָֽד׃\rb* \v 5 \rb and when he arrived,|וַיָּבֹ֗א\rb* \rb the army|הַחַ֙יִל֙\rb* \rb commanders|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb were sitting|יֹֽשְׁבִ֔ים\rb* \rb there.|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb “I have a message|דָּבָ֥ר\rb* \rb for you,|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb commander,”|הַשָּׂ֑ר\rb* \rb he said.|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb “For|אֶל־\rb* \rb which|מִ֣י\rb* \rb of us?”|מִכֻּלָּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Jehu.|יֵהוּא֙\rb*
\p \rb “For you,|אֵלֶ֥יךָ\rb* \rb commander,”|הַשָּֽׂר׃\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb So Jehu got up|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb and went|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb into the house,|הַבַּ֔יְתָה\rb* \rb where the young prophet poured|וַיִּצֹ֥ק\rb* \rb the oil|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb his head|רֹאשׁ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and declared,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘I anoint you|מְשַׁחְתִּ֧יךָֽ\rb* \rb king|לְמֶ֛לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 7 \rb And you are to strike down|וְהִ֨כִּיתָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of your master|אֲדֹנֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb Ahab,|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb so that I may avenge|וְנִקַּמְתִּ֞י\rb* \rb the blood|דְּמֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb of My servants|עֲבָדַ֣י\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֗ים\rb* \rb and the blood|וּדְמֵ֛י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb shed by the hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb of Jezebel.|אִיזָֽבֶל׃\rb* \v 8 \rb The whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb will perish,|וְאָבַ֖ד\rb* \rb and I will cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb from Ahab|לְאַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb every male,|מַשְׁתִּ֣ין\rb*\f + \fr 9:8 \ft Literally \fqa (all) those who urinate against a wall\f* \rb |בְּקִ֔יר\rb*\rb both slave|וְעָצ֥וּר\rb* \rb and free,|וְעָז֖וּב\rb* \rb in Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 9 \rb I will make|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֔ב\rb* \rb like the houses|כְּבֵ֖ית\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֑ט\rb* \rb and|וּכְבֵ֖ית\rb* \rb Baasha|בַּעְשָׁ֥א\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahijah.|אֲחִיָּֽה׃\rb* \v 10 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb on the plot of ground|בְּחֵ֥לֶק\rb* \rb at Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶ֖אל\rb* \rb the dogs|הַכְּלָבִ֛ים\rb* \rb will devour|יֹאכְל֧וּ\rb* \rb Jezebel,|אִיזֶ֜בֶל\rb* \rb and there will be no one|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb to bury her.’”|קֹבֵ֑ר\rb*
\p \rb Then the young prophet opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֥ח\rb* \rb the door|הַדֶּ֖לֶת\rb* \rb and ran.|וַיָּנֹֽס׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb When Jehu|וְיֵה֗וּא\rb* \rb went out|יָצָא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his master,|אֲדֹנָ֔יו\rb* \rb they asked,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “Is everything all right?|הֲשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb Why|מַדּ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb did this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb madman|הַמְשֻׁגָּ֥ע\rb* \rb come|בָּֽא־\rb* \rb to you?”|אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb “You|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his kind|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their babble,”|שִׂיחֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb he replied.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb “That is a lie!”|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb* \rb they said.|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb “Tell|הַגֶּד־\rb* \rb us|לָ֑נוּ\rb* \rb now!”|נָ֖א\rb*
\p \rb So Jehu answered,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “He talked|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb about this|כָּזֹ֤את\rb* \rb and that,|וְכָזֹאת֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb I anoint|מְשַׁחְתִּ֥יךָֽ\rb* \rb you king|לְמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb Israel.’”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Quickly,|וַֽיְמַהֲר֗וּ\rb* \rb each man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb his garment|בִּגְד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and put it|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb under Jehu|תַחְתָּ֖יו\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the bare|גֶּ֣רֶם\rb* \rb steps.|הַֽמַּעֲל֑וֹת\rb* \rb Then they blew|וַֽיִּתְקְעוּ֙\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֔ר\rb* \rb and proclaimed,|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb “Jehu|יֵהֽוּא׃\rb* \rb is king!”|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb*
\s1 Jehu Kills Joram and Ahaziah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 22:8–9|2CH 22:8-9\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb Thus Jehu|יֵה֛וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoshaphat,|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֥ט\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nimshi,|נִמְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb conspired|וַיִּתְקַשֵּׁ֗ר\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Joram.|יוֹרָ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb (Now Joram|וְיוֹרָם֩\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had been|הָיָ֨ה\rb*\rb |ה֚וּא\rb* \rb defending|שֹׁמֵ֜ר\rb* \rb Ramoth-gilead|בְּרָמֹ֣ת\rb*\rb |גִּלְעָ֗ד\rb* \rb against|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram,|אֲרָֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb but King|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָ֨ם\rb*\f + \fr 9:15 \ft Or \fqa Jehoram\ft , a variant of \fqa Joram\ft ; also in verses 17, 21, 22, 23, and 24\f* \rb had returned|וַיָּשָׁב֩\rb* \rb to Jezreel|בִיְזְרְעֶ֗אל\rb* \rb to recover|לְהִתְרַפֵּ֣א\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the wounds|הַמַּכִּים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had suffered|יַכֻּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb at the hands of the Arameans|אֲרַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb in the battle|בְּהִלָּ֣חֲמ֔וֹ\rb* \rb against|אֶת־\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb their king.)|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲרָ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb So Jehu|יֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb*\rb |יֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb you commanders wish to make me king,|נַפְשְׁכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb then do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let anyone|יֵצֵ֤א\rb* \rb escape|פָלִיט֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb to go|לָלֶ֖כֶת\rb* \rb and tell it|לַגִּיד\rb* \rb in Jezreel.”|בְּיִזְרְעֶֽאל׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Then Jehu|יֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb got into his chariot|וַיִּרְכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb to Jezreel,|יִזְרְעֶ֔אלָה\rb* \rb because|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Joram|יוֹרָ֖ם\rb* \rb was laid up|שֹׁכֵ֣ב\rb* \rb there.|שָׁ֑מָּה\rb* \rb And Ahaziah|וַֽאֲחַזְיָה֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb had gone down|יָרַ֖ד\rb* \rb to see|לִרְא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him.|יוֹרָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Now the watchman|וְהַצֹּפֶה֩\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֨ד\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the tower|הַמִּגְדָּ֜ל\rb* \rb in Jezreel|בְּיִזְרְעֶ֗אל\rb* \rb saw|וַיַּ֞רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jehu’s|יֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb troops|שִׁפְעַ֤ת\rb* \rb approaching,|בְּבֹא֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he called out,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֑ה\rb* \rb a company of troops!”|שִׁפְעַ֖ת\rb*
\p \rb “Choose|קַ֥ח\rb* \rb a rider,”|רַכָּ֛ב\rb* \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָ֗ם\rb* \rb commanded.|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Send him out|וּֽשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb to meet them|לִקְרָאתָ֖ם\rb* \rb and ask,|וְיֹאמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Have you come in peace?’”|הֲשָׁלֽוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb So a horseman|רֹכֵ֨ב\rb*\rb |הַסּ֜וּס\rb* \rb rode off|וַיֵּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb to meet Jehu|לִקְרָאת֗וֹ\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb asks:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Have you come in peace?’”|הֲשָׁל֔וֹם\rb*
\p \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb do you|לְּךָ֥\rb* \rb know about peace?”|וּלְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֛וּא\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb “Fall in|סֹ֣ב\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb behind me.”|אַחֲרָ֑י\rb*
\p \rb And the watchman|הַצֹּפֶה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb reported,|וַיַּגֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb “The messenger|הַמַּלְאָ֥ךְ\rb* \rb reached|בָּֽא־\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb them,|הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb but he is not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb coming back.”|שָֽׁב׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb So the king sent out|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb* \rb a second|שֵׁנִי֒\rb* \rb horseman,|רֹכֵ֣ב\rb*\rb |סוּס֮\rb* \rb who went|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb asks:|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Have you come in peace?’”|שָׁל֑וֹם\rb*
\p \rb “What|מַה־\rb* \rb do you|לְּךָ֥\rb* \rb know about peace?”|וּלְשָׁל֖וֹם\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֛וּא\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֧אמֶר\rb* \rb “Fall in|סֹ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb behind me.”|אַחֲרָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Again the watchman|הַצֹּפֶה֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb reported,|וַיַּגֵּ֤ד\rb* \rb “He reached|בָּ֥א\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but he is not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb coming back.|שָׁ֑ב\rb* \rb And the charioteer|וְהַמִּנְהָ֗ג\rb* \rb is driving like|כְּמִנְהַג֙\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֣וּא\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Nimshi|נִמְשִׁ֔י\rb*\f + \fr 9:20 \ft Or \fqa grandson of Nimshi\ft ; see verse 14.\f*—\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb he is driving|יִנְהָֽג׃\rb* \rb like a madman!”|בְשִׁגָּע֖וֹן\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb “Harness!”|אֱסֹ֔ר\rb* \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָם֙\rb* \rb shouted,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb and they harnessed|וַיֶּאְסֹ֖ר\rb* \rb his chariot.|רִכְבּ֑וֹ\rb*
\p \rb Then Joram|יְהוֹרָ֣ם\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb and Ahaziah|וַאֲחַזְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb set out,|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb in his own chariot,|בְּרִכְבּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and met|וַיֵּֽצְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |לִקְרַ֣את\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵה֔וּא\rb*\rb |וַיִּמְצָאֻ֔הוּ\rb* \rb on the property|בְּחֶלְקַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָב֥וֹת\rb* \rb the Jezreelite.|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb |וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb When Joram|יְהוֹרָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|כִּרְא֤וֹת\rb* \rb Jehu,|יֵה֔וּא\rb* \rb he asked,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Have you come in peace,|הֲשָׁל֣וֹם\rb* \rb Jehu?”|יֵה֑וּא\rb*
\p \rb “How|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb can there be|עַד־\rb* \rb peace,”|הַשָּׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb he replied,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “as long as|הָרַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb the idolatry|זְנוּנֵ֞י\rb*\f + \fr 9:22 \ft Hebrew \fqa adultery \ft or \fqa prostitution\ft , here a metaphor for idolatry\f* \rb and witchcraft|וּכְשָׁפֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb of your mother|אִמְּךָ֛\rb* \rb Jezebel abound?”|אִיזֶ֧בֶל\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָ֛ם\rb*\rb |יָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb turned around|וַיַּהֲפֹ֧ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 9:23 \ft Literally \fqa turned his hands\f* \rb and fled,|וַיָּנֹ֑ס\rb* \rb calling out|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ahaziah,|אֲחַזְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb “Treachery,|מִרְמָ֥ה\rb* \rb Ahaziah!”|אֲחַזְיָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Then Jehu|וְיֵה֞וּא\rb* \rb drew|מִלֵּ֧א\rb*\rb |יָד֣וֹ\rb* \rb his bow|בַקֶּ֗שֶׁת\rb* \rb and shot|וַיַּ֤ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Joram|יְהוֹרָם֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the shoulders.|זְרֹעָ֔יו\rb* \rb The arrow|הַחֵ֖צִי\rb* \rb pierced|וַיֵּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb his heart,|מִלִּבּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and he slumped down|וַיִּכְרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in his chariot.|בְּרִכְבּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb And Jehu said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Bidkar|בִּדְקַר֙\rb* \rb his officer,|שְׁלֹשָׁה\rb* \rb “Pick him up|שָׂ֚א\rb* \rb and throw him|הַשְׁלִכֵ֔הוּ\rb*\rb |בְּחֶלְקַ֕ת\rb* \rb into the field|שְׂדֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָב֣וֹת\rb* \rb the Jezreelite.|הַיִּזְרְעֵאלִ֑י\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb remember that|זְכֹ֞ר\rb* \rb when you|וָאַ֗תָּה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb were riding|רֹכְבִ֤ים\rb* \rb together|צְמָדִים֙\rb* \rb behind|אַֽחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Ahab,|אַחְאָ֣ב\rb* \rb the LORD|וַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb lifted up|נָשָׂ֣א\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb burden|הַמַּשָּׂ֖א\rb* \rb against him:|עָלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 26 \rb ‘As surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֡א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as I saw|רָאִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb the blood|דְּמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Naboth|נָבוֹת֩\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the blood|דְּמֵ֨י\rb* \rb of his sons|בָנָ֜יו\rb* \rb yesterday,|אֶ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb so will I repay|וְשִׁלַּמְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֛\rb* \rb on this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb plot of ground,|בַּחֶלְקָ֥ה\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.’|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb Now then,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb pick him up|שָׂ֧א\rb* \rb and throw him|הַשְׁלִכֵ֛הוּ\rb* \rb on the plot of ground.”|בַּחֶלְקָ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb When King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Ahaziah|וַאֲחַזְיָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb saw this,|רָאָ֔ה\rb* \rb he fled|וַיָּ֕נָס\rb* \rb up the road|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb toward Beth-haggan.|הַגָּ֑ן\rb*
\p \rb And Jehu|יֵה֗וּא\rb* \rb pursued him,|וַיִּרְדֹּ֨ף\rb*\rb |אַחֲרָ֜יו\rb* \rb shouting,|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb “Shoot|הַכֻּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֞וֹ\rb* \rb too!”|גַּם־\rb*
\p \rb So they shot Ahaziah in|אֶל־\rb* \rb his chariot|הַמֶּרְכָּבָ֗ה\rb* \rb on the Ascent|בְּמַֽעֲלֵה־\rb* \rb of Gur,|גוּר֙\rb*\f + \fr 9:27 \ft See Syriac, Vulgate, and LXX; Hebrew \fqa “Shoot him, too, in his chariot!” (They did this) on the Ascent of Gur,\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb near Ibleam,|יִבְלְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and he fled|וַיָּ֥נָס\rb* \rb to Megiddo|מְגִדּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and died|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb* \rb there.|שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 28 \rb Then his servants|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb carried him by chariot|וַיַּרְכִּ֧בוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלְָ֑מָה\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֨וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֧וֹ\rb* \rb with his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb in his tomb|בִקְבֻרָת֛וֹ\rb*\rb |עִם־\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David.|דָּוִֽד׃פ\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb (In the eleventh|אַחַ֣ת\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|וּבִשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Joram|לְיוֹרָ֖ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahab,|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb had become king|מָלַ֥ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah.)|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\s1 Jezebel’s Violent Death
\p \v 30 \rb Now when Jehu|יֵה֖וּא\rb* \rb arrived|וַיָּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb in Jezreel,|יִזְרְעֶ֑אלָה\rb* \rb Jezebel|וְאִיזֶ֣בֶל\rb* \rb heard of it.|שָׁמְעָ֗ה\rb* \rb So she painted|וַתָּ֨שֶׂם\rb*\rb |בַּפּ֤וּךְ\rb* \rb her eyes,|עֵינֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb adorned|וַתֵּ֣יטֶב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her head,|רֹאשָׁ֔הּ\rb* \rb and looked down|וַתַּשְׁקֵ֖ף\rb* \rb from|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb a window.|הַחַלּֽוֹן׃\rb* \v 31 \rb And as Jehu|וְיֵה֖וּא\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb the gate,|בַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb* \rb she asked,|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Have you come in peace,|הֲשָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb O Zimri,|זִמְרִ֖י\rb* \rb murderer|הֹרֵ֥ג\rb* \rb of your master?”|אֲדֹנָֽיו׃\rb*\f + \fr 9:31 \ft Or \fqa “Is there peace for Zimri, the murderer of his master?”\ft \ref See 1|1\ref* Kings 16:10.\f*
\p \v 32 \rb He looked up|וַיִּשָּׂ֤א\rb*\rb |פָנָיו֙\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the window|הַ֣חַלּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb and called out,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֥י\rb* \rb is on my side?|אִתִּ֖י\rb* \rb Who?”|מִ֑י\rb*
\p \rb And two|שְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb or three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb eunuchs|סָרִיסִֽים׃\rb* \rb looked down|וַיַּשְׁקִ֣יפוּ\rb* \rb at him.|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb “Throw her down!”|שִׁמְטֻהוּ\rb* \rb yelled Jehu.|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb So they threw her down,|וַֽיִּשְׁמְט֑וּהָ\rb* \rb and her blood|מִדָּמָ֧הּ\rb* \rb splattered|וַיִּ֨ז\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wall|הַקִּ֛יר\rb* \rb and on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the horses|הַסּוּסִ֖ים\rb* \rb as they trampled her underfoot.|וַֽיִּרְמְסֶֽנָּה׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb Then Jehu went in|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb and ate|וַיֹּ֣אכַל\rb* \rb and drank.|וַיֵּ֑שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb “Take care of|פִּקְדוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֞א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb cursed woman,”|הָאֲרוּרָ֤ה\rb* \rb he said,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “and bury her,|וְקִבְר֔וּהָ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb she was|הִֽיא׃\rb* \rb the daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of a king.”|מֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb But when they went out|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to bury her,|לְקָבְרָ֑הּ\rb* \rb they found|מָ֣צְאוּ\rb* \rb nothing|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb but|כִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb her|בָ֗הּ\rb* \rb skull,|הַגֻּלְגֹּ֛לֶת\rb* \rb her feet,|וְהָרַגְלַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and the palms|וְכַפּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of her hands.|הַיָּדָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb So they went back|וַיָּשֻׁבוּ֮\rb* \rb and told|וַיַּגִּ֣ידוּ\rb* \rb Jehu,|לוֹ֒\rb* \rb who replied,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “This|ה֔וּא\rb* \rb is the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He spoke|דִּבֶּ֗ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb Elijah|אֵלִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the Tishbite:|הַתִּשְׁבִּ֖י\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ‘On the plot of ground|בְּחֵ֣לֶק\rb* \rb at Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶ֔אל\rb* \rb the dogs|הַכְּלָבִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will devour|יֹאכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of Jezebel.|אִיזָֽבֶל׃\rb* \v 37 \rb And Jezebel’s|אִיזֶ֗בֶל\rb* \rb body|נִבְלַ֣ת\rb* \rb will lie|וְהָיָת\rb* \rb like dung|כְּדֹ֛מֶן\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb in the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb on the plot of ground|בְּחֵ֣לֶק\rb* \rb at Jezreel,|יִזְרְעֶ֑אל\rb* \rb so that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb no one|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb can say:|יֹאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is Jezebel.’|אִיזָֽבֶל׃פ\rb*\f + \fr 9:37 \ft See verse 10 and 1 Kings 21:23.\f*”
\c 10
\s1 Ahab’s Seventy Sons Killed
\p \v 1 \rb Now Ahab|וּלְאַחְאָ֛ב\rb* \rb had seventy|שִׁבְעִ֥ים\rb* \rb sons|בָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb in Samaria.|בְּשֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb So Jehu|יֵה֨וּא\rb* \rb wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּב֩\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִ֜ים\rb* \rb and sent them|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb to Samaria|שֹׁמְר֗וֹן\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the officials|שָׂרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Jezreel,|יִזְרְעֶאל֙\rb*\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate \fqa officials of the city \f* \rb to the elders,|הַזְּקֵנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the guardians of the sons|הָאֹמְנִ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 10:1 \ft Hebrew does not include \fqa of the sons\ft .\f* \rb of Ahab,|אַחְאָ֖ב\rb* \rb saying:|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 2 \rb “When this|הַזֶּה֙\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb letter|הַסֵּ֤פֶר\rb* \rb arrives,|כְּבֹ֨א\rb* \rb since|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb your master’s|אֲדֹנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb are with you|וְאִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and you have|וְאִתְּכֶם֙\rb* \rb chariots|הָרֶ֣כֶב\rb* \rb and horses,|וְהַסּוּסִ֔ים\rb* \rb a fortified|מִבְצָ֖ר\rb* \rb city|וְעִ֥יר\rb* \rb and weaponry,|וְהַנָּֽשֶׁק׃\rb* \v 3 \rb select|וּרְאִיתֶ֞ם\rb* \rb the best|הַטּ֤וֹב\rb* \rb and most worthy|וְהַיָּשָׁר֙\rb* \rb son|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your master,|אֲדֹנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb set him|וְשַׂמְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb his father’s|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb throne,|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb and fight|וְהִֽלָּחֲמ֖וּ\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb your master’s|אֲדֹנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb house.”|בֵּ֥ית\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb But they were terrified|וַיִּֽרְאוּ֙\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb and reasoned,|וַיֹּ֣אמְר֔וּ\rb* \rb “If|הִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb two|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb kings|הַמְּלָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb stand|עָמְד֖וּ\rb* \rb against him,|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb* \rb how|וְאֵ֖יךְ\rb*\rb |נַעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb can we?”|אֲנָֽחְנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So the palace|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb* \rb administrator,|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the overseer|וַאֲשֶׁ֪ר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb of the city,|הָעִ֟יר\rb* \rb the elders,|וְהַזְּקֵנִים֩\rb* \rb and the guardians|וְהָאֹמְנִ֨ים\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb a message to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehu:|יֵה֤וּא׀\rb* \rb “We|אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb* \rb are your servants,|עֲבָדֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb and we will do|נַעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb whatever|וְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you say.|תֹּאמַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֵלֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb We will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb make anyone|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb king.|נַמְלִ֣יךְ\rb* \rb Do|עֲשֵֽׂה׃\rb* \rb whatever is good|הַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb in your sight.”|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Then Jehu wrote|וַיִּכְתֹּ֣ב\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶם֩\rb* \rb a second|שֵׁנִ֜ית\rb* \rb letter|סֵ֨פֶר׀\rb* \rb and said:|לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb “If|אִם־\rb*\rb |לִ֨י\rb* \rb you are on my side,|אַתֶּ֜ם\rb*\rb |וּלְקֹלִ֣י׀\rb* \rb and if you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb will obey me,|שֹׁמְעִ֗ים\rb* \rb then bring|קְחוּ֙\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁי֙\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of your master’s|אֲדֹנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וּבֹ֧אוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֛י\rb* \rb sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb to me|אֶת־\rb* \rb at Jezreel|יִזְרְעֶ֑אלָה\rb* \rb by this time|כָּעֵ֥ת\rb* \rb tomorrow.”|מָחָ֖ר\rb*
\p \rb Now the sons|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the king,|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb in all,|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb were being brought up|מְגַדְּלִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb by the leading men|גְּדֹלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the city.|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \v 7 \rb And|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when the letter|הַסֵּ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb arrived,|כְּבֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb they took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and slaughtered|וַֽיִּשְׁחֲט֖וּ\rb* \rb all seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb of them.|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb They put|וַיָּשִׂ֤ימוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their heads|רָֽאשֵׁיהֶם֙\rb* \rb in baskets|בַּדּוּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and sent them|וַיִּשְׁלְח֥וּ\rb* \rb to Jehu|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb at Jezreel.|יִזְרְעֶֽאלָה׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb When the messenger|הַמַּלְאָךְ֙\rb* \rb arrived,|וַיָּבֹ֤א\rb* \rb he told|וַיַּגֶּד־\rb* \rb Jehu,|ל֣וֹ\rb* \rb “They have brought|הֵבִ֖יאוּ\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king.”|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb And Jehu ordered,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Pile|שִׂ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֞ם\rb* \rb in two|שְׁנֵ֧י\rb* \rb heaps|צִבֻּרִ֛ים\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֥תַח\rb* \rb of the gate|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb morning.”|הַבֹּֽקֶר׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb The next morning,|בַבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb Jehu went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֔ד\rb* \rb before|אֶל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “You|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb are innocent.|צַדִּקִ֖ים\rb* \rb It was I|אֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb who conspired|קָשַׁ֤רְתִּי\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb my master|אֲדֹנִי֙\rb* \rb and killed him.|וָאֶהְרְגֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb But who|וּמִ֥י\rb* \rb killed|הִכָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these?|אֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Know,|דְּע֣וּ\rb* \rb then,|אֵפ֗וֹא\rb* \rb that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb a word|מִדְּבַ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb has spoken|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb will fail,|יִפֹּ֜ל\rb*\rb |אַ֔רְצָה\rb* \rb for the LORD|וַיהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He promised|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb Elijah.”|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb So Jehu|יֵה֗וּא\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb in Jezreel|בְּיִזְרְעֶ֔אל\rb* \rb who remained|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֤ים\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵית־\rb* \rb of Ahab,|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb as well as all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his great men|גְּדֹלָ֖יו\rb* \rb and close friends|וּמְיֻדָּעָ֣יו\rb* \rb and priests,|וְכֹהֲנָ֑יו\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb* \rb leaving|הִשְׁאִֽיר־\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb without a single|בִּלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb survivor.|שָׂרִֽיד׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then Jehu set out|וַיָּ֙קָם֙\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֔א\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb toward Samaria.|שֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb*\rb |ה֛וּא\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb At Beth-eked|עֵ֥קֶד\rb* \rb of the Shepherds,|הָרֹעִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בַּדָּֽרֶךְ׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Jehu|וְיֵה֗וּא\rb* \rb met|מָצָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb some relatives|אֲחֵי֙\rb* \rb of Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb “Who|מִ֣י\rb* \rb are you?”|אַתֶּ֑ם\rb*
\p \rb “We are|אֲנַ֔חְנוּ\rb* \rb relatives|אֲחֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Ahaziah,”|אֲחַזְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb they answered,|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb “and we have come down|וַנֵּ֛רֶד\rb* \rb to greet|לִשְׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and|וּבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the queen mother.”|הַגְּבִירָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then Jehu ordered,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Take them|תִּפְשׂ֣וּם\rb* \rb alive.”|חַיִּ֔ים\rb* \rb So his men took them|וַֽיִּתְפְּשׂ֖וּם\rb* \rb alive,|חַיִּ֑ים\rb* \rb then slaughtered them|וַֽיִּשְׁחָט֞וּם\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the well|בּ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Beth-eked—|עֵ֗קֶד\rb* \rb forty-two|אַרְבָּעִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb men.|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb He|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb spared|הִשְׁאִ֥יר\rb* \rb none|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of them.|מֵהֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb When he left|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb there,|מִשָּׁ֡ם\rb* \rb he found|וַיִּמְצָ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jehonadab|יְהוֹנָדָב֩\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rechab,|רֵכָ֨ב\rb* \rb who was coming to meet him.|לִקְרָאת֜וֹ\rb* \rb Jehu greeted him|וַֽיְבָרְכֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “Is|הֲיֵ֧שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֣\rb* \rb as true to mine|יָשָׁ֗ר\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb my heart|לְבָבִי֙\rb* \rb is|עִם־\rb* \rb to yours?”|לְבָבֶ֔ךָ\rb*
\p \rb “It is!”|יֵ֛שׁ\rb* \rb Jehonadab|יְהוֹנָדָ֥ב\rb* \rb replied.|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb “If it is,” said Jehu,|וָיֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb “give|תְּנָ֣ה\rb* \rb me|אֶת־\rb* \rb your hand.”|יָדֶ֑ךָ\rb*
\p \rb So he gave him|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb his hand,|יָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and Jehu helped him|וַיַּעֲלֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb into|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb his chariot,|הַמֶּרְכָּבָֽה׃\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \v 16 \rb saying,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “Come|לְכָ֣ה\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֔י\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאֵ֖ה\rb* \rb my zeal|בְּקִנְאָתִ֣י\rb* \rb for the LORD!”|לַיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb So he had him ride|וַיַּרְכִּ֥בוּ\rb*\f + \fr 10:16 \ft LXX, Syriac, and Targum Yonaton; Hebrew \fqa they had him ride\f*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in his chariot.|בְּרִכְבּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb When Jehu came|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to Samaria,|שֹֽׁמְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb he struck down|וַ֠יַּךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb belonging to Ahab|לְאַחְאָ֛ב\rb* \rb who remained|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֧ים\rb* \rb there,|בְּשֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb he had destroyed them,|הִשְׁמִיד֑וֹ\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Elijah.|אֵלִיָּֽהוּ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Jehu Kills the Priests of Baal
\p \v 18 \rb Then Jehu|יֵהוּא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb brought all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb together|וַיִּקְבֹּ֤ץ\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Ahab|אַחְאָ֕ב\rb* \rb served|עָבַ֥ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Baal|הַבַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb a little,|מְעָ֑ט\rb* \rb but Jehu|יֵה֖וּא\rb* \rb will serve him|יַעַבְדֶ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb a lot.|הַרְבֵּֽה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb summon|קִרְא֨וּ\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֜י\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Baal,|הַבַּ֡עַל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his servants,|עֹבְדָ֣יו\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his priests.|כֹּהֲנָיו֩\rb* \rb See that no one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb is missing,|יִפָּקֵ֗ד\rb* \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb I have|לִי֙\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb sacrifice|זֶ֨בַח\rb* \rb for Baal.|לַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb Whoever|כֹּ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb is missing|יִפָּקֵ֖ד\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb live.”|יִֽחְיֶ֑ה\rb*
\p \rb But Jehu|וְיֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb was acting|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb deceptively|בְעָקְבָּ֔ה\rb* \rb in order to|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb destroy|הַאֲבִ֖יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the servants|עֹבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Baal.|הַבָּֽעַל׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And Jehu|יֵה֗וּא\rb* \rb commanded,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Proclaim|קַדְּשׁ֧וּ\rb* \rb a solemn assembly|עֲצָרָ֛ה\rb* \rb for Baal.”|לַבַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb So they announced it.|וַיִּקְרָֽאוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Then Jehu|יֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb sent word|וַיִּשְׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the servants|עֹבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb came;|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb there was not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb a man|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |נִשְׁאַ֥ר\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb failed|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to show.|בָ֑א\rb* \rb They entered|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb the temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Baal,|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb and it|בֵית־\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb was filled|וַיִּמָּלֵ֥א\rb* \rb from end|פֶּ֥ה\rb* \rb to end.|לָפֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And Jehu said|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb to the keeper|לַֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb of the wardrobe,|הַמֶּלְתָּחָ֔ה\rb* \rb “Bring out|הוֹצֵ֣א\rb* \rb garments|לְב֔וּשׁ\rb* \rb for all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the servants|עֹבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Baal.”|הַבָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb So he brought out|וַיֹּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb garments|הַמַּלְבּֽוּשׁ׃\rb* \rb for them.|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Next, Jehu|יֵה֛וּא\rb* \rb and Jehonadab|וִיהוֹנָדָ֥ב\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Rechab|רֵכָ֖ב\rb* \rb entered|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb the temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Baal,|הַבָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb and Jehu said|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb to the servants|לְעֹבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Baal,|הַבַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb “Look around|חַפְּשׂ֤וּ\rb* \rb to see|וּרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb that there are|יֶשׁ־\rb* \rb no|פֶּן־\rb* \rb servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb here|פֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb among you—|עִמָּכֶם֙\rb* \rb only|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb servants|עֹבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Baal.”|הַבַּ֖עַל\rb*\rb |לְבַדָּֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb And they went in|וַיָּבֹ֕אוּ\rb*\f + \fr 10:24 \ft LXX \fqa he went in\ft ; see also verse 25.\f* \rb to offer|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb sacrifices|זְבָחִ֣ים\rb* \rb and burnt offerings.|וְעֹל֑וֹת\rb* \rb Now Jehu|וְיֵה֞וּא\rb* \rb had stationed|שָׂם־\rb* \rb eighty|שְׁמֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb outside|בַחוּץ֙\rb* \rb and warned them,|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “If anyone|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb allows one of|מִן־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am delivering|מֵבִ֣יא\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb your hands|יְדֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to escape,|יִמָּלֵט֙\rb* \rb he will forfeit his life|נַפְשׁ֖וֹ\rb* \rb for|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb theirs.”|נַפְשֽׁוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb When he had finished|כְּכַלֹּת֣וֹ׀\rb* \rb making|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the burnt offering,|הָעֹלָ֗ה\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵ֠הוּא\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to the guards|לָרָצִ֨ים\rb* \rb and officers,|וְלַשָּׁלִשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb “Go in|בֹּ֤אוּ\rb* \rb and kill them.|הַכּוּם֙\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let anyone|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb out.”|יֵצֵ֔א\rb*
\p \rb So the guards|הָֽרָצִים֙\rb* \rb and officers|וְהַשָּׁ֣לִשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb put them|וַיַּכּ֖וּם\rb*\rb |לְפִי־\rb* \rb to the sword,|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb threw the bodies out,|וַיַּשְׁלִ֗כוּ\rb* \rb and went|וַיֵּלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb into|עַד־\rb* \rb the inner room|עִ֥יר\rb* \rb of the temple|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Baal.|הַבָּֽעַל׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb They brought out|וַיֹּצִ֛אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacred pillar|מַצְּב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the temple|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb and burned it.|וַֽיִּשְׂרְפֽוּהָ׃\rb* \v 27 \rb They also demolished|וַֽיִּתְּצ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the sacred pillar|מַצְּבַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Baal.|הַבָּ֑עַל\rb* \rb Then they tore down|וַֽיִּתְּצוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb and made|וַיְשִׂמֻ֥הוּ\rb* \rb it into a latrine,|לְמַחֲרָאוֹת\rb* \rb which it is to|עַד־\rb* \rb this day.|הַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*
\s1 Jehu Repeats Jeroboam’s Sins
\p \v 28 \rb Thus Jehu|יֵה֛וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb eradicated|וַיַּשְׁמֵ֥ד\rb* \rb Baal|הַבַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb from Israel,|מִיִּשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 29 \rb but|רַ֠ק\rb* \rb he|יֵה֖וּא\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֥ר\rb* \rb from|מֵאַֽחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the sins|חֲטָאֵ֞י\rb* \rb that Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֤ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָט֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to commit—|הֶחֱטִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the worship of the golden|הַזָּהָ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb calves|עֶגְלֵי֙\rb* \rb at Bethel|אֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb and Dan.|בְּדָֽן׃ס\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb Nevertheless, the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehu,|יֵה֗וּא\rb* \rb “Because|יַ֤עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have done well|הֱטִיבֹ֙תָ֙\rb* \rb in carrying out|לַעֲשׂ֤וֹת\rb* \rb what is right|הַיָּשָׁר֙\rb* \rb in My sight|בְּעֵינַ֔י\rb* \rb and have done|עָשִׂ֖יתָ\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb was in My heart,|בִּלְבָבִ֔י\rb* \rb four generations|רְבִעִ֔ים\rb* \rb of your sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb will sit|יֵשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \rb of Israel.”|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb Yet Jehu|וְיֵה֗וּא\rb* \rb was not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb careful|שָׁמַ֛ר\rb* \rb to follow|לָלֶ֛כֶת\rb* \rb the instruction|בְּתֽוֹרַת־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his heart.|לְבָב֑וֹ\rb* \rb He did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֗ר\rb* \rb from|מֵעַל֙\rb* \rb the sins|חַטֹּ֣אות\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָֽרָבְעָ֔ם\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to commit.|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb began|הֵחֵ֣ל\rb* \rb to reduce the size|לְקַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of Israel.|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb defeated|וַיַּכֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb throughout|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their territory|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \v 33 \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּן֙\rb* \rb eastward|מִזְרַ֣ח\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֔מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb through all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֔ד\rb* \rb (the region of Gad,|הַגָּדִ֥י\rb* \rb Reuben,|וְהָרֻאובֵנִ֖י\rb* \rb and Manasseh),|וְהַֽמְנַשִּׁ֑י\rb* \rb and from Aroer|מֵעֲרֹעֵר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the Arnon|אַרְנֹ֔ן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb through Gilead|וְהַגִּלְעָ֖ד\rb* \rb to Bashan.|וְהַבָּשָֽׁן׃\rb*
\s1 Jehoahaz Succeeds Jehu in Israel
\p \v 34 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jehu,|יֵה֛וּא\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his might,|גְּבוּרָת֑וֹ\rb*\rb |הֲלֽוֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb And Jehu|יֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Samaria,|בְּשֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֥ז\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb* \v 36 \rb So the duration|וְהַיָּמִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb of Jehu’s|יֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb reign|מָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃פ\rb* \rb was twenty-eight|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנֶֽה־\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*
\c 11
\s1 Athaliah and Joash
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 22:10–12|2CH 22:10-12\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb When Athaliah|וַֽעֲתַלְיָה֙\rb* \rb the mother|אֵ֣ם\rb* \rb of Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb saw|וְרָאֲתָה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb her son|בְּנָ֑הּ\rb* \rb was dead,|מֵ֣ת\rb* \rb she proceeded|וַתָּ֙קָם֙\rb* \rb to annihilate|וַתְּאַבֵּ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמַּמְלָכָֽה׃\rb* \rb heirs.|זֶ֥רַע\rb* \v 2 \rb But Jehosheba|יְהוֹשֶׁ֣בַע\rb*\f + \fr 11:2 \fqa Jehosheba \ft is a variant of \fqa Jehoshabeath\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 22:11.\f* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Joram,|י֠וֹרָם\rb*\f + \fr 11:2 \fqa Joram \ft is a variant spelling of \fqa Jehoram\ft .\f* \rb the sister|אֲח֨וֹת\rb* \rb of Ahaziah,|אֲחַזְיָ֜הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַתִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb Joash|יוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֗ה\rb* \rb and stole him away|וַתִּגְנֹ֤ב\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb who were being murdered.|הַמָּמוֹתְתִים\rb*\rb |אֹת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb She put him and his nurse|מֵינִקְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in a bedroom|בַּחֲדַ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַמִּטּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb to hide|וַיַּסְתִּ֧רוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb from|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Athaliah,|עֲתַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and he was not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb killed.|הוּמָֽת׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb And Joash remained|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb hidden|מִתְחַבֵּ֖א\rb* \rb with his nurse|אִתָּהּ֙\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb for six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb while Athaliah|וַעֲתַלְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb ruled|מֹלֶ֥כֶת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the land.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Joash Anointed King of Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 23:1–11|2CH 23:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 4 \rb Then in the seventh|הַ֠שְּׁבִיעִית\rb* \rb year,|וּבַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֜ע\rb* \rb sent for|שָׁלַ֨ח\rb*\rb |וַיִּקַּ֣ח׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds,|הַמֵּאיוֹת\rb* \rb the Carites,|לַכָּרִי֙\rb*\f + \fr 11:4 \ft Or \fqa the mercenaries \ft or \fqa the executioners\ft ; also in verse 19\f* \rb and the guards,|וְלָ֣רָצִ֔ים\rb* \rb and had them brought|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb There|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb he made|וַיִּכְרֹת֩\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֜ית\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and put them under oath.|וַיַּשְׁבַּ֤ע\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb*
\p \rb He showed|וַיַּ֥רְא\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \v 5 \rb and commanded them,|וַיְצַוֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “This|זֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb is what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to do:|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּן\rb* \rb A third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֤ית\rb* \rb of you|מִכֶּם֙\rb* \rb who come on duty|בָּאֵ֣י\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb shall guard|וְשֹׁ֣מְרֵ֔י\rb*\rb |מִשְׁמֶ֖רֶת\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb palace,|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \v 6 \rb a third shall be|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁית֙\rb* \rb at the gate|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Sur,|ס֔וּר\rb* \rb and a third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb at the gate|בַּשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb behind|אַחַ֣ר\rb* \rb the guards.|הָרָצִ֑ים\rb* \rb You are to take turns|מַסָּֽח׃\rb* \rb guarding|וּשְׁמַרְתֶּ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb the temple—|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*  \v 7 \rb the two|וּשְׁתֵּ֤י\rb* \rb divisions|הַיָּדוֹת֙\rb*\rb |כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb that would go off duty|יֹצְאֵ֣י\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb are to guard|וְשָֽׁמְר֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king.|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb You must surround|וְהִקַּפְתֶּ֨ם\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |סָבִ֗יב\rb* \rb with weapons|וְכֵלָ֣יו\rb* \rb in hand,|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb* \rb and anyone|אִ֚ישׁ\rb* \rb who approaches|וְהַבָּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the ranks|הַשְּׂדֵר֖וֹת\rb* \rb must be put to death.|יוּמָ֑ת\rb* \rb You must stay|וִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb close|אֶת־\rb* \rb to the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb wherever he goes.”|בְּצֵאת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |וּבְבֹאֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb So the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּאיוֹת\rb* \rb did|וַֽיַּעֲשׂ֞וּ\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֣ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֣ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֒\rb* \rb had ordered.|צִוָּה֮\rb* \rb Each of them|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְחוּ֙\rb* \rb his men—|אֲנָשָׁ֔יו\rb* \rb those coming on duty|בָּאֵ֣י\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֔ת\rb* \rb and|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb those going off duty—|יֹצְאֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb and came|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֥ע\rb* \rb the priest.|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb* \v 10 \rb Then the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb to the commanders|לְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּאיוֹת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb the spears|הַחֲנִית֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb shields|הַשְּׁלָטִ֔ים\rb* \rb of King|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֑ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb from|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And the guards|הָרָצִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ׀\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעַמְד֨וּ\rb* \rb with weapons|וְכֵלָ֣יו\rb* \rb in hand|בְּיָד֗וֹ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb surrounding|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb by the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb and the temple,|וְלַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb from the south|הַיְמָנִית֙\rb* \rb side|מִכֶּ֨תֶף\rb*\rb |הַבַּ֤יִת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the north|הַשְּׂמָאלִ֔ית\rb* \rb side|כֶּ֤תֶף\rb* \rb of the temple.|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb Then Jehoiada brought out|וַיּוֹצִ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb son,|בֶּן־\rb* \rb put|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb the crown|הַנֵּ֙זֶר֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb on him,|עָלָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb presented him with the Testimony,|הָ֣עֵד֔וּת\rb* \rb and proclaimed him king.|וַיַּמְלִ֥כוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb They anointed him,|וַיִּמְשָׁחֻ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and the people clapped|וַיַּכּוּ־\rb* \rb their hands|כָ֔ף\rb* \rb and declared,|וַיֹּאמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb “Long live|יְחִ֥י\rb* \rb the king!”|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Death of Athaliah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 23:12–15|2CH 23:12-15\ref*)
\p \v 13 \rb When Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|וַתִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the noise|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb from the guards|הָֽרָצִ֖ין\rb* \rb and the people,|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb she went out|וַתָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb And she looked out|וַתֵּ֡רֶא\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּלֶךְ֩\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֨ד\rb* \rb by|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the pillar,|הָעַמּ֜וּד\rb* \rb according to the custom.|כַּמִּשְׁפָּ֗ט\rb* \rb The officers|וְהַשָּׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb and trumpeters|וְהַחֲצֹֽצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb were beside|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king,|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb were rejoicing|שָׂמֵ֔חַ\rb* \rb and blowing|וְתֹקֵ֖עַ\rb* \rb trumpets.|בַּחֲצֹֽצְר֑וֹת\rb*
\p \rb Then Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb tore|וַתִּקְרַ֤ע\rb* \rb her clothes|בְּגָדֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb and screamed,|וַתִּקְרָ֖א\rb* \rb “Treason!|קֶ֥שֶׁר\rb* \rb Treason!”|קָֽשֶׁר׃ס\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb And Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֨ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ordered|וַיְצַו֩\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of hundreds|הַמֵּיאוֹת\rb* \rb in charge of|פְּקֻדֵ֣י\rb* \rb the army,|הַחַ֗יִל\rb* \rb “Bring her out|הוֹצִ֤יאוּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָהּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb between the ranks,|לַשְּׂדֵרֹ֔ת\rb*\f + \fr 11:15 \ft Or \fqa out from the precincts\f* \rb and put to|הָמֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the sword|בֶּחָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb anyone who follows|וְהַבָּ֥א\rb* \rb her.”|אַחֲרֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb* \rb had said,|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “She must not|אַל־\rb* \rb be put to death|תּוּמַ֖ת\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb So they seized|וַיָּשִׂ֤מוּ\rb*\rb |לָהּ֙\rb* \rb Athaliah|יָדַ֔יִם\rb* \rb as she reached|וַתָּב֛וֹא\rb*\rb |דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the horses’|הַסּוּסִ֖ים\rb* \rb entrance|מְב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to the palace grounds,|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and there|שָֽׁם׃ס\rb* \rb she was put to death.|וַתּוּמַ֖ת\rb*
\s1 Jehoiada Restores the Worship of the LORD
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 23:16–21|2CH 23:16-21\ref*)
\p \v 17 \rb Then Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֜ע\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb made|וַיִּכְרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb a covenant|הַבְּרִ֗ית\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֤ין\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb that they would be|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb the LORD’s|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb people.|לְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb He also made a covenant between|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb So all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|עַם֩\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to the temple|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֜עַל\rb* \rb and tore it down.|וַֽיִּתְּצֻ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb They smashed the altars|מִזְבְּחֹתוֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and idols|צְלָמָיו֙\rb* \rb to pieces,|שִׁבְּר֣וּ\rb*\rb |הֵיטֵ֔ב\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb and they killed|הָרְג֖וּ\rb* \rb Mattan|מַתָּן֙\rb* \rb the priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of Baal|הַבַּ֔עַל\rb* \rb in front of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the altars.|הַֽמִּזְבְּח֑וֹת\rb*
\p \rb And Jehoiada the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb* \rb posted|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb* \rb guards|פְּקֻדּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 19 \rb He took with him|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of hundreds,|הַ֠מֵּאוֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Carites,|הַכָּרִ֨י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the guards,|הָרָצִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb and they brought|וַיֹּרִ֤ידוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king down|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and entered|וַיָּב֛וֹאוּ\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb by way|דֶּֽרֶך־\rb* \rb of the Gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of the Guards.|הָרָצִ֖ים\rb*
\p \rb Then Joash took his seat|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the royal|הַמְּלָכִֽים׃\rb* \rb throne,|כִּסֵּ֥א\rb* \v 20 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb rejoiced.|וַיִּשְׂמַ֥ח\rb* \rb And the city|וְהָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb was quiet,|שָׁקָ֑טָה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb because Athaliah|עֲתַלְיָ֛הוּ\rb* \rb had been put to|הֵמִ֥יתוּ\rb* \rb the sword|בַחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb at the royal|מֶלֶךְ׃ס\rb* \rb palace.|בֵּ֥ית\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Joash|יְהוֹאָ֥שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 11:21 \ft Hebrew \fqa Jehoash\ft , a variant of \fqa Joash \ft (son of Ahaziah) as in verse 2\f* \rb was seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \rb when he became king.|בְּמָלְכֽוֹ׃פ\rb*
\c 12
\s1 Joash Repairs the Temple
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 24:1–14|2CH 24:1-14\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the seventh|שֶׁ֤בַע\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת־\rb* \rb of Jehu,|לְיֵהוּא֙\rb* \rb Joash|יְהוֹאָ֔שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 12:1 \ft Hebrew \fqa Jehoash\ft , a variant of \fqa Joash \ft (son of Ahaziah); also in verses 2, 4, 6, 7, and 18; see 2 Kings 11:2.\f* \rb became king,|מָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb forty|וְאַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Zibiah;|צִבְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb she was from|מִבְּאֵ֥ר\rb* \rb Beersheba.|שָֽׁבַע׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And Joash|יְהוֹאָ֧שׁ\rb* \rb did|וַיַּ֨עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֛ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the days|יָמָ֑יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he was instructed|הוֹרָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb by Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֖ע\rb* \rb the priest.|הַכֹּהֵֽן׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb Nevertheless,|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb the high places|הַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb were not|לֹא־\rb* \rb removed;|סָ֑רוּ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb continued|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb sacrificing|מְזַבְּחִ֥ים\rb* \rb and burning incense|וּֽמְקַטְּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb there.|בַּבָּמֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then Joash|יְהוֹאָ֜שׁ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the priests,|הַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb* \rb “Collect all|כֹּל֩\rb* \rb the money|כֶּ֨סֶף\rb* \rb brought|יוּבָ֤א\rb* \rb as sacred gifts|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb into the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD—|יְהוָה֙\rb*  \rb the census|עוֹבֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |אִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb money,|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb the money|כֶּ֥סֶף\rb* \rb from vows,|נַפְשׁ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |עֶרְכּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and|כָּל־\rb* \rb the money|כֶּ֗סֶף\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb brought|לְהָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb voluntarily|יַֽעֲלֶה֙\rb*\rb |עַ֣ל\rb*\rb |לֶב־\rb*\rb |אִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 5 \rb Let every|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb receive it|יִקְח֤וּ\rb*\rb |לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb from his constituency,|מַכָּר֑וֹ\rb* \rb and let it be used|וְהֵ֗ם\rb* \rb to repair|יְחַזְּקוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb any damage|בֶּ֣דֶק\rb*\rb |בָּֽדֶק׃פ\rb* \rb found|יִמָּצֵ֥א\rb* \rb in the temple.”|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb By the twenty-third|עֶשְׂרִ֧ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹ֛שׁ\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֖ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the reign|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Joash,|יְהוֹאָ֑שׁ\rb* \rb however,|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had not yet|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb repaired|חִזְּק֥וּ\rb* \rb the damage|בֶּ֥דֶק\rb* \rb to the temple.|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \v 7 \rb So King|הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb Joash|יְהוֹאָ֜שׁ\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָא֩\rb* \rb Jehoiada|לִיהוֹיָדָ֤ע\rb*\rb |הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb and the other priests|וְלַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Why|מַדּ֛וּעַ\rb* \rb have you not|אֵינְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb repaired|מְחַזְּקִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the damage|בֶּ֣דֶק\rb* \rb to the temple?|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb take|תִּקְחוּ־\rb* \rb no more|אַל־\rb* \rb money|כֶ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb your constituency,|מַכָּֽרֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb but|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb hand it over|תִּתְּנֻֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb for the repair|לְבֶ֥דֶק\rb* \rb of the temple.”|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb So the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִ֑ים\rb* \rb agreed|וַיֵּאֹ֖תוּ\rb* \rb that they would not|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb receive|קְחַת־\rb* \rb money|כֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb and that they would not|וּלְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb repair|חַזֵּ֖ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |בֶּ֥דֶק\rb* \rb the temple themselves.|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Then Jehoiada|יְהוֹיָדָ֤ע\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵן֙\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb chest,|אֲר֣וֹן\rb* \rb bored|וַיִּקֹּ֥ב\rb* \rb a hole|חֹ֖ר\rb* \rb in its lid,|בְּדַלְתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb and set|וַיִּתֵּ֣ן\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֩\rb* \rb it beside|אֵ֨צֶל\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֜חַ\rb* \rb on the right side|בַּיָּמִין\rb* \rb as one|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb enters|בְּבֽוֹא־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb There|שָׁ֤מָּה\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb who guarded|שֹׁמְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the threshold|הַסַּ֔ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb put|וְנָֽתְנוּ־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb brought|הַמּוּבָ֥א\rb* \rb into the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb Whenever they saw|כִּרְאוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb there was a large amount|רַ֥ב\rb* \rb of money|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb in the chest,|בָּֽאָר֑וֹן\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb scribe|סֹפֵ֤ר\rb* \rb and the high|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb priest|וְהַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb would go up,|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb count|וַיִּמְנ֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb brought|הַנִּמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb into the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb and tie it up in bags.|וַיָּצֻ֙רוּ֙\rb* \v 11 \rb Then they would put|וְנָתְנוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the counted|הַֽמְתֻכָּ֔ן\rb* \rb money|הַכֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|יַד\rb* \rb of those who|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb supervised|הַפְּקֻדִים\rb* \rb the work|הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb who in turn would pay|וַיּוֹצִיאֻ֜הוּ\rb* \rb those doing the work—|הָעֹשִׂ֖ים\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb*\rb |יְהוָֽה׃\rb*  \rb the carpenters,|לְחָרָשֵׁ֤י\rb*\rb |הָעֵץ֙\rb* \rb builders,|וְלַבֹּנִ֔ים\rb* \v 12 \rb masons,|וְלַגֹּֽדְרִים֙\rb* \rb and stonecutters.|וּלְחֹצְבֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הָאֶ֔בֶן\rb* \rb They also purchased|וְלִקְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb timber|עֵצִים֙\rb* \rb and dressed|מַחְצֵ֔ב\rb* \rb stone|וְאַבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb to repair|לְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the damage|בֶּ֣דֶק\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and they paid|יֵצֵ֥א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the other expenses|וּלְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb repairs.|לְחָזְקָֽה׃\rb*
