\s1 The Death of Joash
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 24:23–27|2CH 24:23-27\ref*)
\p \v 17 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Hazael|חֲזָאֵל֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb marched up|יַעֲלֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and fought|וַיִּלָּ֥חֶם\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Gath|גַּ֖ת\rb* \rb and captured it.|וַֽיִּלְכְּדָ֑הּ\rb* \rb Then he|חֲזָאֵל֙\rb* \rb decided|וַיָּ֤שֶׂם\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb to attack|לַעֲל֖וֹת\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb So King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Joash|יְהוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֞ח\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sacred objects|הַקֳּדָשִׁ֡ים\rb* \rb dedicated|הִקְדִּ֣ישׁוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb by his fathers—|אֲבֹתָ֜יו\rb* \rb Jehoshaphat,|יְהוֹשָׁפָ֣ט\rb* \rb Jehoram,|וִיהוֹרָם֩\rb* \rb and Ahaziah,|וַאֲחַזְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Judah—|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb his own consecrated items|קֳדָשָׁ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb found|הַנִּמְצָ֛א\rb* \rb in the treasuries|בְּאֹצְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb and the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace,|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb and he sent them|וַיִּשְׁלַ֗ח\rb* \rb to Hazael|לַֽחֲזָאֵל֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram.|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb So Hazael withdrew|וַיַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Joash,|יוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments,|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*\rb |הֲלוֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And the servants of Joash|עֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb rose up|וַיָּקֻ֥מוּ\rb* \rb and formed|וַיִּקְשְׁרֽוּ־\rb* \rb a conspiracy|קָ֑שֶׁר\rb* \rb and killed|וַיַּכּוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb him|יוֹאָ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb at Beth-millo,|מִלֹּ֖א\rb* \rb on the road down|הַיּוֹרֵ֥ד\rb* \rb to Silla.|סִלָּֽא׃\rb* \v 21 \rb His servants|עֲבָדָיו֙\rb* \rb Jozabad|וְיוֹזָבָ֣ד\rb*\f + \fr 12:21 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Syriac \fqa Jozacar\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shimeath|שִׁ֠מְעָת\rb* \rb and Jehozabad|וִיהוֹזָבָ֨ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shomer|שֹׁמֵ֤ר׀\rb*\f + \fr 12:21 \fqa Shomer \ft is a variant of \fqa Shimrith\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 24:26.\f* \rb struck him down,|הִכֻּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and he died.|וַיָּמֹ֔ת\rb* \rb And they buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David,|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\c 13
\s1 Jehoahaz Reigns in Israel
\p \v 1 \rb In the twenty-third|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹשׁ֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Joash|לְיוֹאָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahaziah|אֲחַזְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֨ז\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehu|יֵה֤וּא\rb* \rb became king|מָ֠לַךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and he reigned in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb seventeen|שְׁבַ֥ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and followed|וַ֠יֵּלֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַחַ֨ר\rb* \rb the sins|חַטֹּ֜את\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֛ט\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to commit;|הֶחֱטִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֥ר\rb* \rb from them.|מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb So the anger|אַ֥ף\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb burned|וַיִּֽחַר־\rb* \rb against Israel,|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and He delivered them|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֞ם\rb* \rb continually|כָּל־\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד׀\rb* \rb of Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֛ד\rb* \rb and his|חֲזָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad.|הֲדַ֥ד\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Then Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֖ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sought|וַיְחַ֥ל\rb* \rb the favor|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb listened|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb He saw|רָאָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the oppression|לַ֣חַץ\rb* \rb that the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָֽם׃\rb* \rb had inflicted|לָחַ֥ץ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb on Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \v 5 \rb So the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb Israel|לְיִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb a deliverer,|מוֹשִׁ֔יעַ\rb* \rb and they escaped|וַיֵּ֣צְא֔וּ\rb*\rb |מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the power|יַד־\rb* \rb of the Arameans.|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb Then the people|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb lived|וַיֵּשְׁב֧וּ\rb* \rb in their own homes|בְּאָהֳלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as they had before.|כִּתְמ֥וֹל\rb*\rb |שִׁלְשֽׁוֹם׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb Nevertheless,|אַ֠ךְ\rb* \rb they did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֜רוּ\rb* \rb from the sins|מֵחַטֹּ֧אות\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֛ם\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to commit,|הֶחֱטִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but they continued to walk in them.|הָלָ֑ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 13:6 \ft LXX, Syriac, Targum Yonaton, and Vulgate; Hebrew \fqa he continued to walk in them\f* \rb The Asherah pole|הָאֲשֵׁרָ֔ה\rb* \rb even|וְגַם֙\rb* \rb remained standing|עָמְדָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Samaria.|בְּשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Jehoahaz|לִיהוֹאָחָ֜ז\rb* \rb had no|לֹא֩\rb* \rb army|עָ֗ם\rb* \rb left,|הִשְׁאִ֨יר\rb* \rb except|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb horsemen,|פָּֽרָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb ten|וַעֲשָׂ֣רָה\rb* \rb chariots,|רֶ֔כֶב\rb* \rb and ten|וַעֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb foot soldiers,|רַגְלִ֑י\rb* \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb had destroyed them|אִבְּדָם֙\rb* \rb and made them|וַיְשִׂמֵ֥ם\rb* \rb like the dust|כֶּֽעָפָ֖ר\rb* \rb at threshing.|לָדֻֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz,|יְהוֹאָחָ֛ז\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb and his might,|וּגְבוּרָת֑וֹ\rb*\rb |הֲלוֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And Jehoahaz|יְהֽוֹאָחָז֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in Samaria.|בְּשֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoash|יוֹאָ֥שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 13:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa Joash\ft , a variant of \fqa Jehoash\ft ; also in verses 10, 12, 13, 14, 15, and 25\f* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 Jehoash Reigns in Israel
\p \v 10 \rb In the thirty-seventh|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָשֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Joash|לְיוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Jehoash|יְהוֹאָ֨שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֤ז\rb* \rb became king|מָ֠לַךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb in Samaria,|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb and he reigned sixteen|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And he did|וַיַּֽעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֗ר\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the sins|חַטֹּ֞אות\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֛ט\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to commit,|הֶחֱטִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb but he walked in them.|הָלָֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 12 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Jehoash,|יוֹאָשׁ֙\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and his might,|וּגְב֣וּרָת֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb including his war|נִלְחַ֔ם\rb* \rb against|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb And Jehoash|יוֹאָשׁ֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers,|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and Jeroboam|וְיָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb succeeded him|יָשַׁ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne.|כִּסְא֑וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoash|יוֹאָשׁ֙\rb* \rb was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb with|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*
\s1 Elisha’s Final Prophecy
\p \v 14 \rb When Elisha|וֶֽאֱלִישָׁע֙\rb* \rb had fallen sick|חָלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with the illness|חָלְי֔וֹ\rb* \rb from which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he would die,|יָמ֖וּת\rb* \rb Jehoash|יוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb came down|וַיֵּ֨רֶד\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb and wept|וַיֵּ֤בְךְּ\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb him,|פָּנָיו֙\rb* \rb saying,|וַיֹּאמַ֔ר\rb* \rb “My father,|אָבִ֣י׀\rb* \rb my father,|אָבִ֔י\rb* \rb the chariots|רֶ֥כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen|וּפָרָשָֽׁיו׃\rb* \rb of Israel!”|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb told|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb him,|לוֹ֙\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֖ח\rb* \rb a bow|קֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb and some arrows.”|וְחִצִּ֑ים\rb*
\p \rb So Jehoash took|וַיִּקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb a bow|קֶ֥שֶׁת\rb* \rb and some arrows.|וְחִצִּֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Then Elisha said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר׀\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb “Put|הַרְכֵּ֤ב\rb* \rb your hand|יָֽדְךָ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bow.”|הַקֶּ֔שֶׁת\rb*
\p \rb So the king put|וַיַּרְכֵּ֖ב\rb* \rb his hand on the bow,|יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb and Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֛ע\rb* \rb put|וַיָּ֧שֶׂם\rb* \rb his hands|יָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb hands.|יְדֵ֥י\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb “Open|פְּתַ֧ח\rb* \rb the east|קֵ֖דְמָה\rb* \rb window,”|הַחַלּ֛וֹן\rb* \rb said Elisha.|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb So he opened it|וַיִּפְתָּ֑ח\rb* \rb and Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֤ע\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “Shoot!”|יְרֵה֙\rb* \rb So he shot.|וַיּ֔וֹר\rb*
\p \rb And Elisha declared:|וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb*
\q1 \rb “This is the LORD’s|לַֽיהוָה֙\rb* \rb arrow|חֵץ־\rb* \rb of victory,|תְּשׁוּעָ֤ה\rb*
\q2 \rb the arrow|וְחֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of victory|תְּשׁוּעָ֣ה\rb* \rb over Aram,|בַֽאֲרָ֔ם\rb*
\q1 \rb for you shall strike|וְהִכִּיתָ֧\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Arameans|אֲרָ֛ם\rb* \rb in Aphek|בַּאֲפֵ֖ק\rb*
\q2 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you have put an end to them.”|כַּלֵּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb Then Elisha said,|וַיֹּ֛אמֶר\rb* \rb “Take|קַ֥ח\rb* \rb the arrows!”|הַחִצִּ֖ים\rb*
\p \rb So he took them,|וַיִּקָּ֑ח\rb* \rb and Elisha said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb “Strike|הַךְ־\rb* \rb the ground!”|אַ֔רְצָה\rb*
\p \rb So he struck|וַיַּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb the ground three|שָֽׁלֹשׁ־\rb* \rb times|פְּעָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and stopped.|וַֽיַּעֲמֹֽד׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb But the man|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of God|הָאֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb was angry|וַיִּקְצֹ֨ף\rb* \rb with him|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “You should have struck|לְהַכּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb the ground five|חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb or|אוֹ־\rb* \rb six|שֵׁשׁ֙\rb* \rb times.|פְּעָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb Then|אָ֛ז\rb* \rb you would have struck down|הִכִּ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Aram|אֲרָ֖ם\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you had put an end to it.|כַּלֵּ֑ה\rb* \rb But now|וְעַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb you will strike down|תַּכֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Aram|אֲרָֽם׃ס\rb* \rb only three|שָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb times.”|פְּעָמִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb And Elisha|אֱלִישָׁ֖ע\rb* \rb died|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb* \rb and was buried.|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֑הוּ\rb*
\p \rb Now the Moabite|מוֹאָ֛ב\rb* \rb raiders|וּגְדוּדֵ֥י\rb* \rb used to come|יָבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb into the land|בָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb every spring.|בָּ֥א\rb*\f + \fr 13:20 \ft Literally \fqa into the land at the coming in of the year\f* \rb |שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*\v 21 \rb Once,|וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb as the Israelites|הֵ֣ם׀\rb* \rb were burying|קֹבְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb a man,|אִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb they saw|רָא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb a band of raiders,|הַגְּד֔וּד\rb* \rb so they threw|וַיַּשְׁלִ֥יכוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the man’s body|הָאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb into Elisha’s|אֱלִישָׁ֑ע\rb*\rb |וַיֵּ֜לֶךְ\rb* \rb tomb.|בְּקֶ֣בֶר\rb* \rb And as soon as his body touched|וַיִּגַּ֤ע\rb* \rb the bones|בְּעַצְמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Elisha,|אֱלִישָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb was revived|וַיְחִ֖י\rb* \rb and stood|וַיָּ֥קָם\rb* \rb up on|עַל־\rb* \rb his feet.|רַגְלָֽיו׃פ\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb And Hazael|וַֽחֲזָאֵל֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֔ם\rb* \rb oppressed|לָחַ֖ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb throughout|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the reign|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz.|יְהוֹאָחָֽז׃\rb* \v 23 \rb But the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb was gracious|וַיָּחָן֩\rb* \rb to Israel|אֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb and had compassion on them,|וַֽיְרַחֲמֵם֙\rb* \rb and He turned|וַיִּ֣פֶן\rb* \rb toward them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb because of|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb His covenant|בְּרִית֔וֹ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Abraham,|אַבְרָהָ֖ם\rb* \rb Isaac,|יִצְחָ֣ק\rb* \rb and Jacob.|וְיַֽעֲקֹ֑ב\rb* \rb And to|עַד־\rb* \rb this day,|עָֽתָּה׃\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb the LORD has been unwilling|אָבָה֙\rb* \rb to destroy them|הַשְׁחִיתָ֔ם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb cast them|הִשְׁלִיכָ֥ם\rb* \rb from|מֵֽעַל־\rb* \rb His presence.|פָּנָ֖יו\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb When Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֣ל\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֑ם\rb* \rb died,|וַיָּ֖מָת\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֥ד\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb* \v 25 \rb Then Jehoash|יְהוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֗ז\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb back|וַיָּ֜שָׁב\rb* \rb from|מִיַּד֙\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb* \rb Ben-hadad|הֲדַ֣ד\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hazael|חֲזָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb the cities|הֶֽעָרִים֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Hazael had taken|לָקַ֗ח\rb* \rb in battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֛ד\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb Jehoahaz.|יְהוֹאָחָ֥ז\rb* \rb Jehoash|יוֹאָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb defeated|הִכָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb Ben-hadad three|שָׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb times,|פְּעָמִים֙\rb* \rb and so recovered|וַיָּ֖שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the cities|עָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*
