\s1 Jehoash Defeats Amaziah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 25:17–24|2CH 25:17-24\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb Then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָה֙\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֤ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb Jehoash|יְהוֹאָ֨שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz,|יְהוֹאָחָ֧ז\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehu.|יֵה֛וּא\rb* \rb “Come,|לְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb let us meet|נִתְרָאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb face to face,”|פָנִֽים׃\rb* \rb he said.|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb But Jehoash|יְהוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb replied|וַיִּשְׁלַ֞ח\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָה֮\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “A thistle|הַח֜וֹחַ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Lebanon|בַּלְּבָנ֗וֹן\rb* \rb sent|שָׁ֠לַח\rb* \rb a message to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a cedar|הָאֶ֜רֶז\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb in Lebanon,|בַּלְּבָנוֹן֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘Give|תְּנָֽה־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your daughter|בִּתְּךָ֥\rb* \rb to my son|לִבְנִ֖י\rb* \rb in marriage.’|לְאִשָּׁ֑ה\rb* \rb Then a wild|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֤ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in Lebanon|בַּלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb came along|וַֽתַּעֲבֹ֞ר\rb* \rb and trampled|וַתִּרְמֹ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the thistle.|הַחֽוֹחַ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb You have indeed defeated|הַכֵּ֤ה\rb*\rb |הִכִּ֙יתָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Edom,|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb and your heart|לִבֶּ֑ךָ\rb* \rb has become proud.|וּֽנְשָׂאֲךָ֖\rb* \rb Glory in that|הִכָּבֵד֙\rb* \rb and stay|וְשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb at home.|בְּבֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb Why|וְלָ֤מָּה\rb* \rb should you stir up|תִתְגָּרֶה֙\rb* \rb trouble|בְּרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb so that you fall—|וְנָ֣פַלְתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and Judah|וִיהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb with you?”|עִמָּֽךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb But Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb listen,|שָׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb so Jehoash|יְהוֹאָ֤שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb advanced.|וַיַּ֨עַל\rb* \rb He|ה֖וּא\rb* \rb and King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Amaziah|וַאֲמַצְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb faced each other|וַיִּתְרָא֣וּ\rb*\rb |פָנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb at Beth-shemesh|שֶׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Judah.|לִיהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 12 \rb And Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb was routed|וַיִּנָּ֥גֶף\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and every man|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb fled|וַיָּנֻ֖סוּ\rb* \rb to his home.|לְאָהֳלוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb |וְאֵת֩\rb*\rb |בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb There at Beth-shemesh,|שָׁ֑מֶשׁ\rb* \rb Jehoash|יְהוֹאָ֣שׁ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb captured|תָּפַ֛שׂ\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֜ה\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Joash,|יְהוֹאָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahaziah.|אֲחַזְיָ֗הוּ\rb*
\p \rb Then Jehoash went|וַיָּבֹאוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and broke down|וַיִּפְרֹץ֩\rb* \rb the wall|בְּחוֹמַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb from the Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb Gate|בְּשַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Corner|הַפִּנָּ֔ה\rb* \rb Gate—|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*  \rb a section of four|אַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb cubits.|אַמָּֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 14:13 \fqa \ref 400|0\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 600|600\ref* feet or 182.9 meters.\f* \v 14 \rb He took|וְלָקַ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָב־\rb* \rb and silver|וְ֠הַכֶּסֶף\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the articles|הַכֵּלִ֜ים\rb* \rb found|הַנִּמְצְאִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and in the treasuries|וּבְאֹֽצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb palace,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb as well as some hostages.|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַתַּֽעֲרֻב֑וֹת\rb* \rb Then he returned|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb to Samaria.|שֹׁמְרֽוֹנָה׃\rb*
\s1 Jeroboam II Succeeds Jehoash in Israel
\p \v 15 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶתֶר֩\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jehoash,|יְהוֹאָ֜שׁ\rb* \rb along with his accomplishments,|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb his might,|וּגְב֣וּרָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and how|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he waged war|נִלְחַ֔ם\rb* \rb against|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*\rb |הֲלֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb And Jehoash|יְהוֹאָשׁ֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵר֙\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb with|עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 The Death of Amaziah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 25:25–28|2CH 25:25-28\ref*)
\p \v 17 \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Joash|יוֹאָשׁ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb lived|וַיְחִ֨י\rb* \rb for fifteen|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \rb after|אַֽחֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb the death|מ֔וֹת\rb* \rb of Jehoash|יְהוֹאָ֥שׁ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoahaz|יְהֽוֹאָחָ֖ז\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \v 18 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֖תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Amaziah,|אֲמַצְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb are they not|הֲלֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And conspirators|קֶ֛שֶׁר\rb* \rb plotted|וַיִּקְשְׁר֨וּ\rb* \rb against Amaziah|עָלָ֥יו\rb* \rb in Jerusalem,|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and he fled|וַיָּ֣נָס\rb* \rb to Lachish.|לָכִ֑ישָׁה\rb* \rb But men were sent|וַיִּשְׁלְח֤וּ\rb* \rb after him|אַֽחֲרָיו֙\rb* \rb to Lachish,|לָכִ֔ישָׁה\rb* \rb and they killed him|וַיְמִתֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb there.|שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 20 \rb They carried him back|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb horses|הַסּוּסִ֑ים\rb* \rb and buried him|וַיִּקָּבֵ֧ר\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of David.|דָּוִֽד׃\rb*
\s1 Azariah Succeeds Amaziah in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 26:1–2|2CH 26:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 21 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֤ם\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקְח֞וּ\rb* \rb Azariah,|עֲזַרְיָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 14:21 \fqa Azariah \ft is also called \fqa Uzziah\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 26:1.\f* \rb who|וְה֕וּא\rb* \rb was sixteen|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb years old,|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb and made him king|וַיַּמְלִ֣כוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֥יו\rb* \rb Amaziah.|אֲמַצְיָֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 22 \rb Azariah was the one|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb who rebuilt|בָּנָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Elath|אֵילַ֔ת\rb*\f + \fr 14:22 \fqa Elath \ft is a variant of \fqa Eloth\ft ; \ref see 1|1\ref* Kings 9:26.\f* \rb and restored it|וַיְשִׁבֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb to Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb King Amaziah|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb rested|שְׁכַֽב־\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers.|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 Jeroboam II Reigns in Israel
\p \v 23 \rb In the fifteenth|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Amaziah|לַאֲמַצְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Joash|יוֹאָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֨ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoash|יוֹאָ֤שׁ\rb* \rb became king|מָ֠לַךְ\rb*\rb |מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and he reigned in Samaria|בְּשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb forty-one|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֖ת\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb* \v 24 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֗ר\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the sins that|חַטֹּאות֙\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֔ט\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to commit.|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb This Jeroboam|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb restored|הֵשִׁיב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the boundary|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |מִלְּב֥וֹא\rb* \rb from Lebo-hamath|חֲמָ֖ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Sea|יָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the Arabah,|הָעֲרָבָ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 14:25 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֤ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֗ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb His servant|עַבְדּ֞וֹ\rb* \rb Jonah|יוֹנָ֤ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amittai,|אֲמִתַּי֙\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |מִגַּ֥ת\rb* \rb from Gath-hepher.|הַחֵֽפֶר׃\rb* \v 26 \rb For|כִּי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saw|רָאָ֧ה\rb* \rb that the affliction|עֳנִ֥י\rb* \rb of the Israelites,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb both slave|עָצוּר֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֶ֣פֶס\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֤פֶס\rb* \rb free,|עָז֔וּב\rb* \rb was very|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb bitter.|מֹרֶ֣ה\rb* \rb There was no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one to help|עֹזֵ֖ר\rb* \rb Israel,|לְיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 27 \rb and since the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had said|דִבֶּ֣ר\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb that He would not blot out|לִמְחוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb from under|מִתַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb heaven,|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb He saved them|וַיּ֣וֹשִׁיעֵ֔ם\rb* \rb by the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֥ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jehoash.|יוֹאָֽשׁ׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶתֶר֩\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Jeroboam,|יָרָבְעָ֜ם\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb and might,|וּגְבוּרָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb and how|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he waged war|נִלְחָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb and recovered|הֵשִׁ֜יב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הֲלֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb both Damascus|דַּמֶּ֧שֶׂק\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Hamath|חֲמָ֛ת\rb* \rb for Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb from Judah,|לִיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb And Jeroboam|יָֽרָבְעָם֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers,|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb*\f + \fr 14:29 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts include \fqa and he was buried in Samaria with\f*\rb |עִ֖ם\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb And his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\c 15
\s1 Azariah Reigns in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 26:3–23|2CH 26:3-23\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the twenty-seventh|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָשֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Jeroboam’s|לְיָרָבְעָ֖ם\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Azariah|עֲזַרְיָ֥ה\rb*\f + \fr 15:1 \fqa Azariah \ft is also called \fqa Uzziah\ft ; also in verses 6, 7, 8, 17, 23, and 27; see 2 Chronicles 26:1.\f* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb He was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb sixteen|שֵׁ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb fifty-two|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Jecoliah;|יְכָלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb she was from Jerusalem.|מִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Amaziah|אֲמַצְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb had done.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Nevertheless,|רַ֥ק\rb* \rb the high places|הַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb were not|לֹא־\rb* \rb taken away;|סָ֑רוּ\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֛ם\rb* \rb continued|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb sacrificing|מְזַבְּחִ֥ים\rb* \rb and burning incense|וּֽמְקַטְּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb there.|בַּבָּמֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb afflicted|וַיְנַגַּ֨ע\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֗לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb with leprosy|מְצֹרָע֙\rb*\f + \fr 15:5 \fqa Leprosy\ft was a term used for various skin diseases; see \ref Leviticus 13|LEV 13\ref*.\f* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb the day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb he died,|מֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb so that he lived|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb* \rb in a separate|הַחָפְשִׁ֑ית\rb* \rb house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb while his|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Jotham|וְיוֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb had charge of|עַל־\rb* \rb the palace|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb and governed|שֹׁפֵ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Azariah,|עֲזַרְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments,|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*\rb |הֲלֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb And Azariah|עֲזַרְיָה֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקְבְּר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb near|עִם־\rb* \rb them|אֲבֹתָ֖יו\rb*\f + \fr 15:7 \ft Literally \fqa with his fathers\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 26:23.\f* \rb in the City|בְּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of David.|דָּוִ֑ד\rb* \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jotham|יוֹתָ֥ם\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 Zechariah Reigns in Israel
\p \v 8 \rb In the thirty-eighth|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁמֹנֶה֙\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Azariah’s|לַעֲזַרְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Zechariah|זְכַרְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb* \rb became king|מָ֠לַךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and he reigned in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb six|שִׁשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb months.|חֳדָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 9 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֙\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb had done.|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb* \rb He did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֗ר\rb* \rb from the sins that|מֵֽחַטֹּאות֙\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֔ט\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to commit.|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Then Shallum|שַׁלֻּ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jabesh|יָבֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb conspired|וַיִּקְשֹׁ֤ר\rb* \rb against Zechariah,|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb struck him down|וַיַּכֵּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb in front of|קָֽבָלְ־\rb* \rb the people,|עָ֖ם\rb*\f + \fr 15:10 \ft Hebrew; some LXX manuscripts \fqa in Ibleam\f* \rb and reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֖תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zechariah,|זְכַרְיָ֑ה\rb* \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 12 \rb |ה֣וּא\rb* \rb So the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb spoken|דִּבֶּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jehu|יֵהוּא֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb was fulfilled:|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb “Four generations|רְבִיעִ֔ים\rb* \rb of your sons|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb will sit|יֵשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the throne|כִּסֵּ֣א\rb* \rb of Israel.”|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*
\s1 Shallum Reigns in Israel
\p \v 13 \rb In the thirty-ninth|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֙שַׁע֙\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Uzziah’s|לְעֻזִיָּ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 15:13 \fqa Uzziah \ft is also called \fqa Azariah\ft ; also in verses 32 and 34; see verse 1.\f* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Shallum|שַׁלּ֤וּם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jabesh|יָבֵישׁ֙\rb* \rb became king,|מָלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and he reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb one full month.|יֶֽרַח־\rb*\rb |יָמִ֖ים\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then Menahem|מְנַחֵ֨ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Gadi|גָּדִ֜י\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּעַל֩\rb* \rb from Tirzah|מִתִּרְצָ֗ה\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to Samaria,|שֹׁמְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb struck down|וַיַּ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and killed|וַיְמִיתֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb Shallum|שַׁלּ֥וּם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jabesh,|יָבֵ֖ישׁ\rb*\rb |בְּשֹׁמְר֑וֹן\rb* \rb and reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Shallum,|שַׁלּ֔וּם\rb* \rb along with the conspiracy|וְקִשְׁר֖וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he led,|קָשָׁ֑ר\rb* \rb they are indeed|הִנָּ֣ם\rb* \rb written|כְּתֻבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb At that time|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Menahem,|מְ֠נַחֵם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb starting from Tirzah,|מִתִּרְצָ֔ה\rb* \rb attacked|יַכֶּֽה־\rb* \rb Tiphsah|תִּפְסַ֨ח\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb* \rb in its|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb vicinity,|גְּבוּלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they would not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb open their gates.|פָתַ֖ח\rb* \rb So he attacked Tiphsah|וַיַּ֑ךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and ripped open|בִּקֵּֽעַ׃פ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the pregnant women.|הֶהָ֥רוֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\s1 Menahem Reigns in Israel
\p \v 17 \rb In the thirty-ninth|שְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֙שַׁע֙\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Azariah’s|לַעֲזַרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Menahem|מְנַחֵ֨ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Gadi|גָּדִ֧י\rb* \rb became king|מָ֠לַךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and he reigned in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנִ֖ים\rb* \v 18 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and throughout|כָּל־\rb* \rb his reign|יָמָֽיו׃\rb* \rb he did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֠ר\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֨ל\rb* \rb the sins that|חַטֹּ֜אות\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֧ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֛ט\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to commit.|הֶחֱטִ֥יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb Then Pul|פ֤וּל\rb*\f + \fr 15:19 \fqa Pul \ft is another name for \fqa Tiglath-pileser\ft ; see verse 29.\f* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb* \rb invaded|בָּ֣א\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb the land,|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb and Menahem|מְנַחֵם֙\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb Pul|לְפ֔וּל\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֖לֶף\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כָּ֑סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 15:19 \fqa \ref 1,000|0\ref* talents\ft is \ref approximately 37|37\ref*.7 tons or 34.2 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb in order to gain his support|לִהְי֤וֹת\rb*\rb |יָדָיו֙\rb*\rb |אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and strengthen|לְהַחֲזִ֥יק\rb* \rb his own grip|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb on the kingdom.|הַמַּמְלָכָ֖ה\rb* \v 20 \rb Menahem|מְנַחֵ֨ם\rb* \rb exacted|וַיֹּצֵא֩\rb* \rb this money|הַכֶּ֜סֶף\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb*\rb |עַ֚ל\rb* \rb each|כָּל־\rb* \rb of the wealthy|הַחַ֔יִל\rb* \rb men|גִּבּוֹרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel—|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*  \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֧ים\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֛ים\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 15:20 \fqa \ref 50|0\ref* shekels\ft is \ref approximately 1|1\ref*.26 pounds or 569.8 grams of silver.\f* \rb from each|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb man—|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb*  \rb to give|לָתֵת֙\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb withdrew|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb remain|עָ֥מַד\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb in the land.|בָּאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Menahem,|מְנַחֵ֖ם\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments,|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*\rb |הֲלוֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel?|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
