\s1 Pekahiah Reigns in Israel
\p \v 23 \rb In the fiftieth|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Azariah’s|לַעֲזַרְיָ֖ה\rb* \rb reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Judah,|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb Pekahiah|פְּקַֽחְיָ֨ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Menahem|מְנַחֵ֧ם\rb* \rb became king|מָ֠לַךְ\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and reigned in Samaria|בְּשֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb two years.|שְׁנָתָֽיִם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb turn away|סָ֗ר\rb* \rb from the sins that|מֵֽחַטֹּאות֙\rb* \rb Jeroboam|יָרָבְעָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nebat|נְבָ֔ט\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had caused Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb to commit.|הֶחֱטִ֖יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Then his officer,|שָׁלִישׁ֗וֹ\rb* \rb Pekah|פֶּ֨קַח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah,|רְמַלְיָ֜הוּ\rb* \rb conspired|וַיִּקְשֹׁ֣ר\rb* \rb against him|עָלָיו֩\rb* \rb along with|אֶת־\rb* \rb Argob,|אַרְגֹּ֣ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Arieh,|הָאַרְיֵ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְעִמּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb Gilead.|גִלְעָדִ֑ים\rb* \rb And at the citadel|בְּאַרְמ֤וֹן\rb* \rb of the king’s|מֶלֶךְ\rb* \rb palace|בֵּית־\rb* \rb in Samaria,|בְשֹׁמְר֜וֹן\rb* \rb Pekah struck down|וַיַּכֵּ֨הוּ\rb* \rb and killed Pekahiah|וַיְמִיתֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb and reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*
