\p \v 1 \rb In the seventeenth|שְׁבַֽע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Pekah|לְפֶ֖קַח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah,|רְמַלְיָ֑הוּ\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֥ז\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Jotham|יוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֣ז\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb sixteen|וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb And unlike David|כְּדָוִ֥ד\rb* \rb his father,|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb he did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb do|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֗ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb his God.|אֱלֹהָ֖יו\rb* \v 3 \rb Instead, he walked|וַיֵּ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb in the ways|בְּדֶ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and even|וְגַ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sacrificed|הֶעֱבִ֣יר\rb* \rb his son|בְּנוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the fire,|בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 16:3 \ft Literally \fqa made his son pass through the fire\f* \rb according to the abominations|כְּתֹֽעֲבוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had driven out|הוֹרִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 4 \rb And he sacrificed|וַיְזַבֵּ֧חַ\rb* \rb and burned incense|וַיְקַטֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb on the high places,|בַּבָּמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the hills,|הַגְּבָע֑וֹת\rb* \rb and under|וְתַ֖חַת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb green|רַעֲנָֽן׃\rb* \rb tree.|עֵ֥ץ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Then|אָ֣ז\rb* \rb Rezin|רְצִ֣ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲ֠רָם\rb* \rb and Pekah|וּפֶ֨קַח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Remaliah|רְמַלְיָ֧הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb came up|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to wage war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb against Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb They besieged|וַיָּצֻ֙רוּ֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֔ז\rb* \rb but could|יָכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb overcome him.|לְהִלָּחֵֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Rezin|רְצִ֨ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb recovered|הֵ֠שִׁיב\rb* \rb Elath|אֵילַת֙\rb*\f + \fr 16:6 \fqa Elath \ft is a variant of \fqa Eloth\ft ; \ref see 1|1\ref* Kings 9:26.\f* \rb for Aram,|לַֽאֲרָ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 16:6 \ft Or \fqa Syria\f* \rb drove out|וַיְנַשֵּׁ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the men of Judah,|הַיְהוּדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |מֵֽאֵיל֑וֹת\rb* \rb and sent|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb the Edomites|וַאֲרַמִּים\rb* \rb into Elath,|אֵילַ֔ת\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb they live|וַיֵּ֣שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃פ\rb* \rb day.|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb So Ahaz|אָחָ֜ז\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֨ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֗ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תִּ֠גְלַת\rb* \rb Tiglath-pileser|פְּלֶ֤סֶר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria,|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “I|אָ֑נִי\rb* \rb am your servant|עַבְדְּךָ֥\rb* \rb and your son.|וּבִנְךָ֖\rb* \rb Come up|עֲלֵ֨ה\rb* \rb and save me|וְהוֹשִׁעֵ֜נִי\rb* \rb from the hands|מִכַּ֣ף\rb* \rb of the kings|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Aram|אֲרָ֗ם\rb*\rb |וּמִכַּף֙\rb* \rb and|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb who are rising up|הַקּוֹמִ֖ים\rb* \rb against me.”|עָלָֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Ahaz|אָחָ֜ז\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also took|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֣סֶף\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and gold|הַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb found|הַנִּמְצָא֙\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in the treasuries|וּבְאֹֽצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the king’s|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and he sent it|וַיִּשְׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb as a gift|שֹֽׁחַד׃\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb* \v 9 \rb So the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb responded|וַיִּשְׁמַ֤ע\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָיו֙\rb* \rb marched up|וַיַּעַל֩\rb*\rb |מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אַשּׁ֤וּר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Damascus,|דַּמֶּ֙שֶׂק֙\rb* \rb and captured it.|וַֽיִּתְפְּשֶׂ֔הָ\rb* \rb He took its people|וַיַּגְלֶ֖הָ\rb* \rb to Kir as captives|קִ֑ירָה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb put Rezin|רְצִ֖ין\rb* \rb to death.|הֵמִֽית׃\rb*
