\s1 Samaria Resettled
\p \v 24 \rb Then the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֡וּר\rb* \rb brought|וַיָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb people from Babylon,|מִבָּבֶ֡ל\rb* \rb Cuthah,|וּ֠מִכּוּ֠תָה\rb* \rb Avva,|וּמֵעַוָּ֤א\rb* \rb Hamath,|וּמֵֽחֲמָת֙\rb* \rb and Sepharvaim|וּסְפַרְוַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and settled them|וַיֹּ֙שֶׁב֙\rb* \rb in the towns|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹֽׁמְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb to replace|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb They took possession of|וַיִּֽרְשׁוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Samaria|שֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb and lived|וַיֵּֽשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb in its towns.|בְּעָרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb when the settlers first|בִּתְחִלַּת֙\rb* \rb lived|שִׁבְתָּ֣ם\rb* \rb there,|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb worship|יָרְא֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb so He|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיְשַׁלַּ֨ח\rb* \rb lions|הָ֣אֲרָי֔וֹת\rb* \rb among them,|בָּהֶם֙\rb* \rb which|וַיִּֽהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb killed some|הֹרְגִ֖ים\rb* \rb of them.|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 26 \rb So they spoke|וַיֹּאמְר֗וּ\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria,|אַשּׁוּר֮\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹר֒\rb* \rb “The peoples|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you have removed|הִגְלִ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb and placed|וַתּ֙וֹשֶׁב֙\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Samaria|שֹׁמְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb know|יָֽדְע֔וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the requirements|מִשְׁפַּ֖ט\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the land.|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb Because of this,|כַּאֲשֶׁר֙\rb*\rb |אֵינָ֣ם\rb*\rb |יֹדְעִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |מִשְׁפַּ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb He has sent|וַיְשַׁלַּח־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lions|הָאֲרָי֗וֹת\rb* \rb among them,|בָּ֣ם\rb* \rb which are indeed|וְהִנָּם֙\rb* \rb killing them off.”|מְמִיתִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb Then the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֜וּר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb commanded:|וַיְצַ֨ו\rb* \rb “Send back|הֹלִ֤יכוּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb of the priests|מֵהַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you carried off|הִגְלִיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb from Samaria,|מִשָּׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and have him go back|וְיֵלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb to live|וְיֵ֣שְׁבוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and teach|וְיֹרֵ֕ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the requirements|מִשְׁפַּ֖ט\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the land.”|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb Thus one|אֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb of the priests|מֵהַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they had carried away|הִגְלוּ֙\rb*\rb |מִשֹּׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֞א\rb* \rb and lived|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb*\rb |בְּבֵֽית־\rb* \rb in Bethel,|אֵ֑ל\rb*\rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb and he began to teach|מוֹרֶ֣ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb how|אֵ֖יךְ\rb* \rb they should worship|יִֽירְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb Nevertheless,|וַיִּהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb the people of each nation|גּ֥וֹי\rb*\rb |גּ֖וֹי\rb* \rb continued to make|עֹשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb their own gods|אֱלֹהָ֑יו\rb* \rb in the cities|בְּעָ֣רֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb had settled,|יֹשְׁבִ֖ים\rb* \rb and they set them up|וַיַּנִּ֣יחוּ׀\rb* \rb in the shrines|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the people|גּ֥וֹי\rb* \rb of Samaria|הַשֹּׁ֣מְרֹנִ֔ים\rb* \rb had made|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb on the high places.|הַבָּמ֗וֹת\rb* \v 30 \rb The men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb made|עָשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |סֻכּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb Succoth-benoth,|בְּנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb the men|וְאַנְשֵׁי־\rb* \rb of Cuth|כ֔וּת\rb* \rb made|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Nergal,|נֵֽרְגַ֑ל\rb* \rb the men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb of Hamath|חֲמָ֖ת\rb* \rb made|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Ashima,|אֲשִׁימָֽא׃\rb* \v 31 \rb the Avvites|וְהָעַוִּ֛ים\rb* \rb made|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb Nibhaz|נִבְחַ֖ז\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Tartak,|תַּרְתָּ֑ק\rb* \rb and the Sepharvites|וְהַסְפַרְוִ֗ים\rb* \rb burned|שֹׂרְפִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their children|בְּנֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb to Adrammelech|לְאַדְרַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Anammelech|וַֽעֲנַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהַּ\rb* \rb of Sepharvaim.|סְפָרִים׃\rb*
\p \v 32 \rb So|וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb the new residents worshiped|יְרֵאִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb but they also appointed|וַיַּעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb for themselves|לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of all sorts|מִקְצוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to serve|עֹשִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the shrines|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb*\rb |הַבָּמֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb of the high places.|בָמ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |וַיִּהְי֛וּ\rb* \v 33 \rb |הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb They worshiped|יְרֵאִ֑ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb but they also served|עֹֽבְדִ֔ים\rb* \rb their own gods|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb according to the customs|כְּמִשְׁפַּט֙\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb from which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they had been carried away.|הִגְל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |מִשָּֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 34 \rb To|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֤וֹם\rb* \rb they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are still practicing|עֹשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb their former|הָרִֽאשֹׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb customs.|כַּמִּשְׁפָּטִ֖ים\rb* \rb None|אֵינָ֤ם\rb* \rb of them worship|יְרֵאִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְאֵינָ֣ם\rb* \rb or observe|עֹשִׂ֗ים\rb* \rb the statutes,|כְּחֻקֹּתָם֙\rb* \rb ordinances,|וּכְמִשְׁפָּטָ֔ם\rb* \rb laws,|וְכַתּוֹרָ֣ה\rb* \rb and commandments|וְכַמִּצְוָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|צִוָּ֤ה\rb* \rb the descendants|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jacob,|יַעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb whom He named|שָׂ֥ם\rb*\rb |שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb For the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb had made|וַיִּכְרֹ֨ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb with the Israelites|אִתָּם֙\rb* \rb and commanded them,|וַיְצַוֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb worship|תִֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֑ים\rb* \rb gods|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb bow down|תִשְׁתַּחֲו֣וּ\rb* \rb to them;|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb serve them|תַעַבְד֔וּם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb sacrifice|תִזְבְּח֖וּ\rb* \rb to them.|לָהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 36 \rb Instead,|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִֽם־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb worship|תִירָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb brought|הֶעֱלָ֨ה\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb with great|גָּד֛וֹל\rb* \rb power|בְּכֹ֧חַ\rb* \rb and an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb arm.|וּבִזְר֥וֹעַ\rb* \rb You are to bow down|תִֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb to Him|וְל֥וֹ\rb* \rb and offer sacrifices to Him.|תִזְבָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \v 37 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb you must always|כָּל־\rb* \rb be careful|תִּשְׁמְר֥וּן\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb to observe|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the statutes,|הַחֻקִּ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb ordinances,|הַמִּשְׁפָּטִ֜ים\rb* \rb laws,|וְהַתּוֹרָ֤ה\rb* \rb and commandments|וְהַמִּצְוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He wrote|כָּתַ֣ב\rb* \rb for you.|לָכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb Do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb worship|תִֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb* \rb gods.|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \v 38 \rb Do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb forget|תִשְׁכָּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb the covenant|וְהַבְּרִ֛ית\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have made|כָּרַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb with you.|אִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb Do not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb worship|תִֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִֽים׃\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb* \v 39 \rb but|כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִֽם־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb worship|תִּירָ֑אוּ\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and He|וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb will deliver|יַצִּ֣יל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your enemies.”|אֹיְבֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*
