\c 18
\s1 Hezekiah Destroys Idolatry in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 29:1–2|2CH 29:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb In the third|שָׁלֹ֔שׁ\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Hoshea|לְהוֹשֵׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Elah|אֵלָ֖ה\rb* \rb over Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Ahaz|אָחָ֖ז\rb* \rb became king|מָלַ֛ךְ\rb*\rb |מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb He was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb twenty-nine|וְעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָתֵ֙שַׁע֙\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Abi,|אֲבִ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 18:2 \fqa Abi \ft is a variant of \fqa Abijah\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 29:1.\f* \rb the daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Zechariah.|זְכַרְיָֽה׃\rb* \v 3 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb David|דָּוִ֥ד\rb* \rb had done.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \v 4 \rb |ה֣וּא׀\rb* \rb He removed|הֵסִ֣יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the high places,|הַבָּמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb shattered|וְשִׁבַּר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sacred pillars,|הַמַּצֵּבֹ֔ת\rb* \rb and cut down|וְכָרַ֖ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Asherah poles.|הָֽאֲשֵׁרָ֑ה\rb* \rb He also demolished|וְכִתַּת֩\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֜שֶׁת\rb* \rb snake|נְחַ֨שׁ\rb* \rb called|וַיִּקְרָא־\rb* \rb Nehushtan|נְחֻשְׁתָּֽן׃\rb*\f + \fr 18:4 \fqa Nehushtan \ft sounds like the Hebrew for \fqa bronze \ft and also for \fqa snake\ft .\f* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֗ה\rb* \rb had made,|עָשָׂ֣ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb up to|עַד־\rb* \rb that|הָהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb*\rb |הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb time|הַיָּמִ֤ים\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb had burned incense|מְקַטְּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to it.|ל֔וֹ\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Hezekiah trusted|בָּטָ֑ח\rb* \rb in the LORD,|בַּיהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb No|לֹא־\rb* \rb king|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb like him,|כָמֹ֗הוּ\rb*\rb |בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb either before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb or after him.|וְאַחֲרָ֞יו\rb* \v 6 \rb He remained faithful|וַיִּדְבַּק֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|בַּֽיהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb turn|סָ֖ר\rb* \rb from following Him;|מֵאַֽחֲרָ֑יו\rb* \rb he kept|וַיִּשְׁמֹר֙\rb* \rb the commandments|מִצְוֺתָ֔יו\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had given|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb Moses.|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb with Hezekiah,|עִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he prospered|יַשְׂכִּ֑יל\rb* \rb wherever|בְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he went.|יֵצֵ֖א\rb* \rb He rebelled|וַיִּמְרֹ֥ד\rb* \rb against the king|בְּמֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb* \rb and refused|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to serve him.|עֲבָדֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 8 \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb defeated|הִכָּ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֛ים\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as Gaza|עַזָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and its borders,|גְּבוּלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb from|מִמִּגְדַּ֥ל\rb* \rb watchtower|נוֹצְרִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb fortified|מִבְצָֽר׃פ\rb* \rb city.|עִ֥יר\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb |וַֽיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb In the fourth|הָֽרְבִיעִית֙\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֤ה\rb* \rb of Hezekiah’s|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb reign,|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb which|הִ֚יא\rb* \rb was the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֔ית\rb* \rb year|הַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb of the reign|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Hoshea|לְהוֹשֵׁ֥עַ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Elah|אֵלָ֖ה\rb* \rb over Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb Shalmaneser|שַׁלְמַנְאֶ֧סֶר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֛וּר\rb* \rb marched|עָלָ֞ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Samaria|שֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb and besieged|וַיָּ֥צַר\rb* \rb it.|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 10 \rb And at the end|מִקְצֵה֙\rb* \rb of three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb the Assyrians captured it.|וַֽיִּלְכְּדֻ֗הָ\rb*
\p \rb So Samaria|שֹׁמְרֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb was captured|נִלְכְּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the sixth|שֵׁ֖שׁ\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַת־\rb* \rb of Hezekiah,|לְחִזְקִיָּ֑ה\rb* \rb which|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb was the ninth|תֵּ֗שַׁע\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַת־\rb* \rb of Hoshea|לְהוֹשֵׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \v 11 \rb The king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֛וּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb exiled|וַיֶּ֧גֶל\rb* \rb the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb to Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּרָה\rb* \rb and settled them|וַיַּנְחֵ֞ם\rb* \rb in Halah,|בַּחְלַ֧ח\rb* \rb in Gozan|גּוֹזָ֖ן\rb* \rb by the Habor|וּבְחָב֛וֹר\rb* \rb River,|נְהַ֥ר\rb* \rb and in the cities|וְעָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the Medes.|מָדָֽי׃\rb* \v 12 \rb This happened because|עַ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְע֗וּ\rb* \rb to the voice|בְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb their God,|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb but violated|וַיַּעַבְרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb His covenant—|בְּרִית֔וֹ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶׁ֖ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶ֣בֶד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb had commanded—|צִוָּ֔ה\rb*  \rb and would neither|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb nor|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb obey.|עָשֽׂוּ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Sennacherib Invades Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 32:1–8|2CH 32:1-8\ref*; \ref Psalm 46:1–11|PSA 46:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 13 \rb In the fourteenth|וּבְאַרְבַּע֩\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֨ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֜ה\rb* \rb of Hezekiah’s|חִזְקִיָּ֗ה\rb* \rb reign,|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֤יב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb* \rb attacked|עָלָ֞ה\rb*\rb |עַ֣ל\rb* \rb and captured|וַֽיִּתְפְּשֵֽׂם׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fortified|הַבְּצֻר֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרֵ֧י\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֛ה\rb* \v 14 \rb So Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֣ה\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb word to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁוּר֩׀\rb* \rb at Lachish,|לָכִ֨ישָׁה׀\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹ֤ר׀\rb* \rb “I have done wrong;|חָטָ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb withdraw|שׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb from me,|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and I will pay|אֶשָּׂ֑א\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you demand|תִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb from me.”|עָלַ֖י\rb*
\p \rb And the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֜וּר\rb* \rb exacted|וַיָּ֨שֶׂם\rb* \rb from|עַל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb hundred|מֵאוֹת֙\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֔סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 18:14 \fqa \ref 300|0\ref* talents\ft is \ref approximately 11|11\ref*.3 tons or 10.3 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb and thirty|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb talents|כִּכַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb*\f + \fr 18:14 \fqa \ref 30|0\ref* talents\ft is \ref approximately 1|1\ref*.13 tons or 1.03 metric tons of gold.\f* \v 15 \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave him|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb that was found|הַנִּמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb in the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and in the treasuries|וּבְאֹצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the royal|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \rb palace.|בֵּ֥ית\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb At that|הַהִ֗יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb stripped the gold|קִצַּ֨ץ\rb* \rb with which|חִזְקִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb he had plated|צִפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֨וֹת\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb doorposts|הָאֹ֣מְנ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb of the temple|הֵיכַ֤ל\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and he|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb gave it|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖ם\rb* \rb to the king|לְמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּֽׁוּר׃פ\rb*
\s1 Sennacherib Threatens Jerusalem
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 32:9–19|2CH 32:9-19\ref*; \ref Isaiah 36:1–22|ISA 36:1-22\ref*)
\p \v 17 \rb Nevertheless, the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֡וּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb the Tartan,|תַּרְתָּ֥ן\rb*\f + \fr 18:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Tartan \ft is the title of a field marshal, general, or commander in the Assyrian military.\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabsaris,|סָרִ֣יס׀\rb*\f + \fr 18:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabsaris \ft is the title of the chief eunuch in the Assyrian military.\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb and the Rabshakeh,|שָׁקֵ֨ה\rb*\f + \fr 18:17 \ft Hebrew \fqa Rabshakeh\ft is the title of a high-ranking Assyrian military officer; here and throughout \ref chapters 18|18\ref* and 19, as well as Isaiah 36 and 37.\f* \rb along with a great army,|כָּבֵ֖ד\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb Lachish|לָכִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb*\rb |בְּחֵ֥יל\rb* \rb at Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb They advanced up|וַֽיַּעֲלוּ֙\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֣אוּ\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*\rb |וַיַּעֲל֣וּ\rb*\rb |וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb and stationed themselves|וַיַּֽעַמְדוּ֙\rb* \rb by the aqueduct|בִּתְעָלַת֙\rb* \rb of the upper|הָֽעֶלְיוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb pool,|הַבְּרֵכָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֕ר\rb* \rb on the road|בִּמְסִלַּ֖ת\rb* \rb to the Launderer’s|כוֹבֵֽס׃\rb* \rb Field.|שְׂדֵ֥ה\rb* \v 18 \rb Then they called|וַֽיִּקְרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king.|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb And Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the palace|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb administrator,|עַל־\rb* \rb Shebnah|וְשֶׁבְנָה֙\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb and Joah|וְיוֹאָ֥ח\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Asaph|אָסָ֖ף\rb* \rb the recorder,|הַמַּזְכִּֽיר׃\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֧א\rb* \rb to them.|אֲלֵהֶ֛ם\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb |רַב־\rb* \rb The Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵהֶם֙\rb* \rb “Tell|אִמְרוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the great|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb king,|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria,|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb What|מָ֧ה\rb* \rb is the basis|בָּטָֽחְתָּ׃\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb confidence|הַבִּטָּח֛וֹן\rb* \rb of yours?|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \v 20 \rb You claim|אָמַ֙רְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to have a strategy|עֵצָ֥ה\rb* \rb and strength|וּגְבוּרָ֖ה\rb* \rb for war,|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb but|אַךְ־\rb* \rb these are empty|שְׂפָתַ֔יִם\rb* \rb words.|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb In|עַל־\rb* \rb whom|מִ֣י\rb* \rb are you now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb trusting,|בָטַ֔חְתָּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you have rebelled|מָרַ֖דְתָּ\rb* \rb against me?|בִּֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb Look|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb now,|עַתָּ֡ה\rb* \rb you are trusting|בָטַ֣חְתָּ\rb* \rb in Egypt,|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb that splintered|הָרָצ֤וּץ\rb*\rb |הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb reed|הַקָּנֶ֨ה\rb* \rb of a staff|מִשְׁעֶנֶת֩\rb*\rb |וּבָ֥א\rb* \rb that will pierce|וּנְקָבָ֑הּ\rb* \rb the hand|בְכַפּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of anyone|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb leans on it.|יִסָּמֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb Such is|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to all|לְכָֽל־\rb* \rb who trust|הַבֹּטְחִ֖ים\rb* \rb in him.|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 22 \rb But if|וְכִי־\rb* \rb you say|תֹאמְר֣וּן\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb ‘We trust|בָּטָ֑חְנוּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb our God,’|אֱלֹהֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb is He|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb not|הֲלוֹא־\rb* \rb the One|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb whose high places|בָּמֹתָ֣יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and altars|מִזְבְּחֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has removed,|הֵסִ֤יר\rb* \rb saying|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to Judah|לִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and Jerusalem:|וְלִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb ‘You must worship|תִּֽשְׁתַּחֲו֖וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֣חַ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem’?|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Now, therefore,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb make a bargain|הִתְעָ֣רֶב\rb*\rb |נָ֔א\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb my master,|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb I will give|וְאֶתְּנָ֤ה\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb two thousand|אַלְפַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb horses—|סוּסִ֔ים\rb*  \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb you can|תּוּכַ֕ל\rb* \rb put|לָ֥תֶת\rb* \rb riders|רֹכְבִ֥ים\rb* \rb on them!|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb For how|וְאֵ֣יךְ\rb* \rb can you repel|תָּשִׁ֗יב\rb*\rb |אֵ֠ת\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb a single|אַחַ֛ד\rb* \rb officer|פַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb among the least|הַקְּטַנִּ֑ים\rb* \rb of my master’s|אֲדֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb servants|עַבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb when you depend|וַתִּבְטַ֤ח\rb*\rb |לְךָ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb for chariots|לְרֶ֖כֶב\rb* \rb and horsemen?|וּלְפָרָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \v 25 \rb So now,|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb was it apart from|הֲמִבַּלְעֲדֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that I have come up|עָלִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb to destroy it?|לְהַשְׁחִת֑וֹ\rb* \rb The LORD Himself|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to me,|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb ‘Go up|עֲלֵ֛ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֖את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb and destroy it.’”|וְהַשְׁחִיתָֽהּ׃\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Then Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Hilkiah,|חִ֠לְקִיָּהוּ\rb* \rb along with Shebnah|וְשֶׁבְנָ֨ה\rb* \rb and Joah,|וְיוֹאָ֜ח\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabshakeh,|שָׁקֵ֗ה\rb* \rb “Please|נָ֤א\rb* \rb speak|דַּבֶּר־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your servants|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb in Aramaic,|אֲרָמִ֔ית\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb we|אֲנָ֑חְנוּ\rb* \rb understand it.|שֹׁמְעִ֖ים\rb* \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb speak|תְּדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb with us|עִמָּ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb in Hebrew|יְהוּדִ֔ית\rb*\f + \fr 18:26 \ft Or \fqa in the dialect of Judah\ft ; also in verse 28\f* \rb in the hearing|בְּאָזְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall.”|הַחֹמָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 27 \rb |רַב־\rb* \rb But the Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֗ה\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb “Has my master|אֲדֹנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb sent me|שְׁלָחַ֣נִי\rb* \rb to speak|לְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb words|הַדְּבָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb only to|הַעַ֨ל\rb* \rb you and|וְאֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb your master,|אֲדֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb and not|הֲלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb sitting|הַיֹּֽשְׁבִים֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the wall,|הַ֣חֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb who are destined with you|עִמָּכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכֹ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת\rb* \rb their own dung|חֲרֵיהֶם\rb* \rb and drink|וְלִשְׁתּ֛וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their own urine?”|שֵׁינֵיהֶם\rb*
\p \v 28 \rb |רַב־\rb* \rb Then the Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֔ה\rb* \rb stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb and called out|וַיִּקְרָ֥א\rb* \rb loudly|בְקוֹל־\rb*\rb |גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb in Hebrew:|יְהוּדִ֑ית\rb*\rb |וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֔אמֶר\rb* \rb “Hear|שִׁמְע֛וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb king,|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria!|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb* \v 29 \rb This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb deceive|יַשִּׁ֥יא\rb* \rb you;|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb he cannot|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֔ל\rb* \rb deliver|לְהַצִּ֥יל\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand.|מִיָּדֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 30 \rb Do not|וְאַל־\rb* \rb let Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb persuade you to trust|יַבְטַ֨ח\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb when he says,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb will surely deliver us;|הַצֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |יַצִּילֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb be given|תִנָּתֵן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.’|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb*
\p \v 31 \rb Do not|אַֽל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֨ה\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֗וּר\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֜ר\rb* \rb Make|עֲשֽׂוּ־\rb* \rb peace|בְרָכָה֙\rb* \rb with me|אִתִּ֤י\rb*\f + \fr 18:31 \ft Or \fqa Make a blessing with me\f* \rb and come out|וּצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb to me.|אֵלַ֔י\rb* \rb Then every one of you|אִישׁ־\rb* \rb will eat|וְאִכְל֤וּ\rb* \rb from his own vine|גַּפְנוֹ֙\rb* \rb and his own fig tree|תְּאֵֽנָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb drink|וּשְׁת֖וּ\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb water|מֵֽי־\rb* \rb from his own cistern,|בוֹרֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 32 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb I come|בֹּאִי֩\rb* \rb and take you away|וְלָקַחְתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb like your own—|כְּאַרְצְכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb a land|אֶרֶץ֩\rb* \rb of grain|דָּגָ֨ן\rb* \rb and new wine,|וְתִיר֜וֹשׁ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb of bread|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb and vineyards,|וּכְרָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of olive trees|זֵ֤ית\rb*\rb |יִצְהָר֙\rb* \rb and honey—|וּדְבַ֔שׁ\rb* \rb so that you may live|וִֽחְי֖וּ\rb* \rb and not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb die.|תָמֻ֑תוּ\rb* \rb But do not|וְאַֽל־\rb* \rb listen|תִּשְׁמְעוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he misleads you|יַסִּ֤ית\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb when he says,|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb ‘The LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will deliver us.’|יַצִּילֵֽנוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb Has the god|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of any|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb nation|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb ever delivered|הַהַצֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |הִצִּ֛ילוּ\rb* \rb his land|אַרְצ֑וֹ\rb* \rb from the hand|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria?|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb* \v 34 \rb Where|אַיֵּה֩\rb* \rb are the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Hamath|חֲמָ֜ת\rb* \rb and Arpad?|וְאַרְפָּ֗ד\rb* \rb Where|אַיֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb are the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Sepharvaim,|סְפַרְוַ֖יִם\rb* \rb Hena,|הֵנַ֣ע\rb* \rb and Ivvah?|וְעִוָּ֑ה\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb* \rb Have they delivered|הִצִּ֥ילוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Samaria|שֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb from my hand?|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb* \v 35 \rb Who|מִ֚י\rb* \rb among all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of these lands|הָֽאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb has delivered|הִצִּ֥ילוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his land|אַרְצָ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand?|מִיָּדִ֑י\rb*\rb |כִּי־\rb* \rb How then can the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb deliver|יַצִּ֧יל\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb from my hand?”|מִיָּדִֽי׃\rb*
\p \v 36 \rb But the people|הָעָ֔ם\rb* \rb remained silent|וְהֶחֱרִ֣ישׁוּ\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb answer|עָנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb a word,|דָּבָ֑ר\rb* \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |הִ֛יא\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb* \rb had commanded,|מִצְוַ֨ת\rb* \rb “Do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb answer him.”|תַעֲנֻֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb Then Hilkiah’s|חִלְקִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the palace|הַ֠בַּיִת\rb* \rb administrator,|עַל־\rb* \rb Shebna|וְשֶׁבְנָ֨א\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֜ר\rb* \rb and Asaph’s|אָסָ֧ף\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb Joah|וְיוֹאָ֨ח\rb* \rb the recorder|הַמַּזְכִּ֛יר\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb with their clothes|בְגָדִ֑ים\rb* \rb torn,|קְרוּעֵ֣י\rb* \rb and they relayed|וַיַּגִּ֣דוּ\rb* \rb to him|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb of the Rabshakeh.|שָׁקֵֽה׃\rb*
\c 19
\s1 Isaiah’s Message of Deliverance
\r \ref Isaiah 37:1–7|ISA 37:1-7\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb On|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb hearing this report,|כִּשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb tore|וַיִּקְרַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes,|בְּגָדָ֑יו\rb* \rb put on|וַיִּתְכַּ֣ס\rb* \rb sackcloth,|בַּשָּׂ֔ק\rb* \rb and entered|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And he sent|וַ֠יִּשְׁלַח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the palace|הַבַּ֜יִת\rb* \rb administrator,|עַל־\rb* \rb Shebna|וְשֶׁבְנָ֣א\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֗ר\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and the leading|זִקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb priests,|הַכֹּֽהֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb all wearing|מִתְכַּסִּ֖ים\rb* \rb sackcloth,|בַּשַּׂקִּ֑ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Amoz|אָמֽוֹץ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb to tell|וַיֹּאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb him,|אֵלָ֗יו\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb Today|יוֹם־\rb*\rb |הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb is a day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb of distress,|צָרָ֧ה\rb* \rb rebuke,|וְתוֹכֵחָ֛ה\rb* \rb and disgrace;|וּנְאָצָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb children|בָנִים֙\rb* \rb have come|בָ֤אוּ\rb* \rb to the point of|עַד־\rb* \rb birth,|מַשְׁבֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb but there is no|אַ֖יִן\rb* \rb strength|וְכֹ֥חַ\rb* \rb to deliver them.|לְלֵדָֽה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֡י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֜יךָ\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb will hear|יִשְׁמַע֩\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb of the Rabshakeh,|שָׁקֵ֗ה\rb* \rb whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb his master|אֲדֹנָיו֙\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֤וּר׀\rb* \rb has sent|שְׁלָח֨וֹ\rb* \rb to defy|לְחָרֵף֙\rb* \rb the living|חַ֔י\rb* \rb God,|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb and He will rebuke him|וְהוֹכִ֙יחַ֙\rb* \rb for the words|בַּדְּבָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb has heard.|שָׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb Therefore lift up|וְנָשָׂ֣אתָ\rb* \rb a prayer|תְפִלָּ֔ה\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb the remnant|הַשְּׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb that still survives.”|הַנִּמְצָאָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb So the servants|עַבְדֵ֛י\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֗אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Isaiah,|יְשַֽׁעַיָֽהוּ׃\rb* \v 6 \rb who|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb “Tell|תֹאמְר֖וּן\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your master|אֲדֹֽנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb ‘Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָא֙\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb the words|הַדְּבָרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have heard,|שָׁמַ֗עְתָּ\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb the servants|נַעֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb* \rb have blasphemed|גִּדְּפ֛וּ\rb* \rb Me.|אֹתִֽי׃\rb* \v 7 \rb Behold,|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I will put|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb a spirit|ר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb in him|בּוֹ֙\rb* \rb so that he will hear|וְשָׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb a rumor|שְׁמוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb and return|וְשָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb to his own land,|לְאַרְצ֑וֹ\rb* \rb where|בְּאַרְצֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb I will cause him to fall|וְהִפַּלְתִּ֥יו\rb* \rb by the sword.’”|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb*
\s1 Sennacherib’s Blasphemous Letter
\r \ref Isaiah 37:8–13|ISA 37:8-13\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb When|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |רַב־\rb* \rb the Rabshakeh|שָׁקֵ֔ה\rb* \rb heard|שָׁמַ֔ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb had left|נָסַ֖ע\rb* \rb Lachish,|מִלָּכִֽישׁ׃\rb* \rb he withdrew|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb and found|וַיִּמְצָא֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king fighting|נִלְחָ֖ם\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Libnah.|לִבְנָ֑ה\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb Now Sennacherib had been warned|וַיִּשְׁמַ֗ע\rb* \rb about|אֶל־\rb* \rb Tirhakah|תִּרְהָ֤קָה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶך־\rb* \rb of Cush:|כּוּשׁ֙\rb*\f + \fr 19:9 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* \rb “Look,|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb he has set out|יָצָ֖א\rb* \rb to fight|לְהִלָּחֵ֣ם\rb* \rb against you.”|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*
\p \rb So Sennacherib again|וַיָּ֙שָׁב֙\rb* \rb sent|וַיִּשְׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֔ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 10 \rb “Give this message|תֹאמְר֗וּן\rb*\rb |כֹּ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֤הוּ\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah:|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*
\pmo \rb ‘Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb let your God,|אֱלֹהֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb in whom|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb trust,|בֹּטֵ֥חַ\rb* \rb deceive you|יַשִּׁאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb by saying|לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb that Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb be delivered|תִנָּתֵן֙\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּֽׁוּר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb Surely|הִנֵּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb have heard|שָׁמַ֗עְתָּ\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֛וּר\rb* \rb have done|עָשׂ֜וּ\rb* \rb to all the other|לְכָל־\rb* \rb countries,|הָאֲרָצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb devoting them to destruction.|לְהַֽחֲרִימָ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 19:11 \ft Forms of the Hebrew \fqa cherem \ft refer to the giving over of things or persons to the LORD, either by destroying them or by giving them as an offering.\f* \rb Will you then|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb be spared?|תִּנָּצֵֽל׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Did the gods|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb destroyed|שִׁחֲת֣וּ\rb* \rb by my fathers|אֲבוֹתַ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb rescue those nations—|הַהִצִּ֨ילוּ\rb* \rb the gods of|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb Gozan,|גּוֹזָ֖ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Haran,|חָרָ֑ן\rb* \rb and Rezeph,|וְרֶ֥צֶף\rb* \rb and of the people|וּבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֶ֖דֶן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb in Telassar?|בִּתְלַאשָּֽׂר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb Where|אַיּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb are the kings|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Hamath,|חֲמָת֙\rb*\rb |וּמֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Arpad,|אַרְפָּ֔ד\rb*\rb |וּמֶ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb Sepharvaim,|סְפַרְוָ֑יִם\rb* \rb Hena,|הֵנַ֖ע\rb* \rb and Ivvah?’”|וְעִוָּֽה׃\rb*
\s1 Hezekiah’s Prayer
\r \ref Isaiah 37:14–20|ISA 37:14-20\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb So Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֧הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb received|וַיִּקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb the letter|הַסְּפָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb from|מִיַּ֥ד\rb* \rb the messengers,|הַמַּלְאָכִ֖ים\rb* \rb read it,|וַיִּקְרָאֵ֑ם\rb* \rb and went up to|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and spread it out|וַיִּפְרְשֵׂ֥הוּ\rb*\rb |חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb* \v 15 \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb prayed|וַיִּתְפַּלֵּ֨ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD:|יְהוָה֮\rb*\rb |וַיֹּאמַר֒\rb*
\pmo \rb “O LORD,|יְהוָ֞ה\rb* \rb God|אֱלֹהֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb enthroned|יֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb between the cherubim,|הַכְּרֻבִ֔ים\rb* \rb You|אַתָּה־\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדְּךָ֔\rb*\rb |ה֤וּא\rb* \rb are God|הָֽאֱלֹהִים֙\rb* \rb over all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth.|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb made|עָשִׂ֔יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the earth.|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \v 16 \rb Incline|הַטֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb Your ear,|אָזְנְךָ֙\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb and hear;|וּֽשֲׁמָ֔ע\rb* \rb open|פְּקַ֧ח\rb* \rb Your eyes,|עֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb and see.|וּרְאֵ֑ה\rb* \rb Listen to|וּשְׁמַ֗ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֔יב\rb* \rb has sent|שְׁלָח֔וֹ\rb* \rb to defy|לְחָרֵ֖ף\rb* \rb the living|חָֽי׃\rb* \rb God.|אֱלֹהִ֥ים\rb*
\pmo \v 17 \rb Truly,|אָמְנָ֖ם\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֛וּר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have laid waste|הֶחֱרִ֜יבוּ\rb* \rb these nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and their lands.|אַרְצָֽם׃\rb* \v 18 \rb They have cast|וְנָתְנ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their gods|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into the fire|בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb* \rb and destroyed them,|וַֽיְאַבְּדֽוּם׃\rb* \rb for|כִּי֩\rb* \rb they|הֵ֗מָּה\rb* \rb were not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb gods,|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb* \rb but|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb only|אִם־\rb* \rb wood|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb and stone—|וָאֶ֖בֶן\rb*  \rb the work|מַעֲשֵׂ֧ה\rb* \rb of human|אָדָ֛ם\rb* \rb hands.|יְדֵֽי־\rb*
\pmo \v 19 \rb And now,|וְעַתָּה֙\rb* \rb O LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb our God,|אֱלֹהֵ֔ינוּ\rb* \rb please|נָ֖א\rb* \rb save us|הוֹשִׁיעֵ֥נוּ\rb* \rb from his hand,|מִיָּד֑וֹ\rb* \rb so that all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the kingdoms|מַמְלְכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb may know|וְיֵֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb You|אַתָּ֛ה\rb* \rb alone,|לְבַדֶּֽךָ׃ס\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb are God.”|אֱלֹהִ֖ים\rb*
\s1 Sennacherib’s Fall Prophesied
\r \ref Isaiah 37:21–35|ISA 37:21-35\ref*)
