\p \v 35 \rb And|וַיְהִי֮\rb* \rb that very|הַהוּא֒\rb* \rb night|בַּלַּ֣יְלָה\rb* \rb the angel|מַלְאַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּצֵ֣א׀\rb* \rb and struck down|וַיַּךְ֙\rb* \rb 185,000 men|מֵאָ֛ה\rb*\rb |שְׁמוֹנִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb in the camp|בְּמַחֲנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the Assyrians.|אַשּׁ֔וּר\rb* \rb When the people got up|וַיַּשְׁכִּ֣ימוּ\rb* \rb the next morning,|בַבֹּ֔קֶר\rb* \rb there|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb were all|כֻלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb the dead|מֵתִֽים׃\rb* \rb bodies!|פְּגָרִ֥ים\rb* \v 36 \rb So Sennacherib|סַנְחֵרִ֣יב\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֑וּר\rb* \rb broke camp|וַיִּסַּ֣ע\rb* \rb and withdrew.|וַיֵּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb He returned|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb to Nineveh|בְּנִֽינְוֵֽה׃\rb* \rb and stayed there.|וַיֵּ֖שֶׁב\rb*
\p \v 37 \rb One day,|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb while he|ה֨וּא\rb* \rb was worshiping|מִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֶ֜ה\rb* \rb in the temple|בֵּ֣ית׀\rb* \rb of his god|אֱלֹהָ֗יו\rb* \rb Nisroch,|נִסְרֹ֣ךְ\rb* \rb his sons Adrammelech|וְֽאַדְרַמֶּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb and Sharezer|וְשַׂרְאֶ֤צֶרָָ֙\rb*\f + \fr 19:37 \ft LXX and an alternate MT reading (see also \ref Isaiah 37:38|ISA 37:38\ref*); MT lacks \fqa his sons\ft .\f* \rb put him|הִכֻּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb to the sword|בַחֶ֔רֶב\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb and escaped|נִמְלְט֖וּ\rb* \rb to the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Ararat.|אֲרָרָ֑ט\rb* \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Esar-haddon|אֵֽסַר־\rb*\rb |חַדֹּ֥ן\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
