\p \v 1 \rb In those|הָהֵ֔ם\rb* \rb days|בַּיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb became mortally|לָמ֑וּת\rb* \rb ill.|חָלָ֥ה\rb* \rb The prophet|הַנָּבִ֗יא\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Amoz|אָמ֜וֹץ\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֣א\rb* \rb to him|אֵ֠לָיו\rb* \rb and said,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֜יו\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Put your house|לְבֵיתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb in order,|צַ֣ו\rb* \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are about to die;|מֵ֥ת\rb* \rb you will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb recover.’”|תִֽחְיֶֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb Then Hezekiah turned|וַיַּסֵּ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֖יו\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wall|הַקִּ֑יר\rb* \rb and prayed|וַיִּ֨תְפַּלֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 3 \rb “Please,|אָנָּ֣ה\rb* \rb O LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb remember|זְכָר־\rb*\rb |נָ֞א\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I have walked|הִתְהַלַּ֣כְתִּי\rb* \rb before You|לְפָנֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb faithfully|בֶּֽאֱמֶת֙\rb* \rb and with wholehearted|וּבְלֵבָ֣ב\rb* \rb devotion;|שָׁלֵ֔ם\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֑יתִי\rb* \rb what is good|וְהַטּ֥וֹב\rb* \rb in Your sight.”|בְּעֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |בְּכִ֥י\rb* \rb wept|וַיֵּ֥בְךְּ\rb* \rb bitterly.|גָדֽוֹל׃ס\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Before|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb had left|יָצָ֔א\rb* \rb the middle|הַתִּֽיכֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb courtyard,|הָעִיר\rb*\f + \fr 20:4 \ft LXX and an alternate MT reading; the other alternate reads \fqa the middle of the city\f* \rb the word|וּדְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to him,|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 5 \rb “Go back|שׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the leader|נְגִיד־\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֗י\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵי֙\rb* \rb of your father|אָבִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb David,|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘I have heard|שָׁמַ֙עְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your prayer;|תְּפִלָּתֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb I have seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your tears.|דִּמְעָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*\rb |הִנְנִי֙\rb* \rb I will surely heal|רֹ֣פֶא\rb* \rb you.|לָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb On the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֔י\rb* \rb day from now|בַּיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb you will go up|תַּעֲלֶ֖ה\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 6 \rb I will add|וְהֹסַפְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb fifteen|חֲמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb your life.|יָמֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb And I will deliver you|אַצִּ֣ילְךָ֔\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb from the hand|וּמִכַּ֤ף\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Assyria.|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb* \rb I will defend|וְגַנּוֹתִי֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb for My sake|לְמַֽעֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb and for the sake of|וּלְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּֽי׃\rb* \rb David.’”|דָּוִ֥ד\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Then Isaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “Prepare|קְח֖וּ\rb* \rb a poultice|דְּבֶ֣לֶת\rb* \rb of figs.”|תְּאֵנִ֑ים\rb* \rb So they brought it|וַיִּקְח֛וּ\rb* \rb and applied|וַיָּשִׂ֥ימוּ\rb* \rb it to|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the boil,|הַשְּׁחִ֖ין\rb* \rb and Hezekiah recovered.|וַיֶּֽחִי׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Now Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb had asked|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb Isaiah,|יְשַׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb will be the sign|א֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will heal|יִרְפָּ֥א\rb* \rb me|לִ֑י\rb* \rb and that I will go up|וְעָלִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb on the third|הַשְּׁלִישִׁ֖י\rb* \rb day?”|בַּיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֗הוּ\rb* \rb had replied,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “This|זֶה־\rb* \rb will be a sign|הָאוֹת֙\rb* \rb to you|לְּךָ֤\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb He|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַדָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb will do|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He has promised:|דִּבֵּ֑ר\rb* \rb Would you like the shadow|הַצֵּל֙\rb* \rb to go|הָלַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb forward ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb steps,|מַֽעֲל֔וֹת\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb back|יָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb steps?”|מַעֲלֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb “It is easy|נָקֵ֣ל\rb* \rb for the shadow|לַצֵּ֔ל\rb* \rb to lengthen|לִנְט֖וֹת\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb steps,”|מַעֲל֑וֹת\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|יְחִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “but not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |כִ֔י\rb* \rb for it|הַצֵּ֛ל\rb* \rb to go|יָשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb back|אֲחֹרַנִּ֖ית\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb steps.”|מַעֲלֽוֹת׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb So Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb* \rb called out|וַיִּקְרָ֛א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and He brought|וַיָּ֣שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the shadow|הַצֵּ֗ל\rb*\rb |בַּֽ֠מַּעֲלוֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb back|אֲחֹֽרַנִּ֖ית\rb* \rb the ten|עֶ֥שֶׂר\rb* \rb steps|בְּמַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb it had descended|יָרְדָ֜ה\rb* \rb on the stairway|מַעֲלֽוֹת׃פ\rb* \rb of Ahaz.|אָחָ֛ז\rb*
\s1 Hezekiah Shows His Treasures
\r \ref Isaiah 39:1–8|ISA 39:1-8\ref*)
\p \v 12 \rb At that|הַהִ֡יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Merodach-baladan|בַּ֠לְאֲדָן\rb*\f + \fr 20:12 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Syriac (see also \ref Isaiah 39:1|ISA 39:1\ref*); MT \fqa Berodach-baladan\f* \rb son|בֶּֽן־\rb* \rb of Baladan|בַּלְאֲדָ֧ן\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֡ח\rb*\rb |בְּרֹאדַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb letters|סְפָרִ֥ים\rb* \rb and a gift|וּמִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he had heard|שָׁמַ֔ע\rb* \rb about|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb Hezekiah’s|חִזְקִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb illness.|חָלָ֖ה\rb* \v 13 \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּהוּ֒\rb* \rb received|וַיִּשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb the envoys|עֲלֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb and showed them|וַיַּרְאֵ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all that was|כָּל־\rb* \rb in his treasure|נְכֹתֹ֡ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb house—|בֵּ֣ית\rb*  \rb the silver,|הַכֶּסֶף֩\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the gold,|הַזָּהָ֨ב\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the spices,|הַבְּשָׂמִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb and the precious|הַטּ֗וֹב\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb oil,|שֶׁ֣מֶן\rb* \rb as well as his armory—|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |כֵּלָ֔יו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was found|נִמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb in his storehouses.|בְּאֽוֹצְרֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb There was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דָבָ֗ר\rb* \rb in his palace|בְּבֵית֖וֹ\rb* \rb or in all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his dominion|מֶמְשַׁלְתּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb that|אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֛הוּ\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb show them.|הֶרְאָ֧ם\rb*
\p \v 14 \rb Then the prophet|הַנָּבִ֔יא\rb* \rb Isaiah|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֣הוּ\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb and asked,|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb “Where|וּמֵאַ֙יִן֙\rb* \rb did those|הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb come from,|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and what|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb did they say|אָמְר֣וּ׀\rb* \rb to you?”|אֵלָ֜יו\rb*
\p \rb “They came|בָּ֖אוּ\rb* \rb from a distant|רְחוֹקָ֛ה\rb* \rb land,”|מֵאֶ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb replied,|וַיֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb* \rb “from Babylon.”|מִבָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb “What|מָ֥ה\rb* \rb have they seen|רָא֖וּ\rb* \rb in your palace?”|בְּבֵיתֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb Isaiah asked.|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb*
\p \rb “They have seen|רָא֔וּ\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb in my palace,”|בְּבֵיתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb answered|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb Hezekiah.|חִזְקִיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb “There is nothing|לֹא־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb among my treasures|בְּאֹצְרֹתָֽי׃\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb show them.”|הִרְאִיתִ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Then Isaiah|יְשַׁעְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb “Hear|שְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD:|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 17 \rb The time|יָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb will surely|הִנֵּה֮\rb* \rb come|בָּאִים֒\rb* \rb when everything|כָּל־\rb* \rb in your palace|בְּבֵיתֶ֗ךָ\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb and all that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֹתֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb have stored up|אָצְר֧וּ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb will be carried off|וְנִשָּׂ֣א׀\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶ֑לָה\rb* \rb Nothing|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb* \rb will be left,|יִוָּתֵ֥ר\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \v 18 \rb And some of|מִמְּךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |תּוֹלִ֖יד\rb* \rb your descendants,|וּמִבָּנֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb your own|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb flesh and blood,|יֵצְא֧וּ\rb* \rb will be taken away|יִקָּח\rb* \rb to be|וְהָיוּ֙\rb* \rb eunuchs|סָֽרִיסִ֔ים\rb* \rb in the palace|בְּהֵיכַ֖ל\rb* \rb of the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.”|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb But Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Isaiah,|יְשַֽׁעְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb “The word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have spoken|דִּבַּ֑רְתָּ\rb* \rb is good.”|ט֥וֹב\rb* \rb For he thought,|וַיֹּ֕אמֶר\rb* \rb “Will there not|הֲל֛וֹא\rb* \rb at least|אִם־\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb peace|שָׁל֥וֹם\rb* \rb and security|וֶאֱמֶ֖ת\rb* \rb in my lifetime?”|בְיָמָֽי׃\rb*
\s1 Manasseh Succeeds Hezekiah
\p \v 20 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Hezekiah,|חִזְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his might|גְּב֣וּרָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and how|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he constructed|עָשָׂ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pool|הַבְּרֵכָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the tunnel|הַתְּעָלָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 20:20 \ft Or \fqa watercourse \ft or \fqa conduit\f* \rb to bring|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb water|הַמַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb into the city,|הָעִ֑ירָה\rb*\rb |הֲלֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb are they not written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 21 \rb And Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֖הוּ\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers,|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\c 21
\s1 Manasseh Reigns in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 33:1–9|2CH 33:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb was twelve|שְׁתֵּ֨ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb fifty-five|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |חֶפְצִי־\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֥ם\rb* \rb was Hephzibah.|בָֽהּ׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb by following the abominations|כְּתֽוֹעֲבֹת֙\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had driven out|הוֹרִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 3 \rb For he rebuilt|וַיָּ֗שָׁב\rb*\rb |וַיִּ֙בֶן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the high places|הַבָּמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֑יו\rb* \rb Hezekiah|חִזְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb had destroyed,|אִבַּ֖ד\rb* \rb and he raised up|וַיָּ֨קֶם\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּחֹ֜ת\rb* \rb for Baal.|לַבַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb He made|וַיַּ֤עַשׂ\rb* \rb an Asherah pole,|אֲשֵׁרָה֙\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb King|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Ahab|אַחְאָב֙\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had done,|עָשָׂ֗ה\rb* \rb and he worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֙חוּ֙\rb* \rb and served|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֖ד\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven.|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*
\p \v 4 \rb Manasseh also built|וּבָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּחֹ֖ת\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had said,|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb “In Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb I will put|אָשִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My Name.”|שְׁמִֽי׃\rb* \v 5 \rb In both|בִּשְׁתֵּ֖י\rb* \rb courtyards|חַצְר֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb he built|וַיִּ֥בֶן\rb* \rb altars|מִזְבְּח֖וֹת\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven.|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \v 6 \rb He sacrificed|וְהֶעֱבִ֤יר\rb* \rb his own son|בְּנוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the fire,|בָּאֵ֔שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 21:6 \ft Literally \fqa made his son pass through the fire\f* \rb practiced sorcery|וְעוֹנֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and divination,|וְנִחֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb and consulted|וְעָ֥שָׂה\rb* \rb mediums|א֖וֹב\rb* \rb and spiritists.|וְיִדְּעֹנִ֑ים\rb* \rb He did|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb great|הִרְבָּ֗ה\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֛ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb provoking Him to anger.|לְהַכְעִֽיס׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Manasseh even took the carved|פֶּ֥סֶל\rb* \rb Asherah pole|הָאֲשֵׁרָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had made|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb* \rb and set it up|וַיָּ֕שֶׂם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in the temple,|בַּבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb had said|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb David|דָּוִד֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and his son|בְנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb Solomon,|שְׁלֹמֹ֣ה\rb* \rb “In this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb temple|בַּבַּ֨יִת\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem,|וּבִירוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have chosen|בָּחַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb* \rb out of all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb I will establish|אָשִׂ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb forever.|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \v 8 \rb I will never|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb again|אֹסִ֗יף\rb* \rb cause the feet|רֶ֣גֶל\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb to wander|לְהָנִיד֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָ֣אֲדָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb to their fathers,|לַֽאֲבוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb only|רַ֣ק׀\rb* \rb they are careful|יִשְׁמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb to do|לַעֲשׂ֗וֹת\rb* \rb all|כְּכֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have commanded them—|צִוִּיתִ֔ים\rb* \rb the whole|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb Law|הַ֨תּוֹרָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֥י\rb* \rb Moses|מֹשֶֽׁה׃\rb* \rb commanded|צִוָּ֥ה\rb* \rb them.”|אֹתָ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb But the people did not|וְלֹ֖א\rb* \rb listen|שָׁמֵ֑עוּ\rb* \rb and Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb led them astray,|וַיַּתְעֵ֤ם\rb* \rb so that they did|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb greater evil|הָרָ֔ע\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הַ֨גּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had destroyed|הִשְׁמִ֣יד\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the Israelites.|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*
\s1 Manasseh’s Idolatries Rebuked
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 33:10–20|2CH 33:10-20\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֧ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb His servants|עֲבָדָ֥יו\rb* \rb the prophets,|הַנְּבִיאִ֖ים\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb “Since|יַעַן֩\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֤ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb has committed|עָשָׂ֜ה\rb* \rb all|מִכֹּ֛ל\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb abominations,|הַתֹּעֵב֣וֹת\rb* \rb acting more wickedly|הֵרַ֕ע\rb* \rb than the Amorites|הָאֱמֹרִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb preceded him,|לְפָנָ֑יו\rb*\rb |עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb and|גַֽם־\rb* \rb with his idols|בְּגִלּוּלָֽיו׃פ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has caused Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb to sin,|וַיַּחֲטִ֥א\rb* \v 12 \rb |לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘Behold,|הִנְנִי֙\rb* \rb I am bringing|מֵבִ֣יא\rb* \rb such calamity|רָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb that the news|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb will reverberate|תִּצַּ֖לְנָה\rb*\rb |שְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb in the ears|אָזְנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who hear it.|שֹׁמְעָיו\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb I will stretch out|וְנָטִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the measuring line|קָ֣ו\rb* \rb used against Samaria|שֹֽׁמְר֔וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the plumb line|מִשְׁקֹ֖לֶת\rb* \rb used against the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Ahab,|אַחְאָ֑ב\rb* \rb and I will wipe out|וּמָחִ֨יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb one wipes out|יִמְחֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a bowl—|הַצַּלַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb wiping it|מָחָ֔ה\rb* \rb and turning it|וְהָפַ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb upside down.|פָּנֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 14 \rb So I will forsake|וְנָטַשְׁתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of My inheritance|נַחֲלָתִ֔י\rb* \rb and deliver them|וּנְתַתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of their enemies.|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb And they will become|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb plunder|לְבַ֛ז\rb* \rb and spoil|וְלִמְשִׁסָּ֖ה\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb their enemies,|אֹיְבֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 15 \rb because|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they have done|עָשׂ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb evil|הָרַע֙\rb* \rb in My sight|בְּעֵינַ֔י\rb*\rb |וַיִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb and have provoked Me|מַכְעִסִ֖ים\rb* \rb to anger|אֹתִ֑י\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the day|הַיּ֗וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb their fathers|אֲבוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb came|יָצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb out of Egypt|מִמִּצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb until|וְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day.’”|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb Moreover,|וְגַם֩\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb shed|שָׁפַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb so much|הַרְבֵּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb innocent|נָקִ֜י\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֨ם\rb* \rb that|עַ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he filled|מִלֵּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb from end to end,|פֶּ֣ה\rb*\rb |לָפֶ֑ה\rb* \rb in addition to|לְבַ֤ד\rb* \rb the sin|מֵֽחַטָּאתוֹ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had caused Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to commit,|הֶחֱטִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb doing|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Manasseh,|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and the sin|וְחַטָּאת֖וֹ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he committed,|חָטָ֑א\rb* \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb And Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁה֙\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֤ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָ֔יו\rb* \rb and was buried|וַיִּקָּבֵ֥ר\rb* \rb in his palace|בֵּית֖וֹ\rb* \rb garden,|בְּגַן־\rb* \rb the garden|בְּגַן־\rb* \rb of Uzza.|עֻזָּ֑א\rb* \rb And his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Amon|אָמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 Amon Reigns in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 33:21–25|2CH 33:21-25\ref*)
\p \v 19 \rb Amon|אָמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb was twenty-two|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וּשְׁתַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb two|וּשְׁתַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Meshullemeth|מְשֻׁלֶּ֥מֶת\rb* \rb daughter|בַּת־\rb* \rb of Haruz;|חָר֖וּץ\rb* \rb she was from|מִן־\rb* \rb Jotbah.|יָטְבָֽה׃\rb* \v 20 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb had done.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \v 21 \rb He walked|וַיֵּ֕לֶךְ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the ways|הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of his father,|אָבִ֑יו\rb*\rb |הָלַ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and he served|וַֽיַּעֲבֹ֗ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and worshiped|וַיִּשְׁתַּ֖חוּ\rb* \rb the idols|הַגִּלֻּלִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb had served.|עָבַ֣ד\rb* \v 22 \rb He abandoned|וַיַּעֲזֹ֕ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his fathers,|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb and did not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb walk|הָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in the way|בְּדֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb Then the servants|עַבְדֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Amon|אָמ֖וֹן\rb* \rb conspired|וַיִּקְשְׁר֥וּ\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֑יו\rb* \rb and killed|וַיָּמִ֥יתוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb in his palace.|בְּבֵיתֽוֹ׃\rb* \v 24 \rb But the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb killed|וַיַּךְ֙\rb* \rb all those|כָּל־\rb* \rb who had conspired|הַקֹּשְׁרִ֖ים\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb Amon,|אָמ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and they made his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb king|וַיַּמְלִ֧יכוּ\rb*\rb |עַם־\rb*\rb |הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Amon,|אָמ֖וֹן\rb* \rb along with his accomplishments,|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb* \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 26 \rb And he was buried|וַיִּקְבֹּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb in his tomb|בִּקְבֻרָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the garden|בְּגַן־\rb* \rb of Uzza,|עֻזָּ֑א\rb* \rb and his son|בְנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃פ\rb*
\c 22
\s1 Josiah Reigns in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 34:1–2|2CH 34:1-2\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb thirty-one|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֤ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַת֙\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Jedidah|יְדִידָ֥ה\rb* \rb daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Adaiah;|עֲדָ֖יָה\rb* \rb she was from Bozkath.|מִבָּצְקַֽת׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb what was right|הַיָּשָׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the eyes|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb and walked|וַיֵּ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb in all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the ways|דֶּ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb of his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb David;|דָּוִ֣ד\rb* \rb he did not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turn aside|סָ֖ר\rb* \rb to the right|יָמִ֥ין\rb* \rb or to the left.|וּשְׂמֹֽאול׃פ\rb*
\s1 Funding the Temple Repairs
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 34:8–13|2CH 34:8-13\ref*)
\p \v 3 \rb Now|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb in the eighteenth|בִּשְׁמֹנֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb of his reign,|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb King|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֑הוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֣ח\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb Shaphan|שָׁפָ֨ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Azaliah,|אֲצַלְיָ֤הוּ\rb* \rb the son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Meshullam,|מְשֻׁלָּם֙\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb saying,|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 4 \rb “Go up|עֲלֵ֗ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb the high|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb and have him count|וְיַתֵּ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֔סֶף\rb* \rb that has been brought|הַמּוּבָ֖א\rb* \rb into the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |שֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the doorkeepers|הַסַּ֖ף\rb*\rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb have collected|אָסְפ֛וּ\rb* \rb from the people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \v 5 \rb And let them deliver it|וְיִתְּנֹה\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|יַד֙\rb* \rb of the supervisors|הַמֻּפְקָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb of those doing|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb the work|הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb on the house|בְּבֵית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb who in turn are to give|וְיִתְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֗וֹ\rb* \rb to the workmen|לְעֹשֵׂ֤י\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb repairing|לְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb* \rb the damages|בֶּ֥דֶק\rb*\rb |הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \rb to the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD—|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*  \v 6 \rb to the carpenters,|לֶחָ֣רָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb builders,|וְלַבֹּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and masons—|וְלַגֹּֽדְרִ֑ים\rb*  \rb to buy|וְלִקְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb timber|עֵצִים֙\rb* \rb and dressed|מַחְצֵ֔ב\rb* \rb stone|וְאַבְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb to repair|לְחַזֵּ֖ק\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple.|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \v 7 \rb But|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb they need not|לֹא־\rb* \rb account|יֵחָשֵׁ֣ב\rb*\rb |אִתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb for the money|הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb put|הַנִּתָּ֣ן\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb their hands,|יָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb since|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb work|עֹשִֽׂים׃\rb* \rb with integrity.”|בֶאֱמוּנָ֖ה\rb*
\s1 Hilkiah Finds the Book of the Law
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 34:14–21|2CH 34:14-21\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb Then Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֜הוּ\rb* \rb the high|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb priest|הַכֹּהֵ֤ן\rb* \rb said to|וַ֠יֹּאמֶר\rb* \rb Shaphan|שָׁפָ֣ן\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֔ר\rb* \rb “I have found|מָצָ֖אתִי\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֧פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law|הַתּוֹרָ֛ה\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD!”|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb And he|חִלְקִיָּ֧ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|וַיִּתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb it|הַסֵּ֛פֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Shaphan,|שָׁפָ֖ן\rb* \rb who read it.|וַיִּקְרָאֵֽהוּ׃\rb*
\p \v 9 \rb And Shaphan|שָׁפָ֤ן\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵר֙\rb* \rb went|וַיָּבֹ֞א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and reported,|וַיָּ֥שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֑ר\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֗אמֶר\rb* \rb “Your servants|עֲבָדֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb have paid out|הִתִּ֤יכוּ\rb* \rb the money|הַכֶּ֙סֶף֙\rb* \rb that was found|הַנִּמְצָ֣א\rb* \rb in the temple|בַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb and have put|וַֽיִּתְּנֻ֗הוּ\rb* \rb it into|עַל־\rb* \rb the hands|יַד֙\rb* \rb of the workers|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb*\rb |הַמְּלָאכָ֔ה\rb* \rb and supervisors|הַמֻּפְקָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.”|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb Moreover , Shaphan|שָׁפָ֤ן\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵר֙\rb* \rb told|וַיַּגֵּ֞ד\rb* \rb the king,|לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb has given|נָ֣תַן\rb* \rb me|לִ֔י\rb* \rb a book.”|סֵ֚פֶר\rb* \rb And Shaphan|שָׁפָ֖ן\rb* \rb read it|וַיִּקְרָאֵ֥הוּ\rb* \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the king.|הַמֶּֽלֶךְ׃\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb When the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb heard|כִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the Book|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of the Law,|הַתּוֹרָ֑ה\rb* \rb he tore|וַיִּקְרַ֖ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his clothes|בְּגָדָֽיו׃\rb* \v 12 \rb and|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֣ה\rb* \rb the priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֡ן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Ahikam|אֲחִיקָ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁ֠פָן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Achbor|עַכְבּ֨וֹר\rb*\f + \fr 22:12 \fqa Achbor \ft is another name for \fqa Abdon\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 34:20.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Micaiah,|מִיכָיָ֜ה\rb*\f + \fr 22:12 \fqa Micaiah \ft is a variant of \fqa Micah\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 34:20.\f*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb Shaphan|שָׁפָ֣ן\rb* \rb the scribe,|הַסֹּפֵ֗ר\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and Asaiah|עֲשָׂיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the servant|עֶֽבֶד־\rb* \rb of the king:|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb* \v 13 \rb “Go|לְכוּ֩\rb* \rb and inquire|דִרְשׁ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb for me,|בַּעֲדִ֣י\rb* \rb for|וּבְעַד־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb and for|וּבְעַד֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֛י\rb* \rb in this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb book|הַסֵּ֥פֶר\rb* \rb that has been found.|הַנִּמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb great|גְדוֹלָ֞ה\rb* \rb is the wrath|חֲמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |הִיא֙\rb* \rb burns|נִצְּתָ֣ה\rb* \rb against us|בָ֔נוּ\rb* \rb because|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb our fathers|אֲבֹתֵ֗ינוּ\rb* \rb have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb obeyed|שָׁמְע֜וּ\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb book|הַסֵּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb by doing|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb all|כְּכָל־\rb* \rb that is written|הַכָּת֥וּב\rb* \rb about us.”|עָלֵֽינוּ׃\rb*
\s1 Huldah’s Prophecy
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 34:22–28|2CH 34:22-28\ref*)
\p \v 14 \rb So Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb the priest,|הַ֠כֹּהֵן\rb* \rb Ahikam,|וַאֲחִיקָ֨ם\rb* \rb Achbor,|וְעַכְבּ֜וֹר\rb* \rb Shaphan,|וְשָׁפָ֣ן\rb* \rb and Asaiah|וַעֲשָׂיָ֗ה\rb* \rb went|וַיֵּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and spoke|וַֽיְדַבְּר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Huldah|חֻלְדָּ֨ה\rb* \rb the prophetess,|הַנְּבִיאָ֜ה\rb* \rb the wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת׀\rb* \rb of Shallum|שַׁלֻּ֣ם\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Tikvah,|תִּקְוָ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 22:14 \fqa Tikvah \ft is a variant of \fqa Tokhath\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 34:22.\f* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Harhas,|חַרְחַס֙\rb*\f + \fr 22:14 \fqa Harhas \ft is a variant of \fqa Hasrah\ft ; \ref see 2|2\ref* Chronicles 34:22.\f* \rb the keeper|שֹׁמֵ֣ר\rb* \rb of the wardrobe.|הַבְּגָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb She|וְהִ֛יא\rb* \rb lived|יֹשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb* \rb in Jerusalem,|בִּירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb in the Second District.|בַּמִּשְׁנֶ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 22:14 \ft Or \fqa the Second Quarter\ft , a newer section of Jerusalem; Hebrew \fqa the Mishneh\f*
\p \v 15 \rb And Huldah said|וַתֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to them,|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֥ר\rb* \rb ‘Tell|אִמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb the man|לָאִ֔ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb sent|שָׁלַ֥ח\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֵלָֽי׃\rb* \v 16 \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb I am about to bring|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb calamity|רָעָ֛ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its people,|יֹֽשְׁבָ֑יו\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb according to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the book|הַסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb has read,|קָרָ֖א\rb* \v 17 \rb because|תַּ֣חַת׀\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have forsaken Me|עֲזָב֗וּנִי\rb* \rb and burned incense|וַֽיְקַטְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb to other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb gods,|לֵאלֹהִ֣ים\rb* \rb that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb they might provoke Me to anger|הַכְעִיסֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb with all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the works|מַעֲשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb of their hands.|יְדֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֛י\rb* \rb will be kindled|וְנִצְּתָ֧ה\rb* \rb against this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb place|בַּמָּק֥וֹם\rb* \rb and will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb be quenched.’|תִכְבֶּֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 18 \rb But as for|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb who sent|הַשֹּׁלֵ֤חַ\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְרֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb tell him|תֹאמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑יו\rb*\rb |כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the LORD,|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel,|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says:|אָמַ֤ר\rb* \rb ‘As for the words|הַדְּבָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you heard,|שָׁמָֽעְתָּ׃\rb* \v 19 \rb because|יַ֠עַן\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָ֨בְךָ֜\rb* \rb was tender|רַךְ־\rb* \rb and you humbled yourself|וַתִּכָּנַ֣ע׀\rb* \rb before|מִפְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb when you heard|בְּֽשָׁמְעֲךָ֡\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I spoke|דִּבַּרְתִּי֩\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֜ה\rb* \rb place|הַמָּק֨וֹם\rb* \rb and against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb its people,|יֹשְׁבָ֗יו\rb* \rb that they would become|לִהְי֤וֹת\rb* \rb a desolation|לְשַׁמָּה֙\rb* \rb and a curse,|וְלִקְלָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb and because you have torn|וַתִּקְרַע֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your clothes|בְּגָדֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and wept|וַתִּבְכֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb before Me,|לְפָנָ֑י\rb*\rb |וְגַ֧ם\rb* \rb I|אָנֹכִ֛י\rb* \rb have heard you,’|שָׁמַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb ‘Therefore|לָכֵן֩\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I will indeed gather|אֹֽסִפְךָ֜\rb* \rb you to|עַל־\rb* \rb your fathers,|אֲבֹתֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb and you will be gathered|וְנֶאֱסַפְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your grave|קִבְרֹתֶיךָ֮\rb* \rb in peace.|בְּשָׁלוֹם֒\rb* \rb Your eyes|עֵינֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb see|תִרְאֶ֣ינָה\rb* \rb all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the calamity|הָֽרָעָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will bring|מֵבִ֖יא\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb place.’”|הַמָּק֣וֹם\rb*
\p \rb So they brought|וַיָּשִׁ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb her|אֶת־\rb* \rb answer|דָּבָֽר׃\rb* \rb back to the king.|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*
\c 23
\s1 Josiah Renews the Covenant
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 34:29–33|2CH 34:29-33\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb summoned|וַיִּשְׁלַ֖ח\rb*\rb |וַיַּאַסְפ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֔יו\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb and Jerusalem.|וִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And he|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb went up|וַיַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb to the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֡ה\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֨י\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֩\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֜ם\rb* \rb as well as|אִתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb the priests|וְהַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb and the prophets—|וְהַנְּבִיאִ֔ים\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb small|לְמִקָּטֹ֣ן\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb great—|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb and in their hearing|בְאָזְנֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb he read|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the Book|סֵ֣פֶר\rb* \rb of the Covenant|הַבְּרִ֔ית\rb* \rb that had been found|הַנִּמְצָ֖א\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb So the king|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb* \rb stood|וַיַּעֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb by|עַֽל־\rb* \rb the pillar|הָ֨עַמּ֜וּד\rb* \rb and made|וַיִּכְרֹ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb a covenant|הַבְּרִ֣ית׀\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb to follow|לָלֶ֜כֶת\rb*\rb |אַחַ֤ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and to keep|וְלִשְׁמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb His commandments,|מִצְוֺתָ֜יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb decrees,|עֵדְוֺתָ֤יו\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and statutes|חֻקֹּתָיו֙\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his soul,|נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb* \rb and to carry out|לְהָקִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb covenant|הַבְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb that were written|הַכְּתֻבִ֖ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb book.|הַסֵּ֣פֶר\rb* \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb entered|וַיַּעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb into the covenant.|בַּבְּרִֽית׃\rb*
\s1 Josiah Destroys Idolatry
\r \ref 1 Kings 13:1–10|1KI 13:1-10\ref*; \ref 2 Chronicles 34:3–7|2CH 34:3-7\ref*)
\p \v 4 \rb Then the king|הַמֶּ֡לֶךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֣ו\rb* \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּהוּ֩\rb* \rb the high|הַגָּד֜וֹל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb priest,|הַכֹּהֵ֨ן\rb* \rb the priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֣י\rb* \rb second in rank,|הַמִּשְׁנֶה֮\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the doorkeepers|שֹׁמְרֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַסַּף֒\rb* \rb to remove|לְהוֹצִיא֙\rb* \rb from the temple|מֵהֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the articles|הַכֵּלִ֗ים\rb* \rb made|הָֽעֲשׂוּיִם֙\rb* \rb for Baal,|לַבַּ֣עַל\rb* \rb Asherah,|וְלָֽאֲשֵׁרָ֔ה\rb* \rb and all|וּלְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֣א\rb* \rb of heaven.|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb And he burned them|וַֽיִּשְׂרְפֵ֞ם\rb* \rb outside|מִח֤וּץ\rb* \rb Jerusalem|לִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb in the fields|בְּשַׁדְמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Kidron|קִדְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb and carried|וְנָשָׂ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their ashes|עֲפָרָ֖ם\rb*\rb |בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb to Bethel.|אֵֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb Josiah also did away with|וְהִשְׁבִּ֣ית\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the idolatrous priests|הַכְּמָרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb ordained|נָֽתְנוּ֙\rb* \rb by the kings|מַלְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to burn incense|וַיְקַטֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb on the high places|בַּבָּמוֹת֙\rb* \rb of the cities|בְּעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and in the places all around|וּמְסִבֵּ֖י\rb* \rb Jerusalem—|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb those who had burned incense|הַֽמְקַטְּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to Baal,|לַבַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb to the sun|לַשֶּׁ֤מֶשׁ\rb* \rb and moon,|וְלַיָּרֵ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb to the constellations,|וְלַמַּזָּל֔וֹת\rb* \rb and to all|וּלְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the host|צְבָ֥א\rb* \rb of heaven.|הַשָּׁמָֽיִם׃\rb*
\p \v 6 \rb He brought|וַיֹּצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Asherah pole|הָאֲשֵׁרָה֩\rb* \rb from the house|מִבֵּ֨ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֜ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Kidron|קִדְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb Valley|נַ֣חַל\rb* \rb outside|מִח֤וּץ\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|לִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb and there|קִדְר֖וֹן\rb*\rb |בְּנַ֥חַל\rb* \rb he burned|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb* \rb it,|אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb ground|וַיָּ֣דֶק\rb* \rb it to powder,|לְעָפָ֑ר\rb* \rb and threw|וַיַּשְׁלֵךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its dust|עֲפָרָ֔הּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the graves|קֶ֖בֶר\rb* \rb of the common|בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb people.|הָעָֽם׃\rb* \v 7 \rb He also tore down|וַיִּתֹּץ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the quarters|בָּתֵּ֣י\rb* \rb of the male shrine prostitutes|הַקְּדֵשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb that were|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the house|בְּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb had woven|אֹרְג֥וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb tapestries|בָּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for Asherah.|לָאֲשֵׁרָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Then Josiah brought|וַיָּבֵ֤א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּֽהֲנִים֙\rb* \rb from the cities|מֵעָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and desecrated|וַיְטַמֵּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the high places,|הַבָּמ֗וֹת\rb* \rb from|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb Geba|מִגֶּ֖בַע\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |בְּאֵ֣ר\rb* \rb Beersheba,|שָׁ֑בַע\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb had burned incense.|קִטְּרוּ־\rb* \rb He tore down|וְנָתַ֞ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the high places|בָּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the gates|הַשְּׁעָרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֜תַח\rb* \rb of the gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of Joshua|יְהוֹשֻׁ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb the governor|שַׂר־\rb* \rb of the city,|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb which was|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the left|שְׂמֹ֥אול\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb* \rb gate.|בְּשַׁ֥עַר\rb* \v 9 \rb Although|אַ֗ךְ\rb* \rb the priests|כֹּהֲנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the high places|הַבָּמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb come up|יַֽעֲלוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem,|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*\rb |כִּ֛י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb they ate|אָכְל֥וּ\rb* \rb unleavened bread|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb with|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb their fellow priests.|אֲחֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 10 \rb He also desecrated|וְטִמֵּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Topheth|הַתֹּ֔פֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the Valley|בְּגֵ֣י\rb*\rb |בְנֵי\rb* \rb of Ben-hinnom|הִנֹּ֑ם\rb*\f + \fr 23:10 \ft Or \fqa the Valley of the Son of Hinnom\f* \rb so that no|לְבִלְתִּ֗י\rb* \rb one|אִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb could sacrifice|לְהַעֲבִ֨יר\rb* \rb his son|בְּנ֧וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or daughter|בִּתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 23:10 \ft Literally \fqa could pass his son or daughter through the fire\f* \rb to Molech.|לַמֹּֽלֶךְ׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And he removed|וַיַּשְׁבֵּ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from the entrance|מִבֹּ֣א\rb* \rb to the house|בֵית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb the horses|הַסּוּסִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the kings|מַלְכֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֤ה\rb* \rb had dedicated|נָתְנוּ֩\rb* \rb to the sun.|לַשֶּׁ֙מֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb They were|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb in the court|בַּפַּרְוָרִ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 23:11 \ft Hebrew \fqa parbarim\f* \rb near|אֶל־\rb* \rb the chamber|לִשְׁכַּת֙\rb* \rb of an official|הַסָּרִ֔יס\rb*\rb |נְתַן־\rb* \rb named Nathan-melech.|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Josiah burned up|שָׂרַ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb the chariots|מַרְכְּב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the sun.|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶשׁ\rb*
