\s1 Josiah Restores the Passover
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 35:1–19|2CH 35:1-19\ref*)
\p \v 21 \rb The king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb commanded|וַיְצַ֤ו\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people,|הָעָ֣ם\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb “Keep|עֲשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb the Passover|פֶ֔סַח\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God,|אֱלֹֽהֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb as it is written|כַּכָּת֕וּב\rb* \rb in|עַ֛ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb Book|סֵ֥פֶר\rb* \rb of the Covenant.”|הַבְּרִ֖ית\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb No|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb such|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb Passover|כַּפֶּ֣סַח\rb* \rb had been observed|נַֽעֲשָׂה֙\rb* \rb from the days|מִימֵי֙\rb* \rb of the judges|הַשֹּׁ֣פְטִ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had governed|שָׁפְט֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb through all|וְכֹ֗ל\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the kings|מַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |וּמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb and Judah.|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \v 23 \rb But|כִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb in the eighteenth|בִּשְׁמֹנֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb of Josiah’s|יֹֽאשִׁיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb reign,|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֛ה\rb* \rb Passover|הַפֶּ֧סַח\rb* \rb was observed|נַעֲשָׂ֞ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem.|בִּירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 24 \rb Furthermore,|וְגַ֣ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹֽאשִׁיָּ֑הוּ\rb* \rb removed|בִּעֵ֖ר\rb* \rb the mediums|הָאֹב֣וֹת\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb spiritists,|הַ֠יִּדְּעֹנִים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the household gods|הַתְּרָפִ֨ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb idols,|הַגִּלֻּלִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the abominations|הַשִּׁקֻּצִ֗ים\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb were seen|נִרְאוּ֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb and in Jerusalem.|וּבִיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb He did this|לְ֠מַעַן\rb* \rb to carry out|הָקִ֞ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the words|דִּבְרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the law|הַתּוֹרָה֙\rb* \rb written|הַכְּתֻבִ֣ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the book|הַסֵּ֔פֶר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Hilkiah|חִלְקִיָּ֥הוּ\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb* \rb had found|מָצָ֛א\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb Neither|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb before|לְפָנָ֜יו\rb* \rb nor|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb after Josiah|וְאַחֲרָ֖יו\rb*\rb |כָּמֹֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb was there|הָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb any king|מֶ֗לֶךְ\rb* \rb like him,|וְכָמֹהוּ֩\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb turned|שָׁ֤ב\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb his heart|לְבָב֤וֹ\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his soul|נַפְשׁוֹ֙\rb* \rb and with all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb his strength,|מְאֹד֔וֹ\rb* \rb according to all|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the Law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Moses.|מֹשֶׁ֑ה\rb*
\p \v 26 \rb Nevertheless,|אַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb turn away|שָׁ֣ב\rb* \rb from the fury|מֵחֲר֤וֹן\rb* \rb of His burning|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb anger,|אַפּוֹ֙\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb was kindled|חָרָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אַפּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb against Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb because of|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּֽׁה׃\rb* \rb had done|הַכְּעָסִ֔ים\rb* \rb to provoke Him to anger.|הִכְעִיס֖וֹ\rb* \v 27 \rb For the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb had said,|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb “I will|גַּ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb remove|אָסִיר֙\rb* \rb Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb My sight,|פָּנַ֔י\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I removed|הֲסִרֹ֖תִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel.|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb I will reject|וּ֠מָאַסְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֤את\rb* \rb city|הָעִ֨יר\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I chose,|בָּחַ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I said,|אָמַ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb ‘My Name|שְׁמִ֖י\rb* \rb shall be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb there.’”|שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\s1 The Death of Josiah
