\p \v 29 \rb During Josiah’s reign,|בְּיָמָ֡יו\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֨ה\rb* \rb Neco|נְכֹ֧ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֛יִם\rb* \rb marched up|עָלָה֩\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb help the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Assyria|אַשּׁ֖וּר\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|פְּרָ֑ת\rb* \rb River.|נְהַר־\rb* \rb King|הַמֶּ֤לֶךְ\rb* \rb Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb went out|וַיֵּ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb to confront him,|לִקְרָאת֔וֹ\rb* \rb but Neco faced|כִּרְאֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb him|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb and killed him|וַיְמִיתֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb at Megiddo.|בִּמְגִדּ֔וֹ\rb*
\p \v 30 \rb From Megiddo|מִמְּגִדּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb his servants|עֲבָדָ֥יו\rb* \rb carried his body|מֵת֙\rb* \rb in a chariot,|וַיַּרְכִּבֻ֨הוּ\rb* \rb brought him to|וַיְבִאֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb Jerusalem,|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and buried him|וַֽיִּקְבְּרֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb in his own tomb.|בִּקְבֻֽרָת֑וֹ\rb* \rb Then the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb Jehoahaz|יְהֽוֹאָחָז֙\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah,|יֹ֣אשִׁיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb anointed him,|וַיִּמְשְׁח֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and made him king|וַיַּמְלִ֥יכוּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb his father.|אָבִֽיו׃פ\rb*
\s1 Jehoahaz Succeeds Josiah
