\p \v 31 \rb Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֣ז\rb* \rb was twenty-three|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb months.|חֳדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Hamutal|חֲמוּטַ֥ל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּֽת־\rb* \rb of Jeremiah;|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb she was from Libnah.|מִלִּבְנָֽה׃\rb* \v 32 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his fathers|אֲבֹתָֽיו׃\rb* \rb had done.|עָשׂ֖וּ\rb*
\p \v 33 \rb And Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֨ה\rb* \rb Neco|נְכֹ֤ה\rb* \rb imprisoned Jehoahaz|וַיַּאַסְרֵהוּ֩\rb* \rb at Riblah|בְרִבְלָה֙\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Hamath|חֲמָ֔ת\rb* \rb so that he could not reign|בִּמְלֹךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem,|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and he imposed|וַיִּתֶּן־\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Judah|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb a levy|עֹ֙נֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb of a hundred|מֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb talents|כִכַּר־\rb* \rb of silver|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*\f + \fr 23:33 \fqa \ref 100|0\ref* talents\ft is \ref approximately 3|3\ref*.77 tons or 3.42 metric tons of silver.\f* \rb and a talent|וְכִכַּ֥ר\rb* \rb of gold.|זָהָֽב׃\rb*\f + \fr 23:33 \fqa A talent\ft is \ref approximately 75|75\ref*.4 pounds or 34.2 kilograms of gold.\f* \v 34 \rb Then Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֨ה\rb* \rb Neco|נְכֹ֜ה\rb* \rb made Eliakim|אֶלְיָקִ֣ים\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Josiah|יֹאשִׁיָּ֗הוּ\rb* \rb king|וַיַּמְלֵךְ֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in place of|תַּ֚חַת\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֔יו\rb* \rb Josiah,|יֹאשִׁיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb and he changed|וַיַּסֵּ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Eliakim’s name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Jehoiakim.|יְהוֹיָקִ֑ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb But Neco took|לָקָ֔ח\rb* \rb Jehoahaz|יְהוֹאָחָ֣ז\rb* \rb and carried him off|וַיָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb to Egypt,|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb where he died.|וַיָּ֥מָת\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*
\p \v 35 \rb So Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִים֙\rb* \rb paid|נָתַ֤ן\rb* \rb the silver|וְהַכֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְהַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb to Pharaoh Neco,|לְפַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb but|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb to meet|עַל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh’s|פַרְעֹ֑ה\rb* \rb demand|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb he taxed|הֶעֱרִ֣יךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*\rb |לָתֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |הַכֶּ֖סֶף\rb* \rb and exacted|נָגַ֞שׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the silver|הַכֶּ֤סֶף\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from the people,|עַ֣ם\rb*\rb |הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb each|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb according to his wealth.|כְּעֶרְכּ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |לָתֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |לְפַרְעֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |נְכֹֽה׃ס\rb*
