\s1 Babylon Controls Jehoiakim
\p \v 1 \rb During Jehoiakim’s reign,|בְּיָמָ֣יו\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻכַדְנֶאצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb invaded.|עָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb So Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֥ים\rb* \rb became|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb his|ל֨וֹ\rb* \rb vassal|עֶ֙בֶד֙\rb* \rb for three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb years,|שָׁנִ֔ים\rb* \rb until he turned|וַיָּ֖שָׁב\rb* \rb and rebelled|וַיִּמְרָד־\rb* \rb against Nebuchadnezzar.|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*
\p \v 2 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb sent|וַיְשַׁלַּ֣ח\rb* \rb Chaldean,|כַשְׂדִּים֩\rb*\f + \fr 24:2 \ft Or \fqa Babylonian\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |גְּדוּדֵ֨י\rb* \rb Aramean,|אֲרָ֜ם\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb*\rb |גְּדוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb Moabite,|מוֹאָ֗ב\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |גְּדוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb and Ammonite|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb raiders|גְּדוּדֵ֣י\rb* \rb against Jehoiakim|בּ֡וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb in order|וַיְשַׁלְּחֵ֥ם\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַֽאֲבִיד֑וֹ\rb* \rb Judah,|בִּֽיהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb according to the word|כִּדְבַ֣ר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb had spoken|דִּבֶּ֔ר\rb* \rb through|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb His servants|עֲבָדָ֥יו\rb* \rb the prophets.|הַנְּבִיאִֽים׃\rb* \v 3 \rb Surely|אַ֣ךְ׀\rb* \rb this happened|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb to Judah|בִּֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb command,|פִּ֣י\rb* \rb to remove them|לְהָסִ֖יר\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb His presence|פָּנָ֑יו\rb* \rb because of the sins|בְּחַטֹּ֣את\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֔ה\rb* \rb and all|כְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he had done,|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb* \v 4 \rb and also for|וְגַ֤ם\rb* \rb the innocent|הַנָּקִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb blood|דַּֽם־\rb* \rb he had shed.|שָׁפָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb For he had filled|וַיְמַלֵּ֥א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb with innocent|נָקִ֑י\rb* \rb blood,|דָּ֣ם\rb* \rb and the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was unwilling|אָבָ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb to forgive.|לִסְלֹֽחַ׃\rb*
\p \v 5 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֛תֶר\rb* \rb of the acts|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Jehoiakim,|יְהוֹיָקִ֖ים\rb* \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his accomplishments,|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֑ה\rb* \rb are they|הֵ֣ם\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹא־\rb* \rb written|כְּתוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the Book|סֵ֛פֶר\rb* \rb of the Chronicles|דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb of the Kings|לְמַלְכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah?|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb*
\s1 Jehoiachin Reigns in Judah
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 36:9–10|2CH 36:9-10\ref*)
\p \v 6 \rb And Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִ֖ים\rb* \rb rested|וַיִּשְׁכַּ֥ב\rb* \rb with|עִם־\rb* \rb his fathers,|אֲבֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb and his son|בְּנ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֥ין\rb* \rb reigned|וַיִּמְלֹ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in his place.|תַּחְתָּֽיו׃\rb*
\p \v 7 \rb Now the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb march out|לָצֵ֖את\rb* \rb of his land|מֵֽאַרְצ֑וֹ\rb* \rb again,|הֹסִ֥יף\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֗ל\rb* \rb had taken|לָקַ֞ח\rb* \rb all|כֹּ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb his territory,|הָיְתָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לְמֶ֥לֶךְ\rb*\rb |מִצְרָֽיִם׃פ\rb* \rb from the Brook|מִנַּ֤חַל\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the Euphrates|פְּרָ֔ת\rb* \rb River.|נְהַר־\rb*
\p \v 8 \rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֣ין\rb* \rb was eighteen|שְׁמֹנֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֤ה\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְּמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb* \rb months.|חֳדָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Nehushta|נְחֻשְׁתָּ֥א\rb* \rb daughter|בַת־\rb* \rb of Elnathan;|אֶלְנָתָ֖ן\rb* \rb she was from Jerusalem.|מִירוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb And he did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb his father|אָבִֽיו׃\rb* \rb had done.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*
\s1 The Captivity of Jerusalem
\r \ref Lamentations 1:1–22|LAM 1:1-22\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb At that|הַהִ֔יא\rb* \rb time|בָּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the servants|עַבְדֵ֛י\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻכַדְנֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb marched up|עָלָה\rb* \rb to Jerusalem,|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb and the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb came|וַתָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb under siege.|בַּמָּצֽוֹר׃\rb* \v 11 \rb And Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּבֹ֛א\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb while his servants|וַעֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb were besieging it.|צָרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 12 \rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֤ין\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Judah,|יְהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb his mother,|וְאִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb his servants,|וַעֲבָדָ֖יו\rb* \rb his commanders,|וְשָׂרָ֣יו\rb* \rb and his officials|וְסָֽרִיסָ֑יו\rb* \rb all surrendered|וַיֵּצֵ֞א\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon.|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*\rb |ה֣וּא\rb*
\p \rb So in the eighth|שְׁמֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb year|בִּשְׁנַ֥ת\rb* \rb of his reign,|לְמָלְכֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb took him captive.|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \v 13 \rb As|כַּֽאֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb had declared,|דִּבֶּ֥ר\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar also carried off|וַיּוֹצֵ֣א\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the treasures|אוֹצְרוֹת֙\rb* \rb from the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֽוֹצְר֖וֹת\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb palace,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and he cut into pieces|וַיְקַצֵּ֞ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the gold|הַזָּהָ֗ב\rb* \rb articles|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֤ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֜ה\rb* \rb in the temple|בְּהֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD.|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \v 14 \rb He carried into exile|וְהִגְלָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem—|יְ֠רוּשָׁלִַם\rb* \rb |וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the commanders|הַשָּׂרִ֞ים\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֣ת׀\rb* \rb mighty men|גִּבּוֹרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of valor,|הַחַ֗יִל\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the craftsmen|הֶחָרָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb and metalsmiths—|וְהַמַּסְגֵּ֑ר\rb*  \rb ten|עֲשָׂרָה\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb captives in all.|גּוֹלֶ֔ה\rb* \rb Only|זוּלַ֖ת\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb the poorest|דַּלַּ֥ת\rb* \rb people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb remained.|נִשְׁאַ֔ר\rb*
\p \v 15 \rb Nebuchadnezzar carried away|וַיֶּ֥גֶל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֖ין\rb* \rb to Babylon,|בָּבֶ֑לָה\rb* \rb as well as|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַ֠מֶּלֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb mother,|אֵ֣ם\rb* \rb his|הַמֶּ֜לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb wives,|נְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb his officials,|סָרִיסָ֗יו\rb* \rb and the leading men|וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |אֱוִלֵי\rb* \rb of the land.|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb He took them|הוֹלִ֛יךְ\rb* \rb into exile|גּוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb |וְאֵת֩\rb* \rb The king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb* \rb also brought|וַיְבִיאֵ֧ם\rb* \rb into exile|גּוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb thousand|אֲלָפִ֗ים\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of valor|הַחַ֜יִל\rb* \rb and a thousand|אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb craftsmen|וְהֶחָרָ֤שׁ\rb* \rb and metalsmiths—|וְהַמַּסְגֵּר֙\rb* \rb all|הַכֹּ֕ל\rb* \rb strong|גִּבּוֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb and fit|עֹשֵׂ֣י\rb* \rb for battle.|מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*
\p \v 17 \rb Then the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb made Mattaniah,|מַתַּנְיָ֥ה\rb* \rb Jehoiachin’s uncle,|דֹד֖וֹ\rb* \rb king|וַיַּמְלֵ֧ךְ\rb* \rb in his place|תַּחְתָּ֑יו\rb* \rb and changed|וַיַּסֵּ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his name|שְׁמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb to Zedekiah.|צִדְקִיָּֽהוּ׃פ\rb*
\s1 Zedekiah Reigns in Judah
