\p \v 18 \rb Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֣הוּ\rb* \rb was twenty-one|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |וְאַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb years old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb when he became king,|בְמָלְכ֔וֹ\rb* \rb and he reigned|מָלַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּירוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb eleven|וְאַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb years.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb His mother’s|אִמּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb name|וְשֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb was Hamutal|חֲמִיטַל\rb* \rb daughter|בַּֽת־\rb* \rb of Jeremiah;|יִרְמְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb she was from Libnah.|מִלִּבְנָֽה׃\rb*
\p \v 19 \rb And Zedekiah did|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb evil|הָרַ֖ע\rb* \rb in the sight|בְּעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb just as|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Jehoiakim|יְהוֹיָקִֽים׃\rb* \rb had done.|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \v 20 \rb For|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb because|עַל־\rb* \rb of the anger|אַ֣ף\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb all this happened|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִירוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb and Judah,|וּבִ֣יהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb He finally banished|הִשְׁלִכ֥וֹ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb His presence.|פָּנָ֑יו\rb*
