\c 25
\s1 Nebuchadnezzar Besieges Jerusalem
\r \ref 2 Chronicles 36:15–21|2CH 36:15-21\ref*; \ref Jeremiah 39:1–10|JER 39:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb So|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb in the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִ֜ית\rb* \rb year|בִשְׁנַ֨ת\rb* \rb of Zedekiah’s reign,|לְמָלְכ֗וֹ\rb* \rb on the tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֣וֹר\rb*\rb |לַחֹדֶשׁ֒\rb* \rb day of the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִי֮\rb* \rb month,|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֻכַדְנֶאצַּ֨ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb*\rb |ה֧וּא\rb* \rb marched|בָּ֠א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb* \rb with his entire|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army.|חֵיל֛וֹ\rb* \rb They encamped|וַיִּ֣חַן\rb* \rb outside the city|עָלֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb and built|וַיִּבְנ֥וּ\rb*\f + \fr 25:1 \ft Literally \fqa He encamped outside it and they built\f* \rb a siege wall|דָּיֵ֥ק\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb all around it.|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \v 2 \rb And the city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb was kept|וַתָּבֹ֥א\rb* \rb under siege|בַּמָּצ֑וֹר\rb* \rb until|עַ֚ד\rb* \rb King|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb Zedekiah’s|צִדְקִיָּֽהוּ׃\rb* \rb eleventh|עַשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year.|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 3 \rb By the ninth day|בְּתִשְׁעָ֣ה\rb* \rb of the fourth month,|לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 25:3 \ft Probable reading (see \ref Jeremiah 52:6|JER 52:6\ref*); MT does not include \fqa fourth\ft .\f* \rb the famine|הָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֑יר\rb* \rb was so severe|וַיֶּחֱזַ֥ק\rb* \rb that the people|לְעַ֥ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb* \rb had|הָ֥יָה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb food.|לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \v 4 \rb Then the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb* \rb was breached;|וַתִּבָּקַ֣ע\rb* \rb and though the Chaldeans|וְכַשְׂדִּ֥ים\rb*\f + \fr 25:4 \ft That is, the Babylonians; also in verses 5, 6, 10, 13, 24, 25, and 26 \f*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb had surrounded|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the city,|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb of war|הַמִּלְחָמָ֤ה׀\rb* \rb fled by night|הַלַּ֙יְלָה֙\rb* \rb by way|דֶּ֜רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the gate|שַׁ֣עַר׀\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the two walls|הַחֹמֹתַ֗יִם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb near|עַל־\rb* \rb the king’s|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb garden.|גַּ֣ן\rb*
\p \rb They headed|וַיֵּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb toward|דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb the Arabah,|הָעֲרָבָֽה׃\rb*\f + \fr 25:4 \ft Or \fqa the Jordan Valley\f* \v 5 \rb but the army|חֵיל־\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּים֙\rb* \rb pursued|וַיִּרְדְּפ֤וּ\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and overtook|וַיַּשִּׂ֥גוּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in the plains|בְּעַרְב֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Jericho,|יְרֵח֑וֹ\rb* \rb and his whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb army|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb* \rb deserted|נָפֹ֖צוּ\rb* \rb him.|מֵעָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 6 \rb The Chaldeans seized|וַֽיִּתְפְּשׂוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֔לֶךְ\rb* \rb and brought him up|וַיַּעֲל֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb at Riblah,|רִבְלָ֑תָה\rb* \rb where they pronounced|וַיְדַבְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb judgment|מִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb* \rb on him.|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \v 7 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb they slaughtered|שָׁחֲט֖וּ\rb* \rb the sons|בְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb of Zedekiah|צִדְקִיָּ֔הוּ\rb* \rb before his eyes.|לְעֵינָ֑יו\rb* \rb Then|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb they put out|עִוֵּ֔ר\rb* \rb his|צִדְקִיָּ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb eyes,|עֵינֵ֤י\rb* \rb bound him|וַיַּאַסְרֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb with bronze shackles,|בַֽנְחֻשְׁתַּ֔יִם\rb* \rb and took him|וַיְבִאֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽל׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Temple Destroyed
\r \ref Jeremiah 52:12–23|JER 52:12-23\ref*)
\p \v 8 \rb On the seventh|בְּשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb day of the fifth|הַֽחֲמִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb month,|וּבַחֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הִ֗יא\rb* \rb in the nineteenth|תְּשַֽׁע־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb*\rb |שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb year|שְׁנַת֙\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar’s|נְבֻכַדְנֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb reign|לַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb* \rb over Babylon,|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֧ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard,|טַבָּחִ֛ים\rb* \rb a servant|עֶ֥בֶד\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֞א\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb* \v 9 \rb He burned down|וַיִּשְׂרֹ֥ף\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb the royal|הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb palace,|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the houses|בָּתֵּ֧י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem—|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb |וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |שָׂרַ֥ף\rb*\rb |בָּאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb significant|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb building.|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \v 10 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb And the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb army|חֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb under|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb the captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִֽים׃\rb* \rb broke down|נָֽתְצוּ֙\rb* \rb the walls|חוֹמֹ֥ת\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb Jerusalem.|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*
\p \v 11 \rb |וְאֵת֩\rb* \rb Then Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֖ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִֽים׃\rb* \rb carried into exile|הֶגְלָ֕ה\rb*\rb |יֶ֨תֶר\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb who remained|הַנִּשְׁאָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb in the city,|בָּעִ֗יר\rb* \rb along with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the deserters|הַנֹּֽפְלִים֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb had defected|נָפְלוּ֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|הַמֶּ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb and the rest|יֶ֣תֶר\rb* \rb of the population.|הֶהָמ֑וֹן\rb* \v 12 \rb But the captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֑ים\rb* \rb left behind|הִשְׁאִ֖יר\rb* \rb some of the poorest|וּמִדַּלַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb to tend the vineyards|לְכֹֽרְמִ֖ים\rb* \rb and fields.|וּלְיֹגְבִֽים׃\rb*
\p \v 13 \rb Moreover,|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the Chaldeans|כַשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb* \rb broke up|שִׁבְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֜שֶׁת\rb* \rb pillars|עַמּוּדֵ֨י\rb* \rb and|וְֽאֶת־\rb* \rb stands|הַמְּכֹנ֞וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the bronze|הַנְּחֹ֛שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Sea|יָ֧ם\rb*\rb |בְּבֵית־\rb*\rb |יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb and they carried|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bronze|נְחֻשְׁתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb to Babylon.|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb* \v 14 \rb They also|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb took away|לָקָֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb the pots,|הַסִּירֹ֨ת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb shovels,|הַיָּעִ֜ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb wick trimmers,|הַֽמְזַמְּר֣וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb dishes,|הַכַּפּ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the articles|כְּלֵ֧י\rb* \rb of bronze|הַנְּחֹ֛שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb used in the temple service.|יְשָֽׁרְתוּ־\rb* \v 15 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb The captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִֽים׃\rb* \rb also took away|לָקַ֖ח\rb* \rb the censers|הַמַּחְתּוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and sprinkling bowls—|הַמִּזְרָק֗וֹת\rb* \rb anything made of|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb pure gold|זָהָב֙\rb*\rb |זָהָ֔ב\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb or fine silver.|כֶּ֖סֶף\rb*\rb |כָּ֑סֶף\rb*
\p \v 16 \rb As for the two|שְׁנַ֗יִם\rb* \rb pillars,|הָעַמּוּדִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb the|הָֽאֶחָד֙\rb* \rb Sea,|הַיָּ֤ם\rb* \rb and the movable stands|וְהַמְּכֹנ֔וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Solomon|שְׁלֹמֹ֖ה\rb* \rb had made|עָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of the LORD,|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb*\rb |הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb the weight of the bronze|לִנְחֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb from all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb* \rb articles|הַכֵּלִ֥ים\rb* \rb was beyond measure.|מִשְׁקָ֔ל\rb* \v 17 \rb Each|הָאֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb pillar|הָעַמּ֣וּד\rb* \rb was eighteen|שְׁמֹנֶה֩\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֨ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֜ה\rb* \rb tall.|קוֹמַ֣ת׀\rb*\f + \fr 25:17 \fqa \ref 18|8\ref* cubits\ft is \ref approximately 27|27\ref* feet or 8.2 meters.\f* \rb The bronze|נְחֹשֶׁת֮\rb* \rb capital|וְכֹתֶ֨רֶת\rb* \rb atop one pillar|עָלָ֥יו׀\rb*\rb |הַכֹּתֶרֶת֮\rb* \rb was three|שָׁלֹ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה\rb* \rb high,|וְקוֹמַ֣ת\rb*\f + \fr 25:17 \fqa 3 cubits\ft is \ref approximately 4|4\ref*.5 feet or 1.4 meters.\f* \rb with a network|וּשְׂבָכָ֨ה\rb*\rb |הַכֹּתֶ֛רֶת\rb* \rb of bronze|נְחֹ֑שֶׁת\rb* \rb pomegranates|וְרִמֹּנִ֧ים\rb*\rb |עַֽל־\rb* \rb all|הַכֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb around.|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb The second|הַשֵּׁנִ֖י\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb pillar,|לַֽעַמּ֥וּד\rb* \rb with its network,|הַשְּׂבָכָֽה׃\rb* \rb was similar.|וְכָאֵ֛לֶּה\rb*
\s1 Captives Carried to Babylon
