\p \v 18 \rb The captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb also took away|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb Seraiah|שְׂרָיָה֙\rb* \rb the chief|הָרֹ֔אשׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb priest,|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb Zephaniah|צְפַנְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb the priest|כֹּהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb of second rank,|מִשְׁנֶ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the three|שְׁלֹ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb doorkeepers.|שֹׁמְרֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַסַּֽף׃\rb* \v 19 \rb Of those|וּמִן־\rb* \rb still in the city,|הָעִ֡יר\rb* \rb he took|לָקַח֩\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb court official|סָרִ֨יס\rb* \rb who|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |ה֥וּא\rb* \rb had been appointed|פָקִ֣יד׀\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the men|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb of war,|הַמִּלְחָמָ֗ה\rb* \rb as well as five|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb royal|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb advisors.|מֵרֹאֵ֤י\rb*\rb |פְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |נִמְצְא֣וּ\rb*\rb |בָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb He also took|וְאֵ֗ת\rb* \rb the scribe|הַסֹּפֵר֙\rb* \rb of the captain|שַׂ֣ר\rb* \rb of the army,|הַצָּבָ֔א\rb* \rb who had enlisted|הַמַּצְבִּ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land,|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and sixty|וְשִׁשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb men|אִישׁ֙\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ם\rb*\rb |הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb who were found|הַֽנִּמְצְאִ֖ים\rb* \rb in the city.|בָּעִֽיר׃\rb*
\p \v 20 \rb Nebuzaradan|נְבוּזַרְאֲדָ֖ן\rb* \rb captain|רַב־\rb* \rb of the guard|טַבָּחִ֑ים\rb* \rb took|וַיִּקַּ֣ח\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and brought|וַיֹּ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb at Riblah.|רִבְלָֽתָה׃\rb* \v 21 \rb There at Riblah|בְּרִבְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Hamath,|חֲמָ֑ת\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֧ל\rb* \rb struck them|וַיַּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb down|אֹתָם֩\rb* \rb and put them to death.|וַיְמִיתֵ֛ם\rb* \rb So Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb was taken into exile,|וַיִּ֥גֶל\rb* \rb away from|מֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb its own land.|אַדְמָתֽוֹ׃\rb*
\s1 Gedaliah Governs in Judah
\r \ref Jeremiah 40:1–16|JER 40:1-16\ref*)
\p \v 22 \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבֽוּכַדְנֶאצַּ֖ר\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb* \rb appointed|וַיַּפְקֵ֣ד\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Ahikam,|אֲחִיקָ֥ם\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan,|שָׁפָֽן׃פ\rb* \rb over|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|וְהָעָ֗ם\rb*\rb |הַנִּשְׁאָר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had left behind|הִשְׁאִ֔יר\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Judah.|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*
\p \v 23 \rb When all|כָל־\rb* \rb the commanders|שָׂרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the armies|הַחֲיָלִ֜ים\rb*\rb |הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb and their men|וְהָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְעוּ֩\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb had appointed|הִפְקִ֤יד\rb* \rb Gedaliah as governor,|גְּדַלְיָ֔הוּ\rb* \rb they came|וַיָּבֹ֥אוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb* \rb at Mizpah—|הַמִּצְפָּ֑ה\rb*  \rb Ishmael|וְיִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah,|נְתַנְיָ֡ה\rb* \rb Johanan|וְיוֹחָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Kareah,|קָ֠רֵחַ\rb* \rb Seraiah|וּשְׂרָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Tanhumeth|תַּנְחֻ֜מֶת\rb* \rb the Netophathite,|הַנְּטֹפָתִ֗י\rb* \rb and Jaazaniah|וְיַֽאֲזַנְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 25:23 \fqa Jaazaniah \ft is a variant of \fqa Jezaniah\ft ; see \ref Jeremiah 40:8|JER 40:8\ref*.\f* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of the Maacathite,|הַמַּ֣עֲכָתִ֔י\rb*\rb |הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb as well as their men.|וְאַנְשֵׁיהֶֽם׃\rb* \v 24 \rb And Gedaliah|גְּדַלְיָ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb took an oath|וַיִּשָּׁבַ֨ע\rb* \rb before them|לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb and their men,|וּלְאַנְשֵׁיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb assuring|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb them,|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb “Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּֽירְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of the servants|מֵעַבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans.|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֑ים\rb* \rb Live|שְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in the land|בָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb and serve|וְעִבְד֛וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb* \rb and it will be well|וְיִטַ֥ב\rb* \rb with you.”|לָכֶֽם׃ס\rb*
\s1 The Murder of Gedaliah
\r \ref Jeremiah 41:1–10|JER 41:1-10\ref*)
\p \v 25 \rb In the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗י\rb* \rb month, however,|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb Ishmael|יִשְׁמָעֵ֣אל\rb* \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Nethaniah,|נְ֠תַנְיָה\rb* \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Elishama,|אֱלִ֨ישָׁמָ֜ע\rb* \rb who was a member of the royal|הַמְּלוּכָ֗ה\rb* \rb family,|מִזֶּ֣רַע\rb* \rb came|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb with|אִתּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb ten|וַעֲשָׂרָ֤ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁים֙\rb* \rb and struck down|וַיַּכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb and killed|וַיָּמֹ֑ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Gedaliah,|גְּדַלְיָ֖הוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb along with the Judeans|הַיְּהוּדִים֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Chaldeans|הַכַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb at Mizpah.|בַּמִּצְפָּֽה׃\rb* \v 26 \rb Then all|כָל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֜ם\rb* \rb small|מִקָּטֹ֤ן\rb* \rb and|וְעַד־\rb* \rb great,|גָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb together with the commanders|וְשָׂרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the army,|הַחֲיָלִ֔ים\rb* \rb arose|וַיָּקֻ֨מוּ\rb* \rb and fled|וַיָּבֹ֖אוּ\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb fear|יָרְא֖וּ\rb* \rb of|מִפְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the Chaldeans.|כַשְׂדִּֽים׃פ\rb*
\s1 Jehoiachin Released from Prison
\r \ref Jeremiah 52:31–34|JER 52:31-34\ref*)
\p \v 27 \rb |וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb On the twenty-seventh day|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְשִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the twelfth|בִּשְׁנֵ֤ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂר֙\rb* \rb month|חֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the thirty-seventh|בִשְׁלֹשִׁ֨ים\rb*\rb |וָשֶׁ֜בַע\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb of the exile|לְגָלוּת֙\rb* \rb of Judah’s|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Jehoiachin,|יְהוֹיָכִ֣ין\rb* \rb in the year|בִּשְׁנַ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֱוִ֣יל\rb* \rb Evil-merodach|מְרֹדַךְ֩\rb* \rb became king|מֶ֨לֶךְ\rb*\rb |מָלְכ֗וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Babylon,|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb* \rb he released|נָשָׂ֡א\rb*\f + \fr 25:27 \ft Literally \fqa lifted up the head of\f* \rb |רֹ֛אשׁ\rb*\rb King|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb Jehoiachin|יְהוֹיָכִ֥ין\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb from|מִבֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb prison.|כֶּֽלֶא׃\rb* \v 28 \rb And he spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb kindly|טֹב֑וֹת\rb* \rb to Jehoiachin|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and set|וַיִּתֵּן֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his throne|כִּסְא֔וֹ\rb* \rb above|מֵעַ֗ל\rb* \rb the thrones|כִּסֵּ֧א\rb* \rb of the other kings|הַמְּלָכִ֛ים\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in Babylon.|בְּבָבֶֽל׃\rb*
\p \v 29 \rb So Jehoiachin changed|וְשִׁנָּ֕א\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb out of his prison|כִלְא֑וֹ\rb* \rb clothes,|בִּגְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb and he dined|וְאָכַ֨ל\rb*\rb |לֶ֧חֶם\rb* \rb regularly|תָּמִ֛יד\rb* \rb at the king’s table|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb* \rb for the rest|כָּל־\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his life.|חַיָּֽיו׃\rb* \v 30 \rb |מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb And the king|הַמֶּ֖לֶךְ\rb*\rb |וַאֲרֻחָת֗וֹ\rb* \rb provided Jehoiachin|נִתְּנָה־\rb* \rb a daily|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb portion|תָּמִ֧יד\rb* \rb for the rest|כֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of his life.|חַיָּֽו׃\rb*
